 the physical AI revolution.\\" It unifies images, time-series telemetry, and logs into a single searchable platform, automatically encoding and labeling robot sensor/camera data so engineering teams can find incidents, bugs, and patterns via natural-language queries (similar to software observability). The platform supports MCAP/ROS file uploads, similarity search across multi-modal data, and automatic scenario clustering across robot fleets, helping robotics companies manage the terabytes of data they generate monthly."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
org:actuals	organization	Actuals	AI "financial computer" that turns contracts into verified code to compute billing & payroll	Melbourne, Australia	https://actuals.com	{Fintech,Active,"Blackbird Portfolio","Financial software",Billing}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "Fintech", "status": "Active", "twitter": null, "website": "https://actuals.com", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/actuals-com", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/team/silk-kadala", "https://actuals.com/", "https://www.linkedin.com/company/actuals-com", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/dbicknell1", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/jimmy-mcgill", "https://rocketreach.co/david-bicknell-email_3329719", "https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio", "https://fbe.unimelb.edu.au/newsroom/david-bicknell-from-melbourne-to-silicon-valley"], "confidence": "medium", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["foundedYear", "fundingStage", "totalRaised", "totalRaisedUsd", "crunchbase", "twitter", "logoUrl", "exitDetails"]}, "hqCountry": "Australia", "crunchbase": null, "subSectors": ["Financial software", "Billing", "Payroll", "Revenue recognition", "AI / automation", "Enterprise SaaS"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": null, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": null, "fundingStage": null, "snappedSector": "Fintech", "matchedCompany": "Actuals International Pty Ltd (actuals.com) — Melbourne, Australia; AI \\"Financial Computer\\" for billing & payroll. Distinct from the unrelated Amsterdam reconciliation startup actuals.io (founded 2016, Peter Engel) and other same-named firms.", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Actuals is building \\"The Financial Computer\\" — an AI system that converts contracts of any complexity into verified code to compute financial values for billing invoices, revenue recognition/accounting, and payroll. It processes customer contracts alongside activity data to generate invoices and payroll, \\"collapsing the gap between obligation and calculation\\" to materially reduce revenue leakage and handle high-volume exceptions. It targets transaction-heavy sectors such as energy, industrials, healthcare, telecom, and technology, and integrates with ERP/CRM platforms. The Melbourne-headquartered team (with a San Francisco presence) is drawn from Meta, Google, Airwallex, Twitter, KPMG, and Intuit, and the company sits in Blackbird Ventures' portfolio of \\"software products giving functional teams superpowers.\\""}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:50:09.553	Portfolio Company
org:iv-icehouse-ventures	organization	Icehouse Ventures	NZ's most active VC, backing Kiwi founders building globally transformative companies.	Auckland, New Zealand (Parnell — Textile Centre, 125 St Georges Bay Rd)	https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/	{"venture capital",early-stage,"New Zealand",technology,"angel network","deep tech"}	\N	{"bio": "Icehouse Ventures is an Auckland-based venture capital firm and one of New Zealand's most active early-stage investors. It traces its origins to 2003, when the Ice Angels angel network was formed within The Icehouse, the entrepreneurship incubator founded in 2001 as a joint venture between the University of Auckland and private partners. The angel network raised its first fund in 2013 and was formally consolidated and rebranded as Icehouse Ventures in 2019, when external shareholders including Simplicity KiwiSaver, Jarden, and Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1 came on board. Since 2003 it has invested over NZ$800 million into 390+ Kiwi-founded companies, and operates funds and networks including Ice Angels, Arc Angels, and the student-led Firstcut Ventures.", "founded": "2003 (Ice Angels network); consolidated and rebranded as Icehouse Ventures in 2019. Parent The Icehouse founded 2001.", "sources": ["https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/", "https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/about", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icehouse_Ventures", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/robertjpaul", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/ceo-index/one-career-one-company-hundreds-of-investment-successes", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/icehouse-ventures", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/580240/phenomenal-response-70m-raised-for-icehouse-ventures-seed-fund-to-help-start-30-businesses"], "sectorFocus": "Technology and innovation; sector-agnostic across software, deep tech, agritech, climate/sustainable tech, biotech, and consumer, plus a female-founder focused fund.", "notableExits": ["PowerbyProxi (acquired by Apple)", "Aroa Biosurgery (ASX/NZX IPO, ticker ARX)", "Adherium", "Rocos"], "totalInvested": "NZ$800m+", "portfolioCount": "390+ companies", "investmentStage": "Pre-seed to pre-IPO (incubation, seed, early stage, and growth)"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:50:09.897	Investor
