cross construction and industrial workflows. Its modular platform can ingest project plans, precisely localize robots on-site, plan and execute tasks autonomously, coordinate multiple robots as a fleet, and detect and rectify errors in real time. Its first product, Lionel, is an autonomous floor-marking robot for exhibitions and large indoor spaces (300M+ sq ft marked across five continents); it has since developed autonomous concrete-drilling robots for data-center and hyperscale construction, battle-tested via a partnership with Stanley Black & Decker's DeWalt. In May 2026 it raised a US$30M Series B led by Big Pi Ventures to fund AI development, new products and global expansion."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
