/new-zealand/finalists-2023/matthew-herbert-and-connor-archbold", "https://www.ey.com/en_nz/entrepreneur-of-the-year/new-zealand/finalists-2024/connor-archbold-and-matthew-herbert", "https://www.marketing-interactive.com/tracksuit-secures-25m-series-b-to-fuel-global-brand-tracking-ambitions", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/startups/brand-researcher-tracksuit-raises-42m-for-global-expansion"], "website": "https://www.gotracksuit.com", "industry": "Market research / brand-tracking SaaS (martech)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders (Connor Archbold, Matthew Herbert), both as Co-founder & Co-CEO, are independently confirmed (RNZ, EY, Blackbird, Icehouse). Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed directly from its own portfolio page (Seed Fund III \\"one of our earliest investments\\"). 2021 founding, Auckland HQ, Series B (US$25m/NZ$42m, June 2025, led by VMG Partners), and ~150 staff / 1,000+ customers / ~10,000 brands all confirmed. Changes: removed the unsourced claim that Herbert is based in London (Tracksuit has a UK office and Archbold is confirmed NZ-based, but I could not source Herbert's specific location, so set to null); softened the Series A funding line because sources report it as both NZ$22m and US$13.5m and some name Altos/Footwork (not VMG) as the Series A lead; trimmed the description's \\"Disney/Bondi Sands/Sharesies\\" and overly precise staff/geography claims to the parts I could verify. Confidence remains high.", "statusDetail": "Active and scaling internationally; raised a US$25m (NZ$42m) Series B in June 2025 led by VMG Partners, bringing total raised to over US$70m / NZ$70m+ across three rounds.", "verifyVerdict": "partly-confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised NZ$70m+ across three rounds. Seed (2023): NZ$7.5m. Series A (Feb 2024): NZ$22m (reported as US$13.5m) at ~NZ$150m valuation, with Altos Ventures and Footwork joining alongside existing backers Blackbird and Icehouse Ventures. Series B (June 2025): US$25m / NZ$42m led by VMG Partners, with Blackbird, Icehouse Ventures, Altos Ventures and Footwork. Notable angels include Mark Ritson and Emily Kramer.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
