ngDescription": "Ravio is a real-time compensation platform that helps companies benchmark and manage pay, equity, and benefits using live, anonymized market data contributed by participating employers. The platform consolidates total-reward benchmarking, pay-gap/equity analysis, salary banding, and compensation review cycles, syncing directly with customers' HR systems for continuously updated benchmarks across 50+ geographies and 300+ roles. It is trusted by 1,400+ global companies including Wise, Adyen, Pipedrive, Octopus Energy, and Skyscanner. Ravio was co-founded in 2022 by former Deliveroo operators and positions itself as Europe's leading compensation management platform."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
org:iv-wayve	organization	Wayve (Wayve Technologies Ltd)	Embodied-AI self-driving company co-founded by NZ's Alex Kendall; Icehouse Ventures-backed	London, United Kingdom	https://wayve.ai	{self-driving,"autonomous vehicles","embodied AI","deep learning",robotaxi,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Wayve is a London-headquartered autonomous-driving company that uses end-to-end deep learning (\\"embodied AI\\") to build a general-purpose self-driving intelligence from cameras rather than HD maps. It was founded in Cambridge, England in 2017 by Amar Shah and New Zealander Alex Kendall, who has been sole CEO since Shah's 2020 departure. In February 2026 it raised a US$1.2b Series D (US$1.5b total capital including Uber milestone funding) at an US$8.6b valuation, with Uber naming Wayve to power its first robotaxi fleet. New Zealand's Icehouse Ventures was a named investor in that round (NZ$12.5m, per NZ Herald), backing Kiwi founder Kendall.", "notes": "The task premise that there is a separate \\"New Zealand company Wayve\\" is a misconception: there is only one self-driving Wayve (Wayve Technologies Ltd), HQ'd in London and founded in Cambridge, England in 2017. The NZ/Icehouse angle is that co-founder & CEO Alex Kendall is a Christchurch-raised New Zealander (University of Auckland grad), and Auckland-based Icehouse Ventures invested in Wayve's Feb 2026 round (NZ$12.5m per NZ Herald). So icehouseBacked is confirmed, but the company is UK-domiciled, not NZ-domiciled. Funding figures vary by source/currency: the US$1.5b total is reported in NZD as ~$2.5b (NZ Herald) and the Series D component as US$1.2b at US$8.6b valuation (Wayve press release, CNBC); one EU source framed it as ~EUR1b / EUR7.2b. Amar Shah's LinkedIn and current location were not confirmed, so left null.", "stage": "Series D", "status": "active", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://wayve.ai/press/series-d/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/wayve-founded-by-kiwi-alex-kendall-raises-25b-reveals-uber-will-use-its-tech-for-its-first-robotaxis/premium/HJHKW5N4DZFOBA4IPMSPB7XFCE/", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayve", "https://wayve.ai/company/leadership-team/alex-kendall/", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/news/2024/11/07/alex-kendall-wayve-ceo.html", "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/02/24/wayve-fundraise-nvidia-microsoft.html", "https://wayve.ai/press/series-c/", "https://mlg.eng.cam.ac.uk/people/amar-shah/", "https://uk.linkedin.com/in/alexgkendall"], "website": "https://wayve.ai", "industry": "Autonomous vehicles / Embodied AI", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders, NZ origin, Icehouse backing and overall narrative all independently confirmed (Wayve's own Series D press release explicitly lists Icehouse Ventures as a new institutional investor; NZ Herald cites NZ$12.5m). Main correction: the draft called it a \\"US$1.5b Series D.\\" Per Wayve's press release and CNBC, the Series D was US$1.2b at an US$8.6b valuation, with ~US$1.5b total capital secured including Uber's milestone-based commitment; reworded statusDetail, description and fundingNotable accordingly, and corrected the lead investors (Eclipse, Balderton, SoftBank Vision Fund 2 led; the automakers/tech firms were strategic investors). Added Kendall's Christchurch upbringing. Could not confirm Amar Shah's LinkedIn/location (left null).", "statusDetail": "Active private company; raised a US$1.2b Series D (Feb 2026) at an US$8.6b valuation; ~US$1.5b total capital secured including Uber milestone-based commitment", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "US$1.2b Series D (Feb 2026), with ~US$1.5b total capital secured; led by Eclipse, Balderton and SoftBank Vision Fund 2, with strategic investors Mercedes-Benz, Nissan, Stellantis, Microsoft, Nvidia and Uber, and new institutional investors including Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan, Baillie Gifford, British Business Bank, Schroders Capital and NZ's Icehouse Ventures (NZ$12.5m, per NZ Herald). Prior US$1.05b Series C (May 2024) led by SoftBank.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
