any that makes a wireless load-controlling device which sits between the crane hook and the load, using gyroscopic and inertial (flywheel) forces plus accelerometers to accurately rotate, orient and stabilise crane loads. It removes the need for taglines and for \\"dogmen\\"/riggers to stand near suspended loads, improving safety and efficiency on construction, ports, mining and offshore worksites. Originally developed within engineering firm TENSA Equipment (commercial use since 2018) and spun out as Roborigger in 2019, the company has deployed units globally across the EU, Asia, North America and Africa for clients including Multiplex, Lendlease, Acciona and Qube Ports. It raised a $5M Series A from Blackbird Ventures in 2020."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
