line workers and leaders to drive daily improvements across safety, quality and operational efficiency. Its flagship products include the iAuditor inspection/checklist app and the EdApp (Training) microlearning platform, supporting issue reporting, data capture, analytics, IoT sensors, asset management and business insurance. The platform is used by more than 65,000 organizations including Shell, the United Nations, Virgin Active and Mars, powering hundreds of millions of inspections per year. Founded in 2004 in a Townsville garage by Luke Anear, it became one of Australia's most prominent tech unicorns."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
