 a New Zealand marine technology company building electric hydrofoiling vessels that \\"fly\\" above the water using America's Cup-inspired foiling tech, cutting energy consumption by up to ~90% versus conventional boats. Its VS-9 — the world's first certified commercial electric hydrofoiling vessel — entered passenger service with Fullers360 in Auckland in 2024-25 (10 passengers, 25 knots, ~50 nautical mile range), and the company is developing the larger 100-passenger VS-18 commuter ferry and a VS-Drive modular electric propulsion pod. Vessev has begun expanding internationally, with customers in Europe (Finn Lough, Northern Ireland) and plans for Australia and the USA."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
