org:xy-sense	organization	XY Sense	AI-powered occupancy sensors and analytics that optimize how offices use physical space.	Melbourne, Australia	https://xysense.com/	{"Deep Tech & Hardware",Active,"Blackbird Portfolio","Workplace Analytics","Occupancy Sensors"}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "PropTech", "status": "Active", "twitter": "https://x.com/xysense_io", "website": "https://xysense.com/", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/xysense", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio/xy-sense", "https://xysense.com/about-us/", "https://xysense.com/", "https://xysense.com/the-xy-sense-founding-story-why-we-set-out-to-end-the-workplace-data-vacuum/", "https://xysense.com/press-release-xy-sense-raises-aud5m-in-seed-funding-to-transform-workplaces-with-data/", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20220725005617/en/XY-Sense-Secures-a-Total-of-US$10M-to-Deliver-on-Rapidly-Increasing-Global-Demand-for-Leading-Occupancy-Sensor-Analytics-Platform", "https://www.thesaasnews.com/news/xy-sense-raises-10-million-in-funding", "https://www.smartcompany.com.au/startupsmart/xy-sense-smart-sensors-workplace/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/xy-sense", "https://www.linkedin.com/company/xysense", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/birchalex", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/lukedmurray/", "https://x.com/xysense_io", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/xy-sense/__FyMyiv_kfRqPOLKmmv8h5MFrXDCGedPiFLje9zAKPl0"], "confidence": "high", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["totalRaisedUsd", "logoUrl", "founders.twitterUrl", "founders.website"]}, "hqCountry": "Australia", "crunchbase": "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/xy-sense", "subSectors": ["Workplace Analytics", "Occupancy Sensors", "IoT Hardware", "Computer Vision / AI", "Real Estate Technology", "SaaS"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": 2016, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": "~US$10M (incl. AUD$5M seed in 2020 and a US$10M raise in 2022; aggregators report up to ~US$24.5M)", "fundingStage": "Series A", "snappedSector": "Deep Tech & Hardware", "matchedCompany": "XY Sense Pty Ltd (xysense.com) — Melbourne-based workplace occupancy sensor & analytics startup", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "XY Sense is a Melbourne-headquartered workplace intelligence company that builds AI-driven, computer-vision occupancy sensors paired with a cloud analytics platform to help corporate real estate teams measure and optimize how office space is used in real time. Its privacy-first sensors process data on-device, capturing only anonymous X/Y coordinates (no images), with one Area Pro sensor covering up to ~3,000 sq ft. The platform integrates with building systems (HVAC, lighting, booking, cleaning) and is deployed across 30+ countries. Founded in 2016 by Alex Birch and Luke Murray, who previously co-founded workplace SaaS company Serraview."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
org:iv-mint-innovation	organization	Mint Innovation	NZ cleantech using microbes and green chemistry to recover gold and metals from e-waste	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.mint.bio	{cleantech,"e-waste recycling",biotechnology,"circular economy","critical metals","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Mint Innovation is a New Zealand cleantech company founded in 2016 in Auckland that uses proprietary microbes and low-carbon chemistry to recover precious and critical metals (such as gold and copper) from electronic waste, as an alternative to high-temperature smelting. It opened its first commercial-scale e-waste biorefinery in Sydney, Australia in 2022 and is expanding internationally, including a first US facility in Longview, Texas (announced December 2024) and EV-battery (black mass) recycling work in the UK. The company has raised multiple venture rounds, including a NZ$60M Series C closed in February 2023.", "notes": "Distinct from same-named foreign firms; this is the Auckland-founded cleantech, website mint.bio. Founders Will Barker (CEO) and Ollie Crush (CSO) are confirmed on the company's About page and multiple sources. A third early co-founder, Mat Rowe, appears in some secondary sources but is not on Mint's current leadership/About page, so he is omitted. Matt Bedingfield (Global President) and other named executives are leadership, not founders. Sydney biorefinery opened 2022 and began processing in 2023; first US facility is in Longview, Texas (announced Dec 2024). Icehouse backing is confirmed (early investor and one of the two largest shareholders alongside Movac).", "stage": "Series C", "status": "active", "founded": "2016", "sources": ["https://www.mint.bio/about", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/e-waste-recycler-mint-raises-60m-series-c-why-its-still-favouring-offshore-plants-over-nz/JIWIH5JHHVDCPJBKBYLNK5SH3E/", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/mint-innovation", "https://www.mint.bio/news-and-press/mint-innovation-closes-60m-in-series-c-capital-raise", "https://www.mint.bio/news-and-press/mint-innovation-secures-site-for-first-us-e-waste-biotechnology-facility", "https://www.cie.auckland.ac.nz/newsroom/the-venture-using-microbes-to-turn-e-waste-into-precious-metals/", "https://www.blackbird.vc/blog/investment-notes-mint-innovation", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/aucklands-mint-innovation-secures-18m-to-recycle-ev-batteries-for-jaguar-land-rover-in-the-uk/HUUBJZSZ6NDWJLLLFMJMT5P5FU/"], "website": "https://www.mint.bio", "industry": "Cleantech / E-waste recycling biotechnology", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders, Icehouse backing, 2016 Auckland founding, status, and NZ$60M Series C (Feb 2023) all confirmed. Corrected the Series C lead: it was led by Inspire Impact (Liverpool Partners), NOT Movac as drafted; Movac and Icehouse were supporting investors and are the two largest shareholders. Removed the unverified \\"Icehouse ~28% largest single shareholder\\" claim and the unsourced Blackbird/Sam Morgan Series B detail (no source confirmed Blackbird or Sam Morgan in Series B). Made the US facility specific (Longview, Texas, announced Dec 2024). The Sydney plant opened 2022 (commercial processing from 2023), correcting the draft's \\"2024\\" implication. Mat Rowe (possible third co-founder) remains unconfirmed by primary sources and is omitted.", "statusDetail": "Active; opened commercial-scale e-waste biorefinery in Sydney (2022, began processing 2023) and announced a first US facility in Longview, Texas (Dec 2024); also pursuing UK EV-battery recycling.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Closed NZ$60M Series C in Feb 2023, led by Inspire Impact (impact arm of Australia's Liverpool Partners), with Movac, Icehouse Ventures and Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1. Followed a ~NZ$20M Series B (2020) and an earlier Series A. Icehouse Ventures and Movac are reported as the company's two largest shareholders.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026