org:iv-tradify	organization	Tradify	Job management app for tradespeople — quoting, scheduling, invoicing and timesheets	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.tradifyhq.com	{SaaS,"job management","trades / construction tech","field service","small business software","Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "Tradify is a New Zealand-founded job management software platform for tradespeople (electricians, plumbers, HVAC and similar trades), offering quoting, estimating, scheduling, invoicing, timesheets and online payments. Founded by former West Auckland electrician Curtis Bailey, it grew from a single desk at Icehouse Ventures to a team of around 107 serving roughly 20,000 customers across New Zealand, Australia and the UK. It was acquired by UK software company The Access Group in 2024 in a deal reported to exceed NZ$100 million.", "notes": "Icehouse backing is confirmed by Icehouse Ventures' own blog, which states Tradify grew \\"from a single desk at Icehouse Ventures,\\" that Icehouse supported the 2016 and 2017 seed rounds plus the 2021 Series A and 2022 Series B, held ~10% at exit, and that 500+ Icehouse investors benefited. Founding year: Tradify's own pages and Icehouse cite 2013; RNZ/NZ Herald say Bailey began building it in 2010 — 2010 likely reflects initial development, 2013 the company launch. The aggregator-only \\"co-founder Sebastián Šooš\\" claim (Tracxn and downstream listings) could NOT be independently confirmed by any authoritative source and is therefore excluded from the founders list. Michael Steckler became CEO in mid-2020 (a hired executive, not a founder). This is the Auckland, NZ tradie job-management app (tradifyhq.com), not a same-named foreign company.", "stage": "Series B", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2013", "sources": ["https://www.tradifyhq.com/nz/about-us", "https://www.tradifyhq.com/nz/our-story", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/reflections-on-tradify-and-the-venture-ecosystem", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/529663/former-sparkie-in-for-9m-payday-as-his-tradify-app-sells-to-uk-firm-for-100m", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/529637/british-software-giant-set-to-acquire-nz-tech-company-tradify", "https://www.movac.co.nz/portfolio/tradify/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/deals/tradify-seals-100m-plus-sale-to-uk-software-powerhouse/", "https://www.tradifyhq.com/blog/tradify-joins-access-group"], "website": "https://www.tradifyhq.com", "industry": "SaaS / Field Service & Job Management Software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All major draft claims independently confirmed: Curtis Bailey as sole sourced founder, 2013 founding, acquired by The Access Group ~Oct 2024 for NZ$100m+, and Icehouse Ventures backing (their own blog: ~10% stake, single-desk origin, seed 2016/2017 + Series A/B, 500+ investors at exit). Corrected/tightened details: acquisition date stated as announced 2 Oct 2024 (the draft's \\"completion ~31 Oct 2024\\" could not be sourced); added exit cap-table shares (Movac ~36%, Icehouse ~10%, Bailey ~9%, K1W1 ~6%) and Series A ~NZ$55m valuation per RNZ. The speculative second co-founder \\"Sebastián Šooš\\" remains unverified beyond Tracxn-style aggregators and was correctly kept out of the founders list.", "statusDetail": "Acquired by The Access Group (UK) in 2024; deal reported to exceed NZ$100m, announced 2 Oct 2024", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Seed rounds in 2016 and 2017 led by Adam Clark with Icehouse Ventures support; Series A (2021, ~NZ$10m at ~NZ$55m valuation) and Series B (2022) led/joined by Movac. Investors included Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1. At exit Movac held ~36%, Icehouse Ventures ~10%, founder Curtis Bailey ~9%, K1W1 ~6%; over 500 Icehouse investors benefited from the sale.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
