org:iv-adherium	organization	Adherium Limited	NZ-founded respiratory eHealth firm behind the Hailie/Smartinhaler connected inhaler platform	Melbourne, Australia (registered); Auckland, New Zealand (NZ entity)	https://www.adherium.com	{"digital health","respiratory medtech","connected devices","medication adherence","asthma & COPD","Icehouse Portfolio",IPO}	\N	{"bio": "Adherium is a respiratory digital-health company, founded in New Zealand in 2001 as Nexus6 by Garth Sutherland, that makes the Hailie (formerly Smartinhaler) connected inhaler sensor and cloud platform for monitoring medication adherence in asthma and COPD. The Smartinhaler was used widely in clinical trials and gained US FDA 510(k) clearance, and Adherium listed on the ASX in August 2015 (ASX: ADR), raising about A$35m. The company has shifted from a clinical-trials focus to commercialising its devices, with a major investment push into US operations. It remains loss-making, with auditors flagging material uncertainty over going concern.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the NZ-founded, ASX-listed respiratory eHealth firm Adherium Limited (formerly Nexus6) — not the US Nasdaq SPAC \\"Aetherium Acquisition Corp\\" or other same/similar-named entities. Icehouse caveat: sources confirm Ice Angels (the Auckland angel network founded by The Icehouse in 2003, the lineage from which Icehouse Ventures was later formed) was an early backer of Nexus6/Adherium, described as one of its first investments (founding Ice Angel Scott Gilmour cites it directly); I did not find Adherium on the modern \\"Icehouse Ventures\\" fund portfolio page, so the connection is at the Ice Angels/Icehouse level rather than a confirmed Icehouse Ventures fund deal — hence \\"likely.\\" Founder context: Garth Sutherland left as Group CEO in June 2017 (succeeded by Arik Anderson); current CEO is Dawn Bitz (appointed 22 July 2025) — not a founder, listed here only for status context. HQ nuance: registered office is Melbourne, Australia (Collins Square, 727 Collins St), with an Auckland NZ office (16 Kingston St) and US/UK presence; founded and originally based in New Zealand. Status \\"ipo\\" (publicly listed) despite recurring going-concern uncertainty.", "stage": "Public (ASX: ADR)", "status": "ipo", "founded": "2001", "sources": ["https://www.adherium.com/about", "https://www.adherium.com/contact-us/", "https://stockhead.com.au/health/dr-borehams-crucible-sizing-up-the-opportunity-for-asx-biotech-adherium/", "https://www.theicehouse.co.nz/blog/the-icehouse-20-year-publication-part-seven", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icehouse_Ventures", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/garthsutherland", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/garth-sutherland", "https://biosciencemanagers.com/adherium-appoints-dawn-bitz-as-chief-executive-officer/", "https://announcements.asx.com.au/asxpdf/20250829/pdf/06nlf3p3nhp4xn.pdf", "https://www.ausbiotech.org/about-us/30-success-stories/27-adherium"], "website": "https://www.adherium.com", "industry": "Digital health / respiratory medtech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed all major draft claims via fresh searches: Garth Sutherland founded Nexus6 in NZ in 2001 (developed Smartinhaler in his garage), led to ASX IPO and until June 2017, MSc Physics Univ. of Waikato, ex-Microsoft/Gallagher, now CEO of The Insides Company. ASX:ADR listed Aug 2015 (~A$35m, 50c/share, AstraZeneca A$3m foundation investor); loss-making with going-concern flags (net loss ~A$12.7m FY2025, cash A$43,255 at 30 Jun 2025); ~A$4.49m ANREO completed July 2025; Dawn Bitz appointed CEO 22 Jul 2025. Registered office Melbourne, NZ office Auckland — confirmed. Ice Angels/Icehouse backing well-sourced (Nexus6 cited as one of Ice Angels' first investments); kept \\"likely\\" because it is Ice Angels-era rather than the modern Icehouse Ventures fund. Minor edits: tightened oneLiner under 110 chars, added AstraZeneca/IPO-amount detail, added FY2025 financial figures, no factual claims altered or invented.", "statusDetail": "Active and ASX-listed (ASX: ADR) since August 2015; loss-making with recurring auditor going-concern material-uncertainty flags (net loss ~A$12.7m FY2025; cash A$43,255 at 30 June 2025). Founded in NZ as Nexus6; renamed Adherium; registered office in Melbourne with NZ operations retained in Auckland and a US commercial push.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~A$35m in its August 2015 ASX IPO (50c/share), with AstraZeneca a A$3m foundation investor. Earlier backed by NZ's Ice Angels (the angel network founded by The Icehouse) in its Nexus6 days (~2003), where it was one of the network's first investments. Completed an ~A$4.49m accelerated non-renounceable entitlement offer in July 2025.", "icehouseBacked": "likely"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
