org:iv-fileinvite	organization	FileInvite	Secure document-collection automation for banks, credit unions and complex lenders.	Auckland, New Zealand (US office in Broomfield/Denver, Colorado)	https://www.fileinvite.com	{fintech,lending,"document automation",SaaS,"client portals","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "FileInvite is a New Zealand-founded SaaS company that automates secure document and data collection, offering client portals, requests/reminders, e-signatures and CRM integrations. It is focused on banks, credit unions and commercial/complex lenders, generating the large majority of its revenue outside New Zealand (notably Australia and the US). Founded in 2015 by James Sampson, who developed it to solve the document-collection problem at his Auckland web agency, Zyber. The company remains active, launching CRM \\"Connected Workflows\\" in April 2025 and reporting roughly NZ$22.8M ARR for 2024.", "notes": "Not to be confused with same-named generic \\"file invite\\" software products; this is the NZ-origin SaaS associated with Auckland agency Zyber. Icehouse backing is firmly confirmed: Icehouse Ventures (CEO Robbie Paul) led the NZ$10M Series A in July 2022. HQ is functionally split: NZ roots and an Auckland (Penrose) office, but the About page now lists a Broomfield/Denver, Colorado US address as the primary HQ. James Monk (a genuine Zyber co-founder) is listed as a FileInvite co-founder only by aggregators (Tracxn, RocketReach) and could not be confirmed via the company's own materials or press, so he was dropped from the founders list. Cumulative funding (~US$8.17M) and ~$22.8M 2024 ARR come from third-party aggregators (Tracxn/Crunchbase/GetLatka) and may be approximate.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2015", "sources": ["https://www.fileinvite.com/about", "https://www.fileinvite.com/blog/fileinvite-raises-10-million-series-a-to-change-how-information-is-requested", "https://www.fileinvite.com/blog/news-connected-workflows-for-lenders", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/a-kiwi-filesharing-startup-thats-cut-the-time-taken-to-collate-mortgage-documents-by-65-just-raised-nz10-million/", "https://itbrief.co.nz/story/nz-s-fileinvite-raises-10m-in-latest-investment-round", "https://matchstiq.io/stories/james-sampson-founder-of-fileinvite", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/jamessampson-nz", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/fileinvite/__ZaLCstKY5tJTx3Gf_T-WNbrmKtXW9Yp4ApsXAX7UUjg", "https://getlatka.com/companies/fileinvite"], "website": "https://www.fileinvite.com", "industry": "SaaS / Document Workflow Automation", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Dropped co-founder James Monk: although he is a genuine Zyber co-founder, his FileInvite founder status appears only on aggregators (Tracxn/RocketReach), not on the company's About page, the Matchstiq founder profile, or press, so it could not be independently confirmed. Corrected James Sampson's prior background: the draft's \\"Victoria University of Wellington\\" is unsupported — the Matchstiq founder profile says he studied architecture; removed the unverifiable university claim. Confirmed: 2015 founding, James Sampson as Founder & CEO, Icehouse Ventures-led NZ$10M Series A (July 2022), active status with an April 2025 CRM \\"Connected Workflows\\" launch and a reported ~$2M bridge round ahead of Series B. Tightened the oneLiner and updated the description/status with current details.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating; offices in Auckland (Penrose), Broomfield/Denver (Colorado), Manila and San Salvador. Raised NZ$10M Series A in July 2022; launched CRM \\"Connected Workflows\\" in April 2025 and reported a ~$2M bridge round ahead of a planned Series B around late 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "NZ$10M Series A (July 2022) led by Icehouse Ventures, with Forefront Venture Partners (US), Vulpes Ventures (Singapore) and existing shareholder Flying Kiwi Angels. Cumulative funding reported around US$8.17M across rounds (aggregator figure).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
