org:iv-learncoach	organization	LearnCoach	NZ's most-used online tutorial platform helping secondary students prepare for NCEA exams.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://learncoach.com	{EdTech,"Online learning",NCEA,"Secondary education","Video tutorials","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "LearnCoach is a New Zealand EdTech company providing online video tutorials, lessons, activities and government-approved exams to help secondary-school students prepare for NCEA. It was founded in 2012 by former Otago Boys' High School maths teacher David Cameron (after a maths-explainer video he made went viral), alongside his brother Mark Cameron and his then-fiancee Deborah Lambie, and supports roughly 100,000+ students per year. It is described as New Zealand's first online provider government-approved to deliver the New Zealand Curriculum and offers a teacher management platform for monitoring student progress and administering online assessments.", "notes": "Founding year is 2012 per LearnCoach's own About page and award sources; the Icehouse Ventures job board lists 2016 (likely an incorporation/profile artifact) and an RNZ piece loosely said 2013 — 2012 is treated as authoritative. Three co-founders are now independently confirmed: David Cameron (CEO), Mark Cameron (CTO, David's brother), and Deborah Lambie. This is the New Zealand LearnCoach (learncoach.com); not the same-named foreign coaching/education products. Funding figures are in NZ dollars.", "stage": "Pre-Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2012", "sources": ["https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/virtual-classroom-startup-learncoach-raises-45m/OZNT6BZEYXWGWFTQCN4PFDVZBA/", "https://learncoach.com/about-us", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/learncoach", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/national/programmes/ninetonoon/audio/201824074/learncoach-founders-dave-cameron-and-deborah-lambie", "https://nzawards.org.nz/winners/david-cameron/", "https://www.otago.ac.nz/otagomagazine/issue42/profiles/beautiful-ambitions", "https://ecommercenews.co.nz/story/learncoach-closes-1-5m-seed-round", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/deborah-lambie-dreams-come-true-for-former-miss-world-nz-doctor-and-entrepreneur/CTTBCOLXWSXPMWI7IK6PAP5U2U/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/learncoach"], "website": "https://learncoach.com", "industry": "EdTech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Corrected the founders: Deborah Lambie is independently confirmed as a co-founder (RNZ titled the founders 'Dave Cameron & Deborah Lambie'; multiple sources), so her null/uncertain fields were filled — she is a medical doctor, BMedSc Hons (bioethics), Master of Entrepreneurship, CFA charterholder, Miss World NZ 2015 and later investment banker, and David Cameron's then-fiancee/wife (not his wife from the outset). Mark Cameron confirmed as David's older brother with Publons (Clarivate-acquired) background. David Cameron's role normalised to 'Co-founder & CEO'. Funding (NZ$4.5m pre-Series A Sept 2020 at ~NZ$13.5m led by Icehouse Ventures + Impact Enterprise Fund, atop NZ$1.5m 2019 seed, ~25% Icehouse stake), Icehouse backing, active status, 2012 founding, and the description/oneLiner all confirmed accurate. Could not load the LinkedIn profiles or Crunchbase directly to verify those URLs; Deborah Lambie's LinkedIn left null.", "statusDetail": "Active, privately held. Listed in Icehouse Ventures' portfolio; no evidence of acquisition or closure as of 2026.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised a NZ$4.5m pre-Series A in Sept 2020 (valuing the company at ~NZ$13.5m), led by Icehouse Ventures and the Impact Enterprise Fund, on top of a NZ$1.5m seed round in 2019 also led by Icehouse. Icehouse held an approximately 25% stake. Crunchbase lists total funding as roughly US$4.36m.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
