org:iv-nectar	organization	Nectar (Nectar Money / Nectar NZ Limited)	NZ digital lender: 100% online personal loans with 7-minute decisions and same-day funding.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://nectar.co.nz/	{fintech,"digital lending","personal loans","consumer finance",neo-lender,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Nectar (Nectar Money / Nectar NZ Limited) is an Auckland-based fintech operating a fully digital, 100%-online personal-loan platform for New Zealand consumers, with loan decisions in as little as 7 minutes and same-day funding. It offers personal, car, debt-consolidation and emergency loans (up to about NZ$37,500, average around NZ$11,500) and was the first NZ digital lender to release an API for broker applications. The company reports having originated more than NZ$100 million in loans since launch and is funded by both equity and debt investors. It remains active and registered as of 2026.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the New Zealand fintech Nectar / Nectar Money (Nectar NZ Limited, nectar.co.nz), an online personal-loan lender — NOT the US/UK loyalty, HR or insurtech companies of the same name, nor the NZ IT-services firm \\"Nectar Group\\" (nectargroup.co.nz). Single founder (Symon Nausbaum) confirmed across Crunchbase, Scoop, NZ Adviser, the company information memorandum, and the NZ Companies register; no co-founder found. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed both by NZ media (led the Series A; \\"one of Nectar's original equity investors\\") and by the company register, which lists Icehouse Ventures Nominees Limited as a shareholder.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2015", "sources": ["https://nectar.co.nz/", "https://nectar.co.nz/about/", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/BU2303/S00341/nectar-secures-expansion-capital-to-grow-digital-lending-marketshare.htm", "https://www.mpamag.com/nz/news/general/nectar-secures-expansion-capital-to-accelerate-its-growth/440371", "https://nzentrepreneur.co.nz/new-digital-lender-sharing-love/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/nectar-nz-limited", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/symon-nausbaum-3626", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/symon-nausbaum-5418672a", "https://www.bizdb.co.nz/company/9429041980958/", "https://gcifunds.com/case-study/emerging-new-zealand-fintech/", "https://app.dealroom.co/companies/nectar_nz_limited"], "website": "https://nectar.co.nz/", "industry": "Fintech / Consumer Lending", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Draft was substantially accurate. Corrections: (1) Founded year changed 2016 -> 2015 — the NZ Companies Office shows Nectar NZ Limited incorporated 16 Sep 2015 (founder appointed director that day); public launch was early 2017. (2) Description loan range corrected from \\"NZ$2,000-NZ$50,000\\" to up to ~NZ$37,500 (avg ~NZ$11,500), per the Scoop/NZ Adviser reporting. (3) The \\"over NZ$8M equity prior to 2021\\" figure in the draft's fundingNotable could not be independently confirmed and was dropped. (4) Founder's PwC role softened — only BDO Spicers (Corporate Finance) and the ~15-year Instant Finance directorship are firmly sourced; PwC appears only in loosely-worded secondary profiles. Confirmed: sole founder/CEO Symon Nausbaum, active status, Icehouse Ventures backing (also verified via shareholder register), debt facilities (Global Credit Investments senior facility; NZ$10M Cypress Hills Partners mezzanine), Series A NZ$1.2M first close toward NZ$5M target, and >NZ$100M originated. Confidence kept high.", "statusDetail": "Active as of 2026; NZ Companies Office shows Nectar NZ Limited \\"Registered\\" (incorporated 16 Sep 2015) and the company website is live with current content.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Series A led by Icehouse Ventures (an original equity investor): NZ$1.2M first close in Nov 2022 toward a NZ$5M target (reported March 2023). Debt funding includes a senior facility with Global Credit Investments (Sydney) and a NZ$10M mezzanine facility from Cypress Hills Partners (Vancouver). Icehouse Ventures Nominees Ltd appears as a shareholder on the NZ company register.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-melodics	organization	Melodics	Gamified app for learning keys, pad controllers and drums - a "Duolingo" for music practice.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://melodics.com	{"music education",edtech,"music software","consumer app",gamification,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Melodics is an Auckland, New Zealand-based music-technology company that makes software teaching people to play MIDI keyboards, pad controllers (finger drumming) and electronic drums. Its app delivers game-styled lessons, analyses the user's playing and gives real-time feedback on timing, rhythm and accuracy to keep practice engaging. It was conceived in 2014 by former Serato CEO Sam Gribben after he left Serato, and launched in October 2015. The platform reports a community of over 1,000,000 registered musicians worldwide.", "notes": "Icehouse backing is confirmed indirectly: Tuhua Ventures/Tuhua Fund is a venture fund managed by Icehouse Ventures (per Wikipedia's Icehouse Ventures entry and Icehouse's own fund listing), and Tuhua was a named investor in the 2017 round; Melodics also appears in the Icehouse Ventures talent network. Founder caveat: some databases (Tracxn) list Paul Shingles as a 2014 co-founder alongside Gribben, but authoritative NZ reporting (Idealog) states Shingles joined the board as a board member in 2017 (then CCO of Timely, ex-COO of PushPay) — not a founder — so only Gribben is listed. Founding year is 2015 per most sources (idea formed in summer 2014, launched October 2015); some trackers cite 2014. Total funding figures vary by source (US$1.2M named round to ~US$2.89M total per trackers).", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2015", "sources": ["https://idealog.co.nz/venture/2017/09/nz-tech-start-melodics-finds-beat-raises-us12-million", "https://thespinoff.co.nz/business/04-05-2019/melodics-is-the-duolingo-of-learning-to-play-music", "https://www.adsrsounds.com/news/qa-with-sam-gribben-founder-of-melodics/", "https://melodics.com/about", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/samgribben", "https://www.linkedin.com/company/melodics-limited", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/melodics", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icehouse_Ventures", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/163571-68", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/melodics", "https://hoku.nz/ventures/melodics/"], "website": "https://melodics.com", "industry": "Music technology / EdTech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently verified via Idealog, The Spinoff, ADSR, Melodics.com and the Icehouse Ventures talent network. Sam Gribben confirmed as sole founder/CEO and ex-Serato CEO (~10 yrs); Auckland HQ, Oct 2015 launch, 1M+ users, and the Sept 2017 US$1.2M Ableton-led round (with 500 Startups, Tuhua Ventures, K1W1, Alex Rigopulos) all confirmed. Confirmed Paul Shingles was a 2017 board member, NOT a founder (Tracxn miscategorises him), so the draft's single-founder list is correct. Icehouse backing confirmed via Tuhua Ventures (an Icehouse-managed fund). Only minor wording tightened; no factual errors found. Crunchbase page was 403-blocked, but all material facts were corroborated by other authoritative sources.", "statusDetail": "Active and independent; reports 1,000,000+ registered musicians and ongoing product development (e.g. the \\"Songs\\" feature and current mobile apps). Series A was launched in 2019; no public exit or closure reported.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Closed a US$1.2M round in September 2017 led by Berlin-based Ableton, with 500 Startups, NZ funds Tuhua Ventures and K1W1, and Harmonix co-founder Alex Rigopulos; a Series A followed (launched 2019). PitchBook/Tracxn report roughly US$2.89M total raised; figures vary by tracker.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
