org:iv-rocos	organization	Rocos	Cloud platform to connect, monitor and operate robots remotely; acquired by DroneDeploy in 2021.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.rocos.io	{robotics,"cloud platform","robot operations",automation,SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "Rocos was an Auckland, New Zealand robot operations platform that gave robotics companies a cloud backend to connect, monitor and remotely control fleets of robots. Founded in 2017 by David Inggs and Richard Stinear, its software was deployed on robots such as Boston Dynamics' Spot for use cases including agriculture, vineyards and hazardous-environment data capture. In 2021 the company was acquired by US-based DroneDeploy to extend its jobsite automation from aerial drones to ground robots. Terms were undisclosed but reported as an \\"eight-figure\\" sum, and operations remained in New Zealand.", "notes": "Distinct from any same-named foreign company. Both founders independently confirmed by NZ Herald, BusinessDesk, Crunchbase and TheOrg; registry full names are David Kenneth Inggs and Richard Nicholas Stinear. Neno Kabzamalov was an early hire / head of engineering and shareholder, NOT a co-founder, so he is correctly excluded from the founders list. Stage marked Seed as best inference; Rocos raised angel/seed-stage NZ funding and no priced Series round was publicly reported before acquisition; total funding not disclosed. Stinear's exact LinkedIn URL could not be confirmed (null).", "stage": "Seed", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/unleash-the-hounds-nz-robotics-firm-rocos-sold-to-us-company/CDL5RX3FVATC6GZ6PJTF56NU54/", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/technology/ground-meets-air-nz-software-firm-sells-for-eight-figures", "https://www.therobotreport.com/dronedeploy-acquires-robotics-software-startu-rocos/", "https://theorg.com/org/dronedeploy/org-chart/richard-stinear", "https://theorg.com/org/dronedeploy/org-chart/david-inggs", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/rocos", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/rocos"], "website": "https://www.rocos.io", "industry": "Robotics software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Draft was substantially correct. Confirmed: both founders and roles, Auckland NZ, 2017 founding, DroneDeploy 2021 acquisition (eight-figure, post-acquisition roles), and Icehouse Ventures backing (named as investor in NZ Herald + BusinessDesk; was listed on the IV job board, now 404 post-acquisition). Corrections/softening: Stinear's prior Plexure role is Head of Engineering (not CTO — the Plexure CTO title belonged to Inggs); removed \\"Four Forces, Voola\\" from Inggs' background and \\"ICE Angels / Callaghan Innovation\\" from funders as I could not independently confirm them. The \\"late 2017\\" founding nuance retained as 2017. Stinear's LinkedIn URL still unconfirmed (null).", "statusDetail": "Acquired by DroneDeploy (US) in 2021; deal closed ~26 July 2021 and announced ~10-11 August 2021 for an undisclosed \\"eight-figure\\" sum (reported above USD 10M and below the NZ$100M OIO threshold). David Inggs became DroneDeploy's Head of Ground Robotics and Richard Stinear Head of Engineering, Ground Robotics; operations remained in NZ.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Backed by Icehouse Ventures, plus Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1, Aspire NZ Seed Fund, NZ Growth Capital Partners (Crown agency) and the Flux Accelerator. Total raised not publicly disclosed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
