org:iv-aspiring-materials	organization	Aspiring Materials	NZ cleantech turning olivine rock into critical minerals while mineralising industrial CO2	Christchurch, New Zealand	https://www.aspiringmaterials.com	{"carbon capture","carbon mineralisation","critical minerals",cleantech,decarbonisation,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Aspiring Materials is a Christchurch, New Zealand climate-tech company with a patented, waste-free process that extracts critical minerals and essential materials (including magnesium hydroxide, nickel-cobalt-manganese hydroxide, reactive silica and iron) from globally abundant olivine-rich silicate rocks. It uses the magnesium hydroxide to capture and mineralise industrial CO2 emissions into stable carbonates, aiming to decarbonise hard-to-abate industries while reducing critical-mineral supply-chain risk. In March 2025 it opened a critical-minerals pilot production plant in Christchurch, and in May 2025 announced plans for a first commercial-scale facility in Washington State, USA.", "notes": "Founder attribution nuance confirmed: the October 2021 funding press release named Dr Allan Scott (associate professor of civil engineering, University of Canterbury) and Dr Chris Oze as the co-founding scientists. The company's current \\"Our team\\" page lists only two co-founders, Chris Oze (Co-founder/Chief Science Officer) and Mark Chadderton (Co-founder/Chief Executive); Allan Scott does not appear. Scott is therefore a founding co-developer but not a currently listed co-founder, so he is excluded from the founders array to avoid overstating his present role. Founded 2019 (consistent with the 2021 release's \\"two years ago\\"). This is the New Zealand carbon-mineralisation company, distinct from same-named foreign entities. Exact total funding raised is not publicly confirmed.", "stage": "Seed (NZ$1m pre-seed round, Oct 2021)", "status": "active", "founded": "2019", "sources": ["https://www.aspiringmaterials.com/our-team-and-partners", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/BU2110/S00395/aspiring-materials-raises-1m-from-icehouse-ventures-for-carbon-capture-tech.htm", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/climate-tech/kiwi-carbon-capture-startup-aspiring-materials-raises-1-million-seed-round/", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/aspiring-materials-expands-to-the-united-states-to-boost-domestic-supply-of-critical-minerals-302446295.html", "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/aspiring-materials-expands-united-states-120000394.html", "https://www.mining-technology.com/news/aspiring-materials-us-domestic-critical-mineral-supply/", "https://www.christchurchnz.com/business/business-clusters/cleantech/aspiring-materials", "https://www.breakthroughenergy.org/our-work/fellows/lookbook/mark-chadderton/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/aspiring-materials"], "website": "https://www.aspiringmaterials.com", "industry": "Cleantech / Carbon mineralisation and critical minerals", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed against the company's own team page, the Oct 2021 Icehouse-led funding release, and the 6 May 2025 US-expansion announcement (PR Newswire/Mining-Technology). Verified: both co-founders and roles (Oze = Co-founder/CSO, Chadderton = Co-founder/CEO) per the official team page; Icehouse Ventures led the ~NZ$1m pre-seed (Oct 2021) with Outset, plus later backers Motion Capital, K1W1, Breakthrough Energy and Elemental Impact; active status with March 2025 Christchurch pilot plant and planned Washington State commercial facility; Chadderton's industry background and early-2022 full-time start; founded 2019. Allan Scott confirmed as a 2021-named co-founding scientist but absent from the current team page, so correctly left out of the founders array. Minor refinements only (oneLiner shortened, pilot-plant opening dated to March 2025, stage note clarified as pre-seed); no substantive errors found.", "statusDetail": "Active and scaling. Opened a critical-minerals pilot production plant in Christchurch in March 2025, and on 6 May 2025 announced plans for its first commercial-scale facility in Washington State, USA; raising capital for its next growth phase as of 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised a ~NZ$1m pre-seed round in October 2021 led by Icehouse Ventures with support from Outset Ventures. Later named backers include Motion Capital, Outset Ventures, Icehouse Ventures, K1W1, Breakthrough Energy and Elemental Impact. Exact total raised and subsequent round sizes not publicly confirmed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
