org:iv-jasper	organization	Jasper	Tech-enabled commercial real estate fund manager opening up property investing in NZ and Australia	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.jasper.io	{proptech,"commercial real estate","fund management","fractional investment",fintech,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Jasper (Jasper Property Limited) is an Auckland-based, technology-enabled commercial real estate investment and fund manager founded in 2019. It originally launched as a proptech platform offering investors fractional/digitised access to commercial property with lower minimums and improved liquidity, and has deployed multiple wholesale funds across New Zealand and Australia. In February 2023 it spun out its internal software into a separate SaaS company, Caruso, and continued as an active fund manager focused on deal origination, strategy and asset management. By 2025 Jasper reported assets under management surpassing NZ$400 million, concentrated in Auckland industrial/commercial property.", "notes": "This is the New Zealand proptech/CRE fund manager Jasper (jasper.io / Jasper Property Limited), NOT the US AI writing tool \\"Jasper\\" (jasper.ai). Three co-founders independently confirmed: Mark Campbell, Mark Hurley, Oliver Shaw. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed (named in the Sept 2019 ~NZ$2.3m seed round led by M7 Real Estate, alongside James Property Group and RCP). The Caruso SaaS spinout (Feb 2023; Caruso later raised ~NZ$11.2m Series A) is a separate company, not Jasper itself. Funding amounts vary by round/reporting date; treat exact figures as approximate. Oliver Shaw's prior role was at Little Giant (which became part of Isobar after the Dentsu acquisition), not directly \\"Lead Product Developer at Isobar.\\"", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2019", "sources": ["https://ecommercenews.co.nz/story/jasper-raises-2-3m-led-by-european-real-estate-investment-giant", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/BU1906/S00105/entrepreneur-to-transform-commercial-property-investment.htm", "https://www.jasper.io/news/jasper-spins-out-technology-into-new-saas-company", "https://www.jasper.io/news/jasper-surpasses-$300-million-in-assets-under-management", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/alumni/our-alumni/40-under-40/a-z-list-of-profiles/mark-campbell.html", "https://www.stuff.co.nz/business/117674493/proptech-startup-jasper-aims-to-open-up-commercial-property-investing-to-a-lot-more-people", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/companies/banking-finance/property-fund-manager-jasper-opens-second-capital-raise-sets-up-secondary-market/DLYG5TIAREN6S2ELG3S26OV3TM/", "https://www.dentsu.com/au/en/our-news/news-releases/dentsu-aegis-network-acquires-little-giant", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/northern-advocate/news/former-northlander-little-giant-ceo-mark-hurley-a-finalist-in-ey-entrepreneur-of-the-year/XPJE5PNJC3NT3E2FAU5ZFSJRFQ/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/mark-hurley-3", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/oliverjshaw"], "website": "https://www.jasper.io", "industry": "Proptech / Commercial Real Estate Investment", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All four target facts independently confirmed via fresh searches: (1) the three founders (Campbell, Hurley, Shaw) are real and correctly roled; (2) Jasper is still active as a CRE fund manager (AUM over NZ$400m, transacting in 2025); (3) Icehouse Ventures did back the Sept 2019 ~NZ$2.3m seed round (ecommercenews/Scoop); (4) description/oneLiner accurate, including the Feb 24 2023 Caruso spinout with Campbell remaining sole CEO. Minor corrections: clarified Oliver Shaw's prior role was at Little Giant (which became part of Isobar via Dentsu), not \\"Lead Product Developer at Isobar\\"; tightened the lead/participant framing of the seed round (M7 led, Icehouse participated); removed the unverifiable \\"Blackstone/M7 Pan-European JV\\" specifics from Campbell's bio (only M7 Real Estate is directly sourced) and the low-certainty \\"Dallas split time\\" detail for Hurley.", "statusDetail": "Active as a commercial real estate fund manager across NZ and Australia (AUM reported over NZ$400m by 2025, still transacting). In Feb 2023 it spun out its technology into a separate SaaS company, Caruso; co-founders Mark Hurley and Oliver Shaw moved to lead Caruso while co-founder Mark Campbell remained as sole CEO of Jasper.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~NZ$2.3m seed (announced September 2019) led by European real estate manager M7 Real Estate, with Icehouse Ventures, James Property Group and RCP also participating; subsequently raised over NZ$80m in equity from wholesale/private investors across six funds (reported AUM ~NZ$320m by early 2023, surpassing NZ$400m by 2025).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
