org:iv-mccarthy-finch	organization	McCarthyFinch	NZ legal-AI startup whose authorAI engine reads, drafts and reasons like a lawyer (acquired by Onit, 2020)	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.mccarthyfinch.com	{"legal AI",legaltech,"contract review","document automation",NLP,"Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "McCarthyFinch was a New Zealand legal-AI company that spun out of law firm MinterEllisonRuddWatts in 2017 as a joint venture with boutique VC Goat Ventures. Its authorAI platform and authorDOCS product used AI to augment lawyers in reviewing and drafting contracts, claiming up to 70% faster contract reviews and 50%+ productivity gains. It was a 2018 TechCrunch Disrupt Battlefield alumnus and at acquisition had about 45 customers and 17 employees. In November 2020 it was acquired by Houston-based legal-software firm Onit, Inc., with its technology folded into the Onit AI Center of Excellence.", "notes": "Company name is one word \\"McCarthyFinch\\" (input was \\"McCarthy Finch\\"). Do not confuse with same-named foreign firms (e.g., recruitment agencies). Jean Yang was VP of Legal (a founding-team executive), not an independently sourced co-founder, so she is omitted from founders. James Schellhase served as executive chairman around a later funding round. Website mccarthyfinch.com now redirects/relates to Onit. Icehouse Ventures backing remains unconfirmed: the only Icehouse linkage is a PitchBook entry under the post-2020 \\"Onit AI Center of Excellence\\" rebrand, which appears to be a data-conflation artifact, not evidence Icehouse backed McCarthyFinch directly.", "stage": "Acquired (raised ~US$5M before exit)", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2020/11/17/2128393/0/en/Onit-Acquires-New-Zealand-based-McCarthyFinch-to-Drive-Innovation-with-Artificial-Intelligence-and-Workflow-Automation.html", "https://techcrunch.com/2020/11/20/onit-acquires-legal-startup-mccarthyfinch-to-inject-ai-into-legal-workflows/", "https://www.onit.com/news/onit-acquires-mccarthyfinch/", "https://www.thelawyermag.com/nz/news/general/mccarthyfinch-appoints-new-executive-chairman-confirms-new-funding-round/206943", "https://www.artificiallawyer.com/2019/08/21/antipodean-ai-mccarthyfinch-launches-authordocs-for-legal-drafting/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/mccarthyfinch/__LdhSqd1fQO_DdnEf1HuOp-F3fWOB7e7r5fF8TYDBQlM/funding-and-investors", "https://www.lawnext.com/2020/11/onit-adds-to-its-enterprise-workflow-offerings-with-acquisition-of-ai-company-mccarthyfinch.html"], "website": "https://www.mccarthyfinch.com", "industry": "Legal technology (Legal AI)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirmed all key claims via primary sources. TechCrunch confirms ~US$5M raised, 45 customers and 17 employees at acquisition. GlobeNewswire/Onit confirm the Nov 2020 Onit acquisition, Nick Whitehouse as co-founder/CEO (became GM of the Onit AI Center of Excellence), and Jean Yang as VP of Legal (not a founder). NZ Lawyer/CB Insights confirm the JV origin (MinterEllisonRuddWatts + Goat Ventures) and investor list (Goat Ventures, MinterEllisonRuddWatts, K1W1, First NZ Capital, NZVIF, Fantail Ventures); Icehouse Ventures appears in none of them. authorAI/authorDOCS product names confirmed by Artificial Lawyer. Minor smoothing of oneLiner/statusDetail wording; no factual corrections needed. Icehouse backing kept as unconfirmed (effectively not backed).", "statusDetail": "Acquired by Onit, Inc. (Houston, USA) in November 2020; technology rebranded into the Onit AI Center of Excellence and Onit's Precedent AI platform. Deal terms undisclosed.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "~US$5M total raised (per TechCrunch). NZ media named founding investors Goat Ventures and MinterEllisonRuddWatts, plus K1W1, First NZ Capital, NZ Venture Investment Fund (NZVIF) and Fantail Ventures. Icehouse Ventures was not named among McCarthyFinch's investors.", "icehouseBacked": "unconfirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
