org:iv-solve	organization	Solve (Solve Data Inc.)	The "data engine for ecommerce" — real-time data warehousing for DTC/ecommerce brands	New York, USA (engineering team in Wellington, New Zealand)	https://www.solve.io/	{eCommerce,"data warehouse","first-party data",DTC,SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Solve (Solve Data Inc.) is a data platform for ecommerce and DTC brands, positioning itself as the \\"data engine for ecommerce.\\" Its core product is a real-time data warehouse and management layer that can run in the customer's own cloud, giving brands ownership of their first-party data to power segmentation, lifetime value, attribution, cart recovery and messaging. It was founded by the team behind the marketing-automation platform Sailthru (acquired 2018) — Neil Capel (CEO), Guy Horrocks and Nick Gundry — and is New York-based with an engineering team in Wellington, New Zealand. Named customers on its site include Minnow, COAT Paints and AS Beauty.", "notes": "Disambiguation: the Icehouse-backed NZ-linked \\"Solve\\" is Solve Data Inc. / solve.io (ecommerce data-warehouse platform; Icehouse portfolio page links directly to solve.io). It is NOT \\"Solve Intelligence\\" (AI-for-patents, YC-backed), \\"Solve Consultants\\" (solve.co.nz accounting consultancy), or \\"Solve IT\\" (Auckland IT support). The legal entity is \\"Solve Data Limited\\" (Wellington). Founding year is ambiguous across sources: the venture is widely described as founded 2019 by the ex-Sailthru team, but Tracxn/Preqin list the entity as 2012 and a seed round in Sept 2020 — kept 2019 with a caveat.", "stage": "Seed / early-stage (Series A per some databases; exact round details unconfirmed)", "status": "active", "founded": "2019", "sources": ["https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/portfolio", "https://www.solve.io/", "https://www.movac.co.nz/fund-5/investment-notes-3-solve/", "https://www.movac.co.nz/portfolio/solve/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/solve-data/__6wXsRXRQRub9HT23mPFGeBgKI3fbSIaCCu1K6T87l-k", "https://www.preqin.com/data/profile/asset/solve-data-limited/443106", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/solve-io", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/neilcapel/", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/guyhorrocks/", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/nickgundry/"], "website": "https://www.solve.io/", "industry": "eCommerce data platform / data warehousing & marketing automation software (SaaS)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Icehouse backing CONFIRMED — Icehouse Ventures' portfolio page explicitly lists \\"Solve\\" linking to solve.io; Movac (own investment note) and Bowery Capital also confirmed as investors. All three founders independently confirmed via Movac's investment note and portfolio page: Neil Capel (CEO), Guy Horrocks, and Nick Gundry — Gundry's LinkedIn (in/nickgundry, Portland OR) and his product-lead role were located and added (draft had these as null/unconfirmed). CORRECTED: removed the unverified \\"~US$3.1M revenue\\" claim (Tracxn/Preqin: revenue not disclosed) and the unverified customer list (Crown Affair, D.S. & Durga, Cariuma, Emma Lewisham) — replaced with the brands actually shown on solve.io (Minnow, COAT Paints, AS Beauty). Product description reframed toward its core (real-time data warehousing in the customer's own cloud) per Movac. Founding-year discrepancy (2012 entity vs 2019 venture) flagged. Confidence raised to high. LinkedIn/Crunchbase profile pages returned HTTP 403/blocked direct fetch, so some founder detail relies on search-surfaced snippets.", "statusDetail": "Active as of 2026; privately held, ~29 employees (Tracxn, April 2026). Revenue not publicly disclosed.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Backed by NZ VCs Icehouse Ventures (listed in its portfolio, linking to solve.io) and Movac (which published a seed-round investment note), plus US firm Bowery Capital. Specific round amounts/dates not disclosed publicly.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572