org:iv-toku-eyes	organization	Toku (formerly Toku Eyes / Toku, Inc.)	AI that reads standard retinal images to screen for heart, kidney and eye disease	San Diego, USA (originally Auckland, New Zealand)	https://tokueyes.com	{AI,"retinal imaging",oculomics,medtech,"preventive health","Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "Toku is an AI health-tech company founded in New Zealand (out of the University of Auckland) that uses artificial intelligence and standard color retinal (fundus) photographs to non-invasively screen for chronic disease. Its products include THEIA (diabetic eye screening), CLAiR (cardiovascular risk), BioAge (biological age) and MyKidneyAI (chronic kidney disease). The company re-incorporated in the US and moved its headquarters to San Diego as it pursued FDA approval and US market entry. In October 2025 Topcon Healthcare signed a definitive agreement to acquire Toku, Inc.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing is firmly confirmed: it led Toku's first external (seed) raise in 2021 with Artemis Capital and Kera Link, and returned for the US$8m Series A. Disambiguation is critical: this is NOT \\"Toku\\" the APAC cloud-communications/CX fintech (toku.co), which closed a separate US$5m Series A extension in Nov 2024 (led by Betatron) — that company is unrelated. The company rebranded from \\"Toku Eyes\\" to \\"Toku, Inc.\\" as it relocated to the US (Atlanta, then San Diego). Diana Siew (named in one UniServices source) is omitted as she could not be independently confirmed as a co-founder. David Squirrell is confirmed as a genuine co-founder/CMO but no longer appears on the current team page (CMO/Chief Health Officer role is now Michael V. McConnell). Founding year is reported as both 2018 and 2019 across sources.", "stage": "Series A (acquired)", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2019", "sources": ["https://tokueyes.com/our-team/", "https://tokueyes.com/blog/a-new-zealand-startup-using-ai-to-detect-eye-disease-raises-3-35-million/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/toku-eyes-raises-millions-for-ai-tech-that-helps-stop-diabetes-preventable-blindness/PUFQCE5XZOGONYVW5PLDMP6KGQ/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/toku-eyes-poised-for-us-breakthrough-after-big-industry-names-back-135m-raise/O24QIZ424ZFMVC37G6WDGJSPR4/", "https://topconhealthcare.com/article/topcon-healthcare-inc-signs-acquisition-agreement-for-toku-inc-to-expand-fast-non-invasive-chronic-disease-screening/", "https://www.nationalvision.com/news/2023/04/17/toku-inc-series-a-preferred-investment-round-led-by-national-vision-inc-and-topcon-healthcare/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/david-squirrell", "https://www.nzoptics.co.nz/live-articles/topcon-acquires-toku-eyes-ahead-of-us-tech-rollout/", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/stories/toku-eyes-ai-interpreted-retinal-images/"], "website": "https://tokueyes.com", "industry": "Healthcare AI / Medtech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Both founders (Vaghefi, Squirrell) and Icehouse Ventures backing independently confirmed; acquisition by Topcon (announced 17 Oct 2025) confirmed. Key correction: the draft's \\"US$5m Series A extension (2024)\\" and its cited businesswire source (20241120446777) belong to an UNRELATED company (Toku cloud-communications, toku.co), not Toku Eyes — removed both. The US$8m Series A co-led by National Vision and Topcon actually closed April 2023 (not 2022/2024). NZ$8.5m pre-money valuation and ~NZ$4m grants confirmed via NZ Herald. Founding year ambiguous (2018 vs 2019 in sources); kept 2019. Squirrell's LinkedIn left null (unconfirmed) and Diana Siew remains omitted.", "statusDetail": "Definitive acquisition agreement signed by Topcon Healthcare, Inc., announced 17 October 2025; financial terms not disclosed.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "First external (seed) raise of ~NZ$3.6m (A$3.35m), announced June 2021, led by Icehouse Ventures with Artemis Capital and Kera Link International, at a pre-money valuation of ~NZ$8.5m; earlier non-dilutive support came from UniServices and the Mafsen family plus ~NZ$4m in HRC/MBIE/Callaghan Innovation grants. A US$8m (~NZ$13m) Series A closed in April 2023, co-led by National Vision and Topcon Healthcare, with Icehouse Ventures returning. Aggregators (Crunchbase/Tracxn) report roughly US$10.5m raised in total.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
