org:adora	organization	Adora	AI platform that maps your live product experience in real time and flags user friction.	Sydney, Australia	https://www.adora.ai	{"Developer Tools",Active,"Blackbird Portfolio","Product Analytics",SaaS}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "Software", "status": "Active", "twitter": "https://twitter.com/Adora_software", "website": "https://www.adora.ai", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/adora-so", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio/adora", "https://www.blackbird.vc/blog/investment-notes-adora-seed", "https://www.adora.ai/about-us/", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/former-canva-execs-product-mapping-startup-adora-designs-9-9-million-seed-round/", "https://www.smartcompany.com.au/startupsmart/former-canva-executive-9-9-million-funding-product-mapping-startup-adora/", "https://www.thesaasnews.com/news/adora-raises-7-million-seed-round", "https://designerfund.com/blog/announcing-adora", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/adora-aeeb", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/iamnathanscully/"], "confidence": "high", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["logoUrl", "founders.twitterUrl", "founders.website"]}, "hqCountry": "Australia", "crunchbase": "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/adora-aeeb", "subSectors": ["Product Analytics", "SaaS", "Artificial Intelligence", "Session Replay", "Developer/Product Tools"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": 2023, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": "$7M (US$7M / A$9.9M Seed)", "fundingStage": "Seed", "snappedSector": "Developer Tools", "matchedCompany": "Adora (Adora Software Pty Ltd / adora.ai) — AI product-experience mapping platform", "totalRaisedUsd": 7000000, "longDescription": "Adora is a product insights platform that automatically maps a company's entire live product experience in real time, capturing every screen, journey, and interaction across all languages, devices, and user types. Its AI analyses the captured experience to surface friction points, broken flows, and hidden issues, each attached to session replays, so product teams can understand exactly what users experience without manual event tagging. Founded in 2023 by former Canva and Amazon leaders, it launched from private beta with teams at Canva, Notion, Replit, Granola, and Chess.com, and roughly 2,000 companies on its waitlist. Adora is backed by Blackbird Ventures, which led its US$7M (A$9.9M) seed round."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
org:alloy-robotics	organization	Alloy Robotics	Data platform that lets robotics teams search and analyze robot data via natural language	Sydney, Australia	https://www.usealloy.ai/	{"Deep Tech & Hardware",Active,"Blackbird Portfolio","Robotics data infrastructure","Artificial intelligence / Physical AI"}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "Robotics", "status": "Active", "twitter": "https://x.com/alloyrobotics", "website": "https://www.usealloy.ai/", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/alloyrobotics", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio/alloy", "https://www.blackbird.vc/blog/investment-notes-alloy", "https://techcrunch.com/2025/09/23/alloy-is-bringing-data-management-to-the-robotics-industry/", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/waymo-tesla-execs-back-robotics-data-analytics-startup-alloys-4-5-million-pre-seed-round/", "https://www.smartcompany.com.au/startupsmart/alloy-raises-4-5-million-simplify-robotics-data/", "https://www.capitalbrief.com/briefing/robotics-platform-alloy-raises-45m-in-pre-seed-round-led-by-blackbird-2d2cf1c1-524e-4a21-8df3-cc3f73370bcd/", "https://www.usealloy.ai/", "https://www.linkedin.com/company/alloyrobotics", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/josephdharris/"], "confidence": "high", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["crunchbase", "logoUrl", "founders.Joe Harris.twitterUrl", "founders.Joe Harris.website", "founders.Aaqif Zaman.linkedinUrl", "founders.Bernardo Croll.linkedinUrl", "founders.Julia Chen.linkedinUrl"]}, "hqCountry": "Australia", "crunchbase": null, "subSectors": ["Robotics data infrastructure", "Artificial intelligence / Physical AI", "Developer tools / DevOps", "Data analytics", "Enterprise software"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": 2025, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": "A$4.5M (~US$3M)", "fundingStage": "Pre-Seed", "snappedSector": "Deep Tech & Hardware", "matchedCompany": "Alloy (Alloy Technologies Operations Pty Ltd) — usealloy.ai, robotics data platform", "totalRaisedUsd": 3000000, "longDescription": "Alloy builds the data infrastructure layer for robotics teams. Its platform automatically organizes, searches, and analyzes multimodal robot data — images, time-series sensor data, and system logs from MCAP/ROS files — using natural language queries, turning days-long failure investigations into minute-long queries and letting engineers export findings directly as training datasets. Robots can generate up to a terabyte of data per day, and Alloy positions itself as the deployment/monitoring layer for the \\"physical AI\\" revolution. Founded in Sydney in early 2025, it has signed multiple Australian robotics companies as design partners across drone, maritime, defence, and agricultural use cases and is expanding into the US."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
