org:iv-kitea-health	organization	Kitea Health	NZ medtech building a tiny battery-free implantable pressure sensor, first for hydrocephalus	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.kiteahealth.com/	{medtech,"implantable devices",hydrocephalus,"remote patient monitoring",neurotech,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Kitea Health is an Auckland-based medtech company developing miniature, battery-free implantable digital pressure sensors for managing chronic conditions. Its lead clinical application is hydrocephalus (monitoring brain pressure and shunt function), with longer-term plans for heart failure via pulmonary artery pressure monitoring; the rice-grain-sized sensor is read by a wireless wand and app. Spun out of the University of Auckland's Auckland Bioengineering Institute in May 2022, it implanted sensors in adults at Auckland Hospital from mid-2024 and reported a world-first implant in a child with hydrocephalus in January 2025. The device is not yet approved for clinical use and the company is preparing for human trials in the US.", "notes": "Auckland Bioengineering Institute (University of Auckland) spinout, formed May 2022; not to be confused with same-named foreign entities. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed: it participated in the 2023 NZ$6m seed (led by Pacific Channel) and led the oversubscribed NZ$13m pre-Series A (NZ Herald, Dec 2025), and profiled the company in its \\"Startup Blueprint\\" series. Company lists a secondary US address in Camden, Delaware. The company's own site/Icehouse profile now frame heart failure (pulmonary artery pressure monitoring) as the larger commercial opportunity, with hydrocephalus as the lead/initial clinical application. Funding figures are in NZ dollars.", "stage": "Pre-Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2022", "sources": ["https://www.kiteahealth.com/", "https://www.kiteahealth.com/about", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/startup-blueprint-kiteahealth", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/kitea-health-closes-13m-raise-lines-up-human-trials-in-the-us/premium/O3EXTV5CLFHGDBMRRSOJ5QUBWQ/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/kitea-health-raises-6m-as-its-implant-nears-human-trials/FGIMXHRZLJHIDMTBW26ZJMN7BM/", "https://www.pacificchannel.com/stories/pacific-channel-leads-6m-capital-raise-in-kitea-health", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/stories/kitea-health-implantable-tech-battling-chronic-conditions/", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/news/2025/01/24/first-child-receives-brain-sensor.html", "https://www.nzgcp.co.nz/portfolio/case-study/kitea-health", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/kitea-health"], "website": "https://www.kiteahealth.com/", "industry": "Medical devices / Medtech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All key facts independently confirmed via fresh sources. Founders (Simon Malpas CEO, Natalia Lopez COO, Bryon Wright CTO) verified on the company About page and Icehouse blueprint. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed (led the NZ$13m Dec 2025 round; participated in the 2023 seed). NZ$13m oversubscribed pre-Series A close (Dec 2025) with Bioshore and Karst Peak Rx, NZ$6m 2023 seed led by Pacific Channel, and ~NZ$14m grants all confirmed via NZ Herald. Corrections/additions: found and added Natalia Lopez's LinkedIn URL (was null in draft); tightened the oneLiner to <=110 chars and removed the unverified 'world's smallest' superlative phrasing; clarified that Malpas previously co-founded Telemetry Research (sold 2012) and Kaha Sciences (sold 2020) per NZ Herald, rather than the draft's unsourced 'three companies / US chief scientist / Royal Society Fellow 2018' claims, which I could not independently confirm and removed; adjusted the description to reflect that hydrocephalus is the lead clinical application while heart failure is the longer-term commercial target.", "statusDetail": "Active and privately held; closed an oversubscribed NZ$13m pre-Series A round (December 2025) and is preparing for human trials in the US. Device not yet approved for clinical use.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "NZ$6m seed round in 2023 (led by Pacific Channel; Icehouse Ventures, Auckland UniServices, Cure Kids Ventures, NZGCP and angels also participated); oversubscribed NZ$13m pre-Series A round closed December 2025 led by Icehouse Ventures, with Sydney-based health-tech VCs Bioshore and Karst Peak Rx (KP Rx). Also received ~NZ$14m in research grants (including a 2017 MBIE Endeavour fund grant).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
