, "https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/why-uc/our-alumni/alumni-stories/hannah-hardy-jones", "https://www.chrislynchmedia.com/news-items/christchurch-ai-startup-secures-4-1-million-in-seed-funding/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/contentedai"], "website": "https://www.contentedai.com", "industry": "Artificial Intelligence / SaaS (conversation intelligence & document generation)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed via fresh searches: both founders (Lucy Pink, Hannah Hardy-Jones) are real, correctly named, and accurately described as Co-founders (company About page + LinkedIn + multiple media); active status confirmed; Icehouse Ventures participation confirmed by BusinessDesk and IT Brief; full investor list (incl. Phase One Ventures, Exhort Ventures, Shearwater Capital, K1W1, Aspire NZ Seed Fund) confirmed by IT Brief; description and oneLiner accurate. Minor corrections: trimmed the description's unverifiable financial-services/legal sector list to sectors actually cited by sources, removed an unsourced claim about a \\"product-data marketplace\\" from Pink's background, and clarified in notes/funding that the round amount is reported variably as NZD $4.1m / AUD $4.1m / ~USD $2.5m. No fabricated facts found in the draft; founder titles remain Co-founder as no exec titles are publicly stated.", "statusDetail": "Active; closed a $4.1m seed round (announced Feb 2026) led by Altered Capital, expanding into Australia, the UK and US.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~$4.1m seed (oversubscribed) led by Altered Capital, with K1W1, Icehouse Ventures, Aspire NZ Seed Fund, Phase One Ventures, Exhort Ventures and Australia's Shearwater Capital. Reached ~NZD $1.4m ARR before raising. Amount cited as both NZD $4.1m and AUD $4.1m (and ~USD $2.5m in some international coverage); treat as approximate.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-spalk	organization	Spalk	Cloud commentary platform letting broadcasters produce remote, multi-language sports commentary	New York, USA (founded in Auckland, New Zealand)	https://www.spalk.tv	{"sports tech",broadcast,"live commentary",SaaS,media,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Spalk is a New Zealand-founded sports-broadcast technology company whose cloud-based Virtual Commentary Studio lets leagues, broadcasters and rights holders produce and lip-sync remote, multi-language commentary on live sports. Founded in Auckland in 2015 by Ben Reynolds, Michael Prendergast and Sam Viskovich after they built an online following commentating games (Viskovich later left to found UTTR), it now counts the NFL, MLB, DAZN and the Bundesliga among its clients and says it has reached tens of millions of fans. The platform offers a roster of vetted commentators across dozens of languages, positioned as a lower-cost alternative to on-site production. The company operates from New York while retaining its Auckland engineering base.", "notes": "Multiple same-named entities exist; this profile is the NZ-founded sports-commentary platform spalk.tv (Spalk Ltd), not any foreign namesake. Spalk's current about-us page lists only Reynolds (CEO) and Prendergast (CTO) as co-founders, but contemporaneous NZ media confirm Sam Viskovich was an original third co-founder who left around 2016 (now founder/CMO of UTTR). Current non-founder leadership includes Tom Read (Chief Creative Officer) and Matt Smith (Head of Production). Founding origin tied to the 2015 Cricket World Cup, the University of Auckland Velocity programme and Vodafone Xone incubator.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2015", "sources": ["https://www.spalk.tv/about-us", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/talking-sports-commentary-with-spalk-co-founder-ben-reynolds", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/spalk", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/steven-adams-backs-nz-alternative-commentary-startup-spalk-as-it-raises-millions/42NBCS6WV7VU2E7Y5B4Q5V7OQ4/", "https://nzentrepreneur.co.nz/startup-watch-spalk/", "https://www.stuff.co.nz/business/industries/82731717/university-startup-challenge-gives-chance-for-student-founders-to-pitch-for-funding", "https://idealog.co.nz/innovators/2016/08/vodafone-xone-innovators-series-spalks-sam-viskovich-sacrifices-snails-and-why-justin-marshall-should-be-worried", "https://www.sportbusiness.com/news/spalk-completes-3m-series-a-funding-round-led-by-greg-norman-company/", "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/spalk/financials", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/spalk", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/alumni/our-alumni/40-under-40/a-z-list-of-profiles/ben-reynolds.html"], "website": "https://www.spalk.tv", "industry": "Sports broadcast technology / SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Confirmed the company is real, NZ-founded (Auckland, 2015) and Icehouse Ventures-backed (since 2015, plus the 2021 Series A). Corrections: (1) Added a third, well-sourced original co-founder, Sam Viskovich, who the draft omitted (he left ~2016 and now runs UTTR); (2) the US$3M Series A (8 Jul 2021) was LED by the Greg Norman Company, not merely an athlete investor as the draft implied; (3) total funding is ~US$4.5M per Crunchbase/CB Insights, not the ~US$7.75M PitchBook figure in the draft, so that was lowered; (4) softened the \\"patented\\" and \\"50+ languages / thousands of commentators\\" claims to \\"dozens of languages,\\" which sources support (e.g., 21 languages for the 2022 World Cup), as the larger figures and a granted patent could not be independently confirmed; (5) tightened the oneLiner to under 110 chars. Greg Norman was not retained as an athlete-investor since his company led the round; Mitch Evans and Steven Adams remain confirmed athlete investors.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating; its website lists the NFL, MLB, DAZN and the Bundesliga as clients, and it remains listed in the Icehouse Ventures portfolio.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised a US$3M Series A on 8 July 2021 led by the Greg Norman Company, with Stadia Ventures, Icehouse Ventures and APEX Capital participating plus athlete investors including Steven Adams and Mitch Evans. Crunchbase/CB Insights report total funding of about US$4.5M across roughly six rounds; Icehouse Ventures has backed the company since 2015 (with Ice Angels support).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-hnry	organization	Hnry	Automated tax and accounting platform for sole traders, freelancers and contractors.	Wellington, New Zealand	https://hnry.co.nz/	{fintech,accounting,tax,"sole traders",SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Hnry is a New Zealand fintech that provides an all-in-one digital accounting and payments service for the self-employed. It automatically calculates, pays and files taxes, and handles invoicing, expenses, insurance and on-demand accountant support for sole traders, freelancers and contractors. Founded in Wellington by James and Claire Fuller, it has expanded across New Zealand, Australia and the UK. As of December 2025 it had raised almost NZ$100 million since 2018.", "notes": "This is the Wellington, NZ-founded fintech \\"Hnry\\" (hnry.co.nz), distinct from any same-named foreign entity. Founding year is reported variably as 2016 (incorporation), 2017 (NZ launch, per the company's own about page) and 2018 (operations/product launch, cited in funding announcements); used 2017 per the company about page. Claire Fuller's LinkedIn URL (/in/fullerclaire) was surfaced in search results but not opened directly due to LinkedIn's auth wall; her Co-founder & COO role is independently confirmed by Crunchbase and RocketReach.", "stage": "Series C", "status": "active", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://hnry.co.nz/about/", "https://hnry.co.nz/resources/news/hnry-raises-30-mil-to-accelerate-growth/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/581391/tech-firm-hnry-raises-more-than-30m-in-latest-funding-round", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/deals/movac-finally-gets-to-sit-with-hnry-after-30m-series-c-raise/", "https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/investors", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/claire-fuller", "https://www.airtree.vc/open-source-vc/our-investment-in-hnry", "https://www.fintechfutures.com/2023/01/new-zealand-accounting-fintech-hnry-bags-24-5m-in-series-b-funding/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/small-business/nz-accounting-firm-hnry-eye