org:iv-ideally	organization	Ideally	On-demand AI insights platform delivering overnight concept testing for brands	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.goideally.com	{"market research","consumer insights","concept testing",AI,SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Ideally is a New Zealand-founded research and insights platform that lets brands rapidly test concepts, ideas and messages with their target audience and receive robust, statistically valid answers overnight, at a price point it claims is around 10x more affordable than conventional market research. The self-service platform uses built-in generative AI to summarise responses and surface patterns. Founded in 2023, it has grown to serve 250+ brands across markets including the US, Australasia and Singapore, with offices in Auckland, Sydney, Melbourne and New York. It emerged from TRA Labs and Previously Unavailable (the partnership also behind Tracksuit); The Research Agency (TRA) remains its largest shareholder.", "notes": "Disambiguation: the NZ company's site is goideally.com - NOT ideally.com (a US e-commerce company) or ideally.io (Finnish firm). Icehouse backing firmly confirmed: led the ~NZ$2M seed (Jan 2024), co-led the NZ$6M seed extension (Sept/Oct 2024 with OIF Ventures), and named as returning investor in the April 2026 Series A. Origin is TRA Labs + Previously Unavailable (same partnership behind Tracksuit); TRA remains largest shareholder (~42% per Sept 2024 Companies Office filing). Founder locations are Auckland (HQ + NZ LinkedIn profiles). Series A cited as both ~US$10M and NZ$16M - same round, different currency.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2023", "sources": ["https://www.goideally.com/about-us", "https://www.goideally.com/stories/weve-raised-16m-to-reinvent-research-heres-what-comes-next", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/startup-blueprint-ideally", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/kiwi-product-development-insights-platform-ideally-lands-2-million-seed-round/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/we-couldnt-have-done-it-without-ai-ideally-raises-6m/G3UGK3SVYRED3AQY2VHRBQZLJQ/", "https://campaignbrief.co.nz/2026/04/21/ideally-secures-16m-series-a-to-reinvent-the-90b-market-research-industry/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/ideally-raises-16m-at-100m-valuation-for-its-ai-powered-market-research-software/premium/H6Q2JTAOIFBHJOK2XDSNPCRNY4/", "https://www.research-live.com/article/news/ideally-raises-10m-for-us-expansion/id/5148673", "https://tomis.tech/blog/tomis-acquires-new-zealand-based-yonder/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/brendancervin", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/ideally-a895"], "website": "https://www.goideally.com", "industry": "Market research / SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All key facts independently confirmed by fresh searches. The three founders, their roles, and prior backgrounds (Donald-Yonder/TOMIS; Cervin-GeoOp/ArchiPro/Yabble/Tru-Test, UoA BE; Nu'u-Steele-Parkable/Booking.com) all verified. Status (active, US/NY expansion), Icehouse backing (seed Jan 2024 led, NZ$6M seed extension Sept/Oct 2024 led, Series A returning investor), and Series A (NZ$16M/US$10M, April 2026, led by Shearwater Capital, >NZ$100M valuation) all confirmed. Minor refinements: origin specified as TRA Labs + Previously Unavailable with TRA as largest shareholder (~42%); the NZ$6M seed extension was co-led with OIF Ventures (not noted in draft); removed the unverified 'AI chatbot/review system' framing of Yonder. Removed 'in Auckland' from the founding-year claim in description since sources say founded in NZ (HQ Auckland/Grey Lynn) without pinning the founding city explicitly.", "statusDetail": "Active and scaling internationally; opened a New York office and expanding into North America following its April 2026 Series A.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised NZ$16M Series A in April 2026 (~US$10M) at a valuation over NZ$100M (~US$59M), led by Shearwater Capital