base.com/person/mark-gatt-bfe5", "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/thinkladder", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/469726-93", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/thinkladder/__0Kh45a0N7buPXpZbLvjKgGqgmKUU4BdIvyRY2sgDLyE", "https://www.localmatters.co.nz/news/local-folk-mark-gatt/", "https://apps.apple.com/nz/app/thinkladder-self-awareness/id1284511883", "https://www.thinkladder.com/faqs/", "https://yourstory.com/2018/09/app-fridays-thinkladder-wants-pocket-therapist-patients-depression-anxiety"], "website": "https://www.thinkladder.com", "industry": "Digital mental health / wellness software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirmed the draft's key claims. Founders Mark Gatt (Founder & CEO, prior project manager at Springboard Community Works running the Futureworks programme — confirmed via Local Matters and Tracxn) and Kate/Katie Gatt (co-founder, counsellor) are real and correctly named/roled; corrected priorBackground to specify the Futureworks programme and clarified hqLocation as Snells Beach in the Auckland region. Icehouse Ventures backing is corroborated by Crunchbase, CB Insights, PitchBook and Tracxn (not directly listed on Icehouse's own portfolio page, but four aggregators agree), alongside Flux Accelerator, NZGCP, Callaghan Innovation and MBIE; ~NZ$1.25M seed, Apr 5 2018. Status confirmed active (App Store v3.40, Aug 16 2025). Could NOT independently load LinkedIn (HTTP 999) to verify Mark's exact profile URL — retained from draft but unverified; Kate Gatt's LinkedIn not found (null). CB Insights' 2016 founding year conflicts with the 2015 used by most sources; kept 2015 and noted the discrepancy.", "statusDetail": "Active and independent; app (Think Ladder Limited) still updated, with version 3.40 released August 16, 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Reported to have raised roughly NZ$1.25M total in a single seed round (dated April 5, 2018 by data providers) with investors including Icehouse Ventures, 