ures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-the-insides-company	organization	The Insides Company	NZ medtech behind The Insides System, a chyme reinfusion therapy for intestinal failure	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.theinsides.co	{medtech,"medical devices","intestinal failure","chyme reinfusion","university spin-out","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "The Insides Company is an Auckland, New Zealand medtech firm that develops The Insides System, a chyme (intestinal contents) reinfusion device for patients with intestinal failure as an alternative to parenteral nutrition. Founded in 2017 as a University of Auckland / UniServices spin-out (originally Surgical Design Studio) by colorectal surgeons and biomedical engineers, it commercialised the device after an early-stage round led by Icehouse Ventures. The Insides System holds US FDA Breakthrough Device designation and has CE marking and regulatory clearance across markets including the UK, Europe, Australia and New Zealand. It remains a private, operating business led by CEO Garth Sutherland.", "notes": "Not to be confused with same-named foreign businesses; this is the NZ University of Auckland medtech spin-out (originally Surgical Design Studio). Icehouse backing confirmed: it led the bulk of the ~NZ$4.3m August 2019 round (per theicehouse.co.nz). The four scientific/clinical co-founders (Greg O'Grady, Ian Bissett, John Davidson, Rob Davidson) are independently sourced via UniServices and the company about page; Garth Sutherland is the CEO who led commercialisation (joined ~2019, not an original scientific founder). LinkedIn URLs for the four scientific founders were not located, so left null; Garth Sutherland's LinkedIn is confirmed. Total funding (~NZ$10m) is from secondary reporting and not precisely confirmed.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.theinsides.co/about", "https://www.theicehouse.co.nz/blog/changing-lives-inside-and-out", "https://www.uniservices.co.nz/news/greg-ogrady-from-surgeon-to-ceo", "https://www.cie.auckland.ac.nz/newsroom/duncan-cunninghame-taking-new-zealand-medtech-global/", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/about-us/sir-paul-callaghan-100-report/all-companies/the-insides-company/", "https://www.theinsides.co/news/ticl-announces-fpi-milestone-for-reinfuse", "https://www.theinsides.co/news/ticl-ceo-garth-sutherland-annouced-as-top-50-healthcare-tech-ceo", "https://www.snowballeffect.co.nz/offers/show/insides-company-series-a-tmpcl", "https://tin100.com/directory/the-insides-company/"], "website": "https://www.theinsides.co", "industry": "Medical Devices / Medtech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirmed the draft on all material points: the five named individuals (four scientific/clinical co-founders + CEO Garth Sutherland), active private status, Auckland HQ, 2017 founding from Surgical Design Studio, FDA Breakthrough Device designation, and Icehouse Ventures leading the NZ$4.3m August 2019 round (theicehouse.co.nz). Minor corrections: (1) softened the FDA designation year, as sources cite 2018 vs 2019 inconsistently; (2) updated the statusDetail because the REINFUSE study appears to have reached primary completion around November 2025, so it is no longer clearly \\"ongoing.\\" Could not independently confirm LinkedIn URLs for the four scientific founders (left null) or the precise ~NZ$10m total-funding figure (kept as approximate, secondary).", "statusDetail": "Private, operating; The Insides System commercially available in UK, Europe, Australia and NZ, with US FDA Breakthrough Device designation. The pivotal US/UK REINFUSE clinical study reached its primary completion around November 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~NZ$4.3m early-stage round in August 2019 led by Icehouse Ventures, with K1W1 (Sir Stephen Tindall), UniServices, Eden Ventures and the NZ Venture Investment Fund; later ran a Series A on Snowball Effect (Q1 2023). Secondary reporting indicates roughly NZ$10m raised in total (not precisely confirmed).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
