ZZUVF5OLV4BU/", "https://www.nzgcp.co.nz/portfolio/case-study/narrative", "https://matchstiq.io/conversations-nz-tech-leaders/james-broadbent-narrative-ceo/", "https://matchstiq.io/stories/steffan-levet-co-founder-and-co-head-of-engineering-at-narrative", "https://www.stuff.co.nz/business/122255276/peter-thielbacked-photographic-tech-startup-raises-4m-adding-17-staff", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/narrative/__A7Sgv7MNpoNcBsywTCYHF0ocEVgFKpqMiYE_HLD0nLs", "https://www.trysignalbase.com/news/funding/narrative-raises-85m-series-a-funding", "https://techcrunch.com/2020/08/27/narrative-series-a/", "https://newzealand.ai/insights/narrative-ai-auckland"], "website": "https://narrative.so", "industry": "Software (AI / Photography SaaS)", "confidence": "medium", "verifyNote": "Founders, founding year (2017), Auckland HQ, product, active status, and Icehouse Ventures backing all independently confirmed. Corrections: (1) seed round was US$2.58M (≈NZ$4M), not \\"US$4M\\" — the draft conflated the USD and NZD figures into one inflated number; (2) the $8.5M Series A is single-sourced (Signalbase, with a wrong 2018 founding year) and very likely conflated with an unrelated US company (narrative.io's $8.5M Series A led by G20 Ventures), so stage downgraded from \\"Series A\\" to the last well-documented round, \\"Seed\\"; (3) Steffan Levet's title firmed to \\"Co-Founder, Co-CEO & Co-Head of Engineering\\" per Matchstiq; (4) confidence lowered from high to medium due to these issues. NZ Growth Capital Partners' specific round participation is not confirmed in primary seed coverage (only a portfolio case-study page), so phrasing was softened.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating; raised a ~US$2.58M (≈NZ$4M) Founders Fund-led seed in July 2020. A reported ~$8.5M Series A (circa March 2026) is from a single aggregator and is likely a confusion with an unrelated same-named US data-marketplace company.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "~2019 angel round (~NZ$700k)