org:iv-datch	organization	Datch	Voice and AI assistant for industrial frontline workers to capture data and diagnose assets hands-free.	New York, USA (R&D in Auckland & Christchurch, New Zealand)	https://www.datch.io	{"Voice AI","Industrial software","Enterprise asset management","B2B SaaS","Frontline workforce","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Datch builds an AI-powered voice and visual interface for industrial operations, letting frontline workers in manufacturing, energy, utilities and transportation log work, access manuals and diagnose equipment hands-free. Founded in the UK in 2018 by Australian Mark Fosdike and New Zealanders Aric Thorn and Ben Purcell, the now US-based company integrates with enterprise asset management systems and has expanded into AI-driven asset insights. It has raised roughly US$28.7M and maintains New Zealand engineering offices in Auckland and Christchurch alongside US offices in New York and San Francisco.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is Datch / Datch Systems / Datch Inc, the industrial voice-and-visual AI startup (NZ roots, US HQ) — not any same-named foreign company. All three founders confirmed on the company's own About page (Fosdike CEO, Purcell CTO, Thorn CPO) and cross-sourced. Founding year: formal/Icehouse profile and seed press releases say \\"formed in the UK in 2018\\"; several founder interviews (Blackhorn, Voicebot) say Fosdike co-founded it in 2017 — 2018 retained as the more authoritative/consistent figure. Ben Purcell's precise prior roles are the least firmly sourced detail (interviews reference energy-sector engineering across NZ/UK/Germany); phrasing softened accordingly.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://www.datch.io/about", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/datch", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/datch-secures-3-2-million-for-their-industrial-voice-visual-ai-platform-301064767.html", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20220726005355/en/Datch-Raises-$10-Million-in-Series-A-Funding-Led-by-Blackhorn-Ventures", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20240807738419/en/Datch-Closes-$15M-Series-A", "https://www.finsmes.com/2020/05/datch-secures-3-2m-in-funding.html", "https://www.cbinsights.com/investor/tuhua-ventures", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icehouse_Ventures", "https://set.adelaide.edu.au/news/list/2020/06/02/aerospace-alumni-secures-32m-for-industrial-ai-platform", "https://theorg.com/org/datch/org-chart/aric-thorn", "https://www.blackhornvc.com/news-and-posts/solving-the-input-problem-mark-fosdike---cofounder-and-ceo-of-datch-on-building-ai-solutions-that-transform-industrial-frontline-work", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/datchtechnologies/__9u0kf4Idk-yJBigyq3F64ZCDFiGKPA64dD_uAo6q0_k"], "website": "https://www.datch.io", "industry": "Industrial / Enterprise Voice AI software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed all three founders, names and roles via Datch's own About page plus The Org, Crunchbase, Blackhorn, Adelaide and Te Ohaka coverage. Status confirmed active in 2026 (~34 employees) per Tracxn/PitchBook/Crunchbase. Funding confirmed: ~US$28.7M total, US$3.2M seed (May 2020, Blue Bear Capital lead, Tuhua Ventures participating), US$10M Series A (July 2022, Blackhorn lead), US$15M Series A extension (Aug 2024, Third Prime lead). Icehouse backing DOWNGRADED from 'confirmed' to 'likely': the link is indirect — Datch appears on the Icehouse Ventures jobs board and its 2020 seed included Tuhua Ventures (the NZ fund affiliated with The Icehouse/Ice Angels, now part of the Icehouse Ventures group). No source explicitly names 'Icehouse Ventures' as a direct cheque-writer. Minor refinements: softened Ben Purcell's prior-background wording (control-systems claim not independently sourced; energy-sector background is), and added Susquehanna/SIG as a 2024 backer.", "statusDetail": "Active in 2026 (~34 employees); closed a US$15M Series A extension led by Third Prime in August 2024, coinciding with the launch of its Asset Insights product, and continues operating across the US, NZ and Europe.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "~US$28.7M total raised. Seed US$3.2M (May 2020, led by Blue Bear Capital, incl. NZ fund Tuhua Ventures); Series A US$10M (July 2022, led by Blackhorn Ventures); Series A extension to US$15M (Aug 2024, led by Third Prime). Other backers include Boeing, Stage Venture Partners, Lorimer Ventures, Predictive Venture Partners, Plug and Play, and Susquehanna (SIG).", "icehouseBacked": "likely"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-groov	organization	Groov	NZ mental wellbeing platform (formerly Mentemia), co-founded by Sir John Kirwan	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.groovnow.com	{"mental health","workplace wellbeing","digital health",HealthTech,AI,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Groov is a New Zealand digital mental wellbeing company founded in 2018 as Mentemia and rebranded to Groov in March 2022. It was co-founded by former All Black and mental health advocate Sir John Kirwan and tech entrepreneur Adam Clark, offering a consumer wellbeing app alongside paid workplace wellbeing programmes for corporate clients. The company has since evolved toward science-based products including Groov Health (a care platform extending patient support between clinical appointments) and PerformanceCare (an organisational/workforce intelligence platform). Matt Krogstad is the current CEO; Kirwan and Clark remain co-founders on the board.", "notes": "Not to be confused with US retailer Grove Collaborative or same-named \\"Groove\\" software products. Founding year is reported as 2018 by BusinessDesk and the company itself, though some Series A materials cite 2019 for co-founding/launch. Current CEO per the team page is Matt Krogstad; Adam Clark was the founding CEO and remains a co-founder/board member. Aaron Tregaskis is listed as a board member (not a founder). Series A amount not publicly disclosed. Adam Clark's LinkedIn URL not confirmed, left null.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/technology/ongoing-govt-funding-for-john-kirwans-mental-health-platform", "https://www.groovnow.com/blog/mentemia-series-a-funding-announcement", "https://www.groovnow.com/blog/move-to-groov", "https://www.groovnow.com/team", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/acc-kiwisaver-provider-invest-in-sir-john-kirwans-mental-health-app-mentemia/XHLHWISGEPUTHQ54ZA7EVSGLSQ/", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20110228007299/en/Fiserv-Acquires-M-Com-Enhance-Mobile-Banking-Payments", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/PA2203/S00180/new-digital-tools-ramp-up-mental-wellbeing-support.htm"], "website": "https://www.groovnow.com", "industry": "Digital health / mental wellbeing software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirmed all major claims: co-founders Sir John Kirwan and Adam Clark (Clark's M-Com/Fiserv-2011 background verified via Businesswire/Fiserv); 2018 founding (BusinessDesk); March 2022 rebrand from Mentemia; May 2021 Series A led by ACC Impact Fund with Icehouse Ventures (6.5%), Pathfinder and K1W1; Icehouse backing CONFIRMED; cap table matches BusinessDesk; status active with Groov Health/PerformanceCare evolution; current CEO Matt Krogstad confirmed on team page. Minor correction: removed unverified \\"Board Chair\\" title for Kirwan (team page lists him only as Co-founder; Aaron Tregaskis is the named board member). All else stood; confidence high.", "statusDetail": "Active. Has evolved from a consumer/workplace wellbeing app into products including Groov Health (for healthcare providers) and PerformanceCare (for enterprises). No acquisition or closure found.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised a Series A in May 2021 led by ACC's Impact Fund, with Pathfinder KiwiSaver, Icehouse Ventures and Sir Stephen Tindall's K One W One (K1W1) participating. Per BusinessDesk's cap-table reporting: Kirwan (with wife Fiorella) ~27.6% and Adam Clark's trustee company (Sheaf) ~27.6%, ACC Impact Fund ~11.5%, Icehouse Ventures 6.5%, Pathfinder ~3.2% (NZ$800k), K1W1 3%. ACC investment undisclosed but within the Impact Fund's NZ$2m-$15m band. Also received NZ Ministry of Health (COVID-19 response) funding to keep the consumer app free.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-inhibit-coatings	organization	Inhibit Coatings Limited	NZ deep-tech making bound-silver-nanoparticle antimicrobial paints and coatings for food, health and high-touch surfaces	Wellington, New Zealand	https://inhibitcoatings.com/	{"antimicrobial coatings",nanotechnology,"advanced materials","deep tech","food safety","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Inhibit Coatings is a Wellington, New Zealand advanced-materials company founded in November 2016 to commercialise antimicrobial coating technology developed at Victoria University of Wellington. Its proprietary \\"smart chemistry\\" permanently binds silver nanoparticles into polymer-based coatings, giving low-leaching, long-lifetime antimicrobial and antiviral surfaces reported to kill over 650 microorganisms (including Listeria, E. coli and S. aureus). Applications span food processing, healthcare/aged care, flooring and plastics. The company has raised funding from NZ angel and venture investors and won a 2020 KiwiNet research-commercialisation award.", "notes": "Entity is INHIBIT COATINGS LIMITED, Wellington NZ (NZBN 9429045842740 per draft; not independently re-verified this run). Founding details confirmed by NZ Product Accelerator, which states the company was founded in November 2016 by Prof Jim Johnston, Dr Eldon Tate and industry colleagues Hayden Nicholson, Lorne Crowley and Andy Taylor (The Polymer Group, Auckland), with Jim and Hayden as Founding Directors and Eldon as Founding CEO. The company's current team page lists only Dr Eldon Tate as \\"CEO and Founder\\" (plus non-founder staff/board: Dr Emma Wrigglesworth, Stephen Fitzer, Dr Peter Lee, Nina Le Lievre). LinkedIn URLs for co-founders other than Eldon Tate were not found (null); Eldon Tate's LinkedIn URL is carried from the draft and not independently re-verified this run. Not to be confused with similarly named foreign coatings firms.", "stage": "Seed / early-stage angel", "status": "active", "founded": "2016", "sources": ["https://inhibitcoatings.com/", "https://inhibitcoatings.com/our-team/", "https://www.nzproductaccelerator.co.nz/2021/06/18/inhibit-coatings-a-rapid-journey-from-phd-to-start-up-company/", "https://www.booster.co.nz/blog/investing/spotlight-series-inhibit-coatings", "https://kiwinet.org.nz/Awards/Awards2020", "https://www.wgtn.ac.nz/news/2021/12/research-commercialisation-success-brings-new-zealand-innovation-to-the-world", "https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/portfolio", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/175791-07", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/inhibit-coatings", "https://matu.co.nz/portfolio/inhibit-coatings/", "https://www.enterpriseangels.co.nz/project/inhibit-coatings/", "https://www.iponz.govt.nz/case-studies/inhibit-coatings/"], "website": "https://inhibitcoatings.com/", "industry": "Advanced materials / antimicrobial coatings (deep tech)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Draft was substantially correct. Independently confirmed: five 2016 co-founders (Tate, Johnston, Nicholson, Crowley, Taylor) via NZ Product Accelerator; current team page lists only Tate as CEO/Founder; Tate's 2020 KiwiNet Norman Barry Foundation Breakthrough Innovator Award verified verbatim on kiwinet.org.nz; silver-nanoparticle antimicrobial coatings (650+ microorganisms) and food/health applications; active status; ~NZ$2.5M funding with $1.5M scale-up round, $200k NZIB and $350k MBIE COVID grant. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via the Icehouse portfolio listing and a PitchBook/Tracxn institutional-investor summary explicitly naming Icehouse Ventures. Corrections: clarified Johnston and Nicholson are \\"Founding Directors\\" (not generic \\"industry\\") and refined oneLiner to \\"bound\\" silver nanoparticles. Could not confirm the exact Icehouse round/amount/date, nor LinkedIn URLs for co-founders (left null); Eldon Tate's LinkedIn was carried over unverified.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating as of 2025: website live, team page lists CEO/founder plus technical, operations and board members, ongoing R&D and commercialisation; no acquisition or closure reported.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Reported ~NZ$2.5M raised across multiple rounds, including a ~NZ$1.5M raise to scale to commercial-size batches. Investors named across sources include Matū, Enterprise Angels, Angel HQ, Aspire NZ Seed Fund, New Zealand Growth Capital Partners, Powerhouse Ventures, Plug and Play and Icehouse Ventures. Grants include ~NZ$350k from MBIE's COVID-19 Innovation Accelerator Fund and ~NZ$200k from NZ Innovation Booster (NZIB). Exact totals and round structure are not authoritatively confirmed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-joyous	organization	Joyous	AI-powered conversational workforce feedback platform - "the Anti-Survey"	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.bejoyous.ai	{"HR tech","employee feedback",AI,"enterprise SaaS","conversational analytics","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Joyous is an Auckland, New Zealand SaaS company founded in 2017 by brothers Mike and Philip Carden that provides an AI-powered conversational feedback platform for large enterprises, positioning itself as \\"the Anti-Survey\\" alternative to traditional anonymous surveys. The platform lets organizations chat one-on-one with workers at scale, analyzes responses for actionable insights, and generates prioritized action plans. Named customers include large global organizations such as AT&T, KFC, Nokia, Taco Bell and Vodafone. The product was originally at joyoushq.com and now operates under the bejoyous.ai domain with a generative-AI focus.", "notes": "New Zealand HR-tech / employee-feedback SaaS founded by brothers Mike and Philip Carden in Auckland (Feb 2017); not to be confused with same-named foreign products. Website migrated from joyoushq.com to bejoyous.ai (now AI/generative-AI focused, \\"the Anti-Survey\\"). Icehouse Ventures backing is confirmed across multiple sources: a returning investor in the Sept 2021 NZ$15m Series A (led by Square Peg, with AirTree), held a ~10% stake after the 2019 round, and was an early/seed backer. Stage is most reliably documented as Series A (Sept 2021); no later priced round confirmed. The 2019 round is reported as NZ$4m by the NZ Herald.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/kiwi-hr-feedback-startup-joyous-raises-14-million/", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/airtree-ventures-backs-new-zealand-hr-startup-joyous/", "https://itwire.com/it-industry-news/market/nz-startup-joyous-raises-nz$15-million.html", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/joyous-raises-15m-and-breaks-with-the-pack-on-tech-skills-crisis/UKNLQVNYIPFNKXCTDLNLOFFQ5A/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/software-for-listening-to-your-workers-startup-raises-4m/GC6SM67KNY4NKSXNKCQI66KWHI/", "https://www.bejoyous.ai/", "https://www.bejoyous.ai/pages/ruby-kolesky-chief-executive-officer", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/ruby-kolesky", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/pcarden/", "https://medium.com/airtree-venture/10-lessons-with-a-serial-entrepreneur-mike-carden-the-co-founder-of-joyous-f219298fbb00", "https://www.nzgcp.co.nz/about-us/news-and-media/resources/korerorero-mike-carden-joyous"], "website": "https://www.bejoyous.ai", "industry": "HR Tech / Employee Feedback SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Company, founders (Mike and Philip Carden, 2017), Icehouse Ventures backing, the Sept 2021 NZ$15m Series A (Square Peg/AirTree/Icehouse), Ruby Kolesky's 31 May 2024 CEO appointment, the Carden role transitions, the bejoyous.ai \\"Anti-Survey\\" positioning, and the customer list (AT&T, KFC, Nokia, Taco Bell, Vodafone) were all independently confirmed. Corrections: Ruby Kolesky joined Joyous in 2020 (not ~2021) and was Chief Product Officer; her prior background is leadership at Vista Group and AskNicely per the official appointment page (draft's \\"Director of Product and Design at AskNicely\\" softened). The 2019 round is NZ$4m per NZ Herald (not NZ$3.8m), and \\"Tuhua Ventures\\" as a 2019 backer could not be confirmed in sources reviewed, so it was dropped (Sam Morgan confirmed). Removed unconfirmed Sydney/Frisco office detail from statusDetail. Mike Carden's canonical LinkedIn URL could not be verified, so it is null.", "statusDetail": "Active and independent, headquartered in Auckland. Co-founder Ruby Kolesky was appointed sole CEO on 31 May 2024, ending the prior \\"Collective CEO\\" model; co-founders Mike and Philip Carden moved to Chief Revenue Officer and Executive Director of Strategic Accounts respectively, both remaining executive directors on the board.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised NZ$15m (A$14.2m) Series A in September 2021, led by Australian VC Square Peg Capital, with returning investors AirTree Ventures and Icehouse Ventures (described as their third round backing Joyous; post-round Square Peg ~12%, AirTree ~18%, Icehouse ~12%). An earlier 2019 round raised NZ$4m (NZ Herald), with backers including Sam Morgan and Icehouse Ventures (~10%). Icehouse was also a seed investor.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-dexibit	organization	Dexibit	Big data and AI analytics for visitor attractions, museums and galleries	Auckland, New Zealand	https://dexibit.com	{"data analytics","artificial intelligence",SaaS,"visitor attractions",museums,"Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "Dexibit is an Auckland, New Zealand software company providing big data analytics and AI for visitor attractions such as museums, galleries, theme parks and stadiums. Its SaaS platform connects venue operating systems and external data to forecast and analyse visitor behaviour through dashboards, automated reporting and insights. Customers include leading cultural institutions such as the Smithsonian American Art Museum and London's National Gallery, with offices in Auckland, London and Washington DC. In late March 2026 Dexibit was acquired by UK-listed accesso Technology Group for NZ$20.9m (about US$12.1m).", "notes": "This is the Auckland, NZ company (Dexibit Limited), not any same-named foreign entity. Founders Angie Judge (CEO) and Justin Kearney (COO), a married couple, are consistently named co-founders across the company About page, NZ Entrepreneur Q&A and acquisition coverage. Ravi Chandra is Chief Product & Technology Officer in leadership but is not consistently sourced as a co-founder, so he is omitted. Founding year reported variously as 2014-2016; the Icehouse Ventures listing says 2015, used here (medium confidence on exact year). Justin Kearney's prior background and exact shareholding/career-break details could not be independently confirmed and were dropped/softened. MoMA as a customer could not be independently confirmed; Smithsonian and London's National Gallery are confirmed.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2015", "sources": ["https://dexibit.com/about/", "https://nzentrepreneur.co.nz/founder-qa-dexibit/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/dexibit", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/rules-of-attraction-aucklands-ai-savvy-dexibit-sells-to-uk-listed-firm-for-21m/premium/6PXABKWIVJHP3MBYJMLI5536GA/", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/news-in-brief/aucklands-ai-savvy-dexibit-sells-to-uk-listed-firm-for-21m", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/accesso-acquires-dexibit-establishing-the-first-cross-platform-ai-and-analytics-platform-for-visitor-attractions-302728047.html", "https://www.museumnext.com/article/national-gallery-predicts-future-artificial-intelligence/", "https://www.marketscreener.com/news/accesso-technology-group-plc-acquired-dexibit-limited-for-nzd-20-9-million-ce7e51d9db8ff32c"], "website": "https://dexibit.com", "industry": "Data analytics / SaaS for visitor attractions", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Core facts confirmed by fresh searches: company identity, Auckland HQ, museum/visitor-attraction analytics product, both co-founders (Angie Judge CEO, Justin Kearney COO), acquired status, and Icehouse Ventures backing (Robbie Paul: ~NZ$1.8m over 2016/2018/2019, 22% stake). Corrections: refined deal terms to the more precise NZD split (NZ$12.2m upfront + up to NZ$8.7m deferred over three years) rather than the draft's USD estimate; removed Justin Kearney's unverifiable prior-background and career-break claims; softened the MoMA customer claim (Smithsonian and National Gallery London confirmed, MoMA not independently sourced). Acquisition completion date varies by source (March 28 vs March 30, 2026); founding year (2014 vs 2015) remains uncertain.", "statusDetail": "Acquired by UK-listed accesso Technology Group, completing late March 2026, for NZ$20.9m (about US$12.1m); structured as ~NZ$12.2m upfront cash plus up to ~NZ$8.7m in deferred/performance consideration over three years.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Icehouse Ventures invested ~NZ$1.8m across rounds in 2016, 2018 and 2019 (including Seed Fund 2) and held a 22% stake at acquisition, its second-largest shareholder after CEO Angie Judge (~25%). Other backers reported include Lightning Lab, NZ Growth Capital Partners and Rampersand.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-avertana	organization	Avertana	NZ cleantech refining steelmaking slag into titanium dioxide and other raw materials	Auckland, New Zealand	https://avertana.com	{cleantech,"circular economy","materials extraction","titanium dioxide","industrial waste","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Avertana is a New Zealand process-technology company that has developed a proprietary, patented pathway to refine industrial waste (notably steelmaking slag) into valuable mineral and chemical raw materials such as titanium dioxide, gypsum, alum and magnesium sulphate. These outputs feed everyday products including paints, plastics, building materials, fertilisers and water-treatment chemicals, with the process claimed to produce no residual waste and substantially lower CO2 emissions than legacy mining-based methods. The company built a pre-commercial demonstration plant in Auckland and aims to license and scale its technology with global steel-industry partners. It signed its first commercial deal with Chinese steelmaker Tranvic Group and was a recipient of Callaghan Innovation's inaugural Ārohia Innovation Trailblazer grant.", "notes": "This is the Auckland, New Zealand cleantech firm (not a same-named foreign company). Founding year nuance: the concept/team originated ~2012 at LanzaTech, with the company launched/incorporated ~2014 (used as foundedYear); some aggregators date its Series A to 2016. The three co-founders (Obern, Molloy, Ibrahim) are independently confirmed and were all ex-LanzaTech colleagues. Dr Sean Simpson (LanzaTech co-founder) appears in some listings but is Avertana's inaugural Independent Director, NOT a founder, so he is excluded. Current CEO is Michael Oliver; Molloy moved to Founding Director ~2020. LinkedIn for Molloy and Ibrahim could not be unambiguously matched, so left null. Funding figure is uncertain: aggregators say ~NZ$15.6M while a founder bio cites \\"over $30M\\".", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2014", "sources": ["https://avertana.com/", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/stories/avertana-turning-a-what-if-moment-into-a-world-first-in-extraction-technology/", "https://avertana.com/tech-startup-avertanas-first-commercial-deal-is-with-chinese-steelmaker/", "https://nip.auckland.ac.nz/project/avertana/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/jamesobern", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/james-obern", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/alumni/our-alumni/40-under-40/a-z-list-of-profiles/sean-molloy.html", "https://meaningful.business/team/sean-molloy/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/avertana", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/167994-01", "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/avertana", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/stories/first-arohia-innovation-trailblazer-grant-recipients/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/avertana"], "website": "https://avertana.com", "industry": "Cleantech / advanced materials", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders (Obern VP Commercial, Molloy former CEO/Founding Director, Ibrahim Technical Director), ex-LanzaTech origin, Icehouse Ventures backing, the Tranvic deal, and the Ārohia Trailblazer grant were all independently confirmed. Corrections vs draft: clarified current CEO is Michael Oliver (draft omitted this and implied CEO unknown); flagged that the ~NZ$15.6M figure is dated (a founder bio cites over $30M); tightened the description (no residual waste / lower CO2). Sherif Ibrahim and Sean Molloy LinkedIn URLs remain unconfirmed (null); exact founding year (2012 conception vs 2014 launch vs 2016 Series A) and precise total funding could not be definitively pinned, hence partly-confirmed rather than fully confirmed.", "statusDetail": "Active; built a pre-commercial demonstration plant in Auckland and seeking global partners to scale to industrial scale. Current CEO is Michael Oliver (co-founder Sean Molloy stepped back from CEO around 2020).", "verifyVerdict": "partly-confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Reported total raised ranges from ~NZ$15.6M (PitchBook/Tracxn) to \\"over $30M\\" (a 2023-era founder bio); aggregator figures appear dated. Investors include Icehouse Ventures, K1W1, the direct-investment arm of ACC, ICE Angels, Outset Ventures, Pacific Channel, GRC SinoGreen and others (aggregators list ~23 investors). Recipient of Callaghan Innovation's inaugural Ārohia Innovation Trailblazer grant (2024).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-fuel50	organization	Fuel50	AI-powered talent marketplace and skills intelligence platform for internal mobility	Auckland, New Zealand (with US office, Laguna Niguel, California)	https://fuel50.com	{"talent marketplace","skills intelligence","internal mobility","HR tech","AI SaaS","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Fuel50 is a New Zealand-founded SaaS company providing an AI-powered talent marketplace and skills intelligence platform that drives internal talent mobility, workforce reskilling, and employee retention for large enterprises. It was founded by Anne Fulton (Founder & CEO) and Jo Mills (co-founder), with the company's own materials stating the business was conceived in 2013. Headquartered with operations in Auckland, New Zealand and the United States (Laguna Niguel, California), it serves global enterprise customers and has raised more than US$36M, including a US$15.5M Series B in April 2021 led by PeakSpan Capital and Shearwater Capital. The company remains active, launching a Skills Intelligence product in October 2025.", "notes": "This is the New Zealand-founded HR-tech talent-marketplace company Fuel50 (fuel50.com), not any same-named fuel/energy business. Founding-year nuance: Fuel50's own October 2023 press release states the business was 'conceived in 2013'; several third-party profiles cite 2011 as a conception/founding date, so the exact origin year is ambiguous. The draft's claim that Anne Fulton was previously at 'Talent Technologies' and based in 'Manhattan Beach, California' could not be independently confirmed and was removed/nulled. One search snippet erroneously named 'Lisa Miles-Heal' as a co-founder; this is not supported by Fuel50's own materials and was excluded.", "stage": "Series B", "status": "active", "founded": "2013", "sources": ["https://fuel50.com/company/", "https://fuel50.com/2023/10/announcing-fuel50s-new-president-chief-revenue-officer/", "https://fuel50.com/2025/10/fuel50-launches-skills-intelligence/", "https://www.achieveengagement.org/bio/anne-fulton", "https://www.unleash.ai/unleashamerica/contributors/anne-fulton/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/fuel50", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/fuel50/__mqbpMUP1nc8dF6o2IFzZqvHsRmEV9ZXgy0J3Na1P1Pc/funding-and-investors", "https://app.dealroom.co/companies/fuel50", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/fuel50", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/annefultonfuel50", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jomillsnz/", "https://whatfounderswant.com/expert-editions/how-to-get-a-startup-off-the-ground-in-nz/new-zealand-start-a-startup-wiki/fuel50"], "website": "https://fuel50.com", "industry": "HR Technology / SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Confirmed founders Anne Fulton (Founder & CEO) and Jo Mills (co-founder, CXO, promoted to President Oct 2023); active status; Series B and US$36M+ funding. Corrections: removed unconfirmed claims that Anne Fulton was at 'Talent Technologies' and based in Manhattan Beach (set location null); added confirmed background for both founders; softened the 2011-vs-2013 founding nuance (Fuel50's own materials say 'conceived in 2013'). Icehouse Ventures backing downgraded from 'confirmed' to 'likely': it appears in third-party investor lists (Tracxn/Dealroom) and the 2013 seed was led by Ice Angels (the angel network run by The Icehouse), but I found no direct Icehouse Ventures portfolio confirmation on icehouseventures.co.nz.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating globally. Latest disclosed raise was a US$15.5M Series B in April 2021 led by PeakSpan Capital and Shearwater Capital; launched a Skills Intelligence product in October 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised US$36M+ across multiple rounds; early angel/seed funding (Ice Angels, Auckland, 2013), Series A backers including Bonfire Ventures and Rincon Venture Partners, and a US$15.5M Series B in April 2021 led by PeakSpan Capital and Shearwater Capital. Icehouse Ventures appears in third-party investor lists.", "icehouseBacked": "likely"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-foundry-lab	organization	Foundry Lab	Digital Metal Casting: production-grade metal parts cast on-demand from CAD, no tooling, in under a day	Austin, USA (global HQ); R&D HQ: Petone, Lower Hutt, Wellington, New Zealand	https://www.foundrylab.com	{"metal casting","advanced manufacturing","deep tech","additive manufacturing",defense,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Foundry Lab is a New Zealand-born deep-tech manufacturing company that developed Digital Metal Casting (DMC), a tooling-free process using microwave-based melting to cast fully dense, production-grade metal parts directly from digital files, often within hours. Founded in 2018 in Wellington by industrial designer David Moodie, it emerged from stealth in November 2021 with a US$8M Series A led by Blackbird. It targets defense, aerospace and automotive customers across alloys including aluminium, zinc, brass and stainless steel. In November 2024 it announced its first commercial sale, supplying a DMC-3 system to the New Jersey Innovation Institute under a US Army DEVCOM Armaments Center (COMET) initiative.", "notes": "Not to be confused with same-named foreign companies (e.g. AI/cloud \\"Foundry\\", or US semiconductor foundries). This is the NZ-origin microwave metal-casting deep-tech firm. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via multiple independent funding announcements (NZ Herald, PR Newswire, Startup Daily, FinSMEs) and Foundry Lab's listing on the Icehouse Ventures job board. The Icehouse job board lists a US office in Fremont, CA, while the company's own site lists the US global HQ as Austin, TX (current). Series B: Callaghan Innovation reports the company was preparing a Series B with ~US$14M raised to date; aggregators may list a 2025 round, but exact amount/lead/close is unconfirmed by primary or news sources, so treated cautiously. David Moodie's LinkedIn URL is taken from consistent search-result attribution (the page blocks automated fetch).", "stage": "Series A (US$8M, Nov 2021); Series B