TAKYUKRER4Q7XAUKINBQ/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/carbon-footprint-tracking-fintech-cogo-lines-up-35m-raise-as-cop26-looms/AFQNL4J4XJ2IELDTTTZ6U4XZEM/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/cogo/__OzJHbKpOwvEez9tj1IflCMSxuC3inKKvUZ-ZReEbNBM", "https://thespinoff.co.nz/business/23-12-2017/the-rise-of-conscious-and-convenient-consumerism", "https://kindrik.co.nz/case-studies/conscious-consumers/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/cogo-connecting-good"], "website": "https://www.cogo.co/", "industry": "Climate Technology / Fintech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Added co-founder Melissa Keys, who was wrongly omitted from the draft (independently sourced as co-founder of the Conscious Consumers venture that became Cogo, ~2009; departed around the 2016 rebrand). Ben Gleisner (Founder & CEO, ex-Treasury economist) is confirmed via Cogo's own site and NZ Herald. Icehouse Ventures backing is confirmed: NZ Herald names Icehouse Ventures (with K1W1 and NZGCP) as an investor in the ~$8m seed, and Icehouse lists Cogo via its Soul Capital fund. Active status, 2016-founded-from-Conscious-Consumers history, Wellington HQ, and bank partnerships all confirmed. Removed Ben Gleisner's LinkedIn URL (set null): the draft slug /in/ben-gleisner could not be verified and search surfaced a different handle (/in/ben-gleisner-78b56652), so no LinkedIn asserted. Softened funding wording: the \\"$35m\\"/Series A figures were a target/raise-in-progress, not a confirmed closed amount.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating; per Tracxn (2026) ~55 employees, with clients across multiple countries (NatWest, ING, Westpac, Suncorp, Bank of China HK, Kiwibank). Most recent reported activity includes a 2023 funding round.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised an $8m seed round (reported 2020-2021) from investors including Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1, Icehouse Ventures and Crown-backed NZ Growth Capital Partners (NZGCP); total funding reported by Tracxn at ~US$34.3M across