org:iv-nanolayr	organization	Nanolayr	NZ deep-tech nanofibre manufacturer (formerly Revolution Fibres) using electrospinning	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.nanolayr.com	{nanofibre,"advanced materials","deep tech",electrospinning,manufacturing,"Icehouse Portfolio",Closed}	\N	{"bio": "Nanolayr is an Auckland, New Zealand advanced-materials manufacturer that produces high-performance nanofibre textiles at industrial scale using an electrospinning process at its Mangere Bridge plant. Founded in 2009 as Revolution Fibres and rebranded to Nanolayr in May 2021, its product platforms spanned filtration (FilterLayr, including N95/N99 mask media), acoustic insulation (SonoLayr), composite reinforcement (XantuLayr) and bioactive skincare/collagen (DermaLayr/ActivLayr). The company was placed into voluntary administration in October 2025 after being unable to secure sufficient investment to reach profitable commercial revenue scale.", "notes": "Disambiguation: This is the New Zealand nanofibre manufacturer, formerly Revolution Fibres (rebranded May 2021), HQ in Mangere Bridge/Auckland — not the unrelated NanoLayr UK Ltd. Founders Iain Hosie, Simon Feasey and Michael Perrett are consistently corroborated across NZ sources (innovationintextiles, Science Learning Hub, NZ Herald, Tracxn); Perrett is the founder of HRV, which was the company's first customer. Aggregator-only names 'Simon G King' and 'Vlad Stolojan' are excluded — King appears as a later CEO, not a founder, and Stolojan is uncorroborated. Ray Connor was CEO through the COVID-era growth and rebrand. LinkedIn URLs for Feasey and Perrett were not confidently verified, so left null.", "stage": "Venture-backed (private); Series A", "status": "closed", "founded": "2009", "sources": ["https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/574769/textile-firm-nanolayr-placed-in-voluntary-administration", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/auckland-nanofibre-firm-nanolayr-enters-voluntary-administration-process/ARXBXTCAAJC2XGGE5VEK555NYE/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/administrators-get-multiple-offers-for-nanotech-company-nanolayr/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/nanotechnology-company-nanolayr-put-into-voluntary-administration/", "https://www.compositesworld.com/news/revolution-fibres-rebrands-to-nanolayr", "https://innovationintextiles.com/kiwi-nanofibre-producer-raises-6m-in-funding/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/nanolayr", "https://www.movac.co.nz/general/movac-invests-in-revolution-fibres-to-scale-global-growth/", "https://www.sciencelearn.org.nz/resources/1674-producing-commercial-quantities-of-nanofibre", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/iain-hosie-8a82b612/"], "website": "https://www.nanolayr.com", "industry": "Advanced materials / nanotechnology manufacturing", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirmed the draft's core claims: 2009 founding as Revolution Fibres, May 2021 rebrand, Auckland/Mangere Bridge HQ, electrospinning nanofibre tech and product lines, the three founders (Hosie, Feasey, Perrett with HRV link), Icehouse Ventures backing (alongside Movac, K1W1, Ngai Tahu), the ~NZ$6m raise, and the October 2025 voluntary administration (Grant Thornton; Keen and Moore) with a sale still in process as of 11 Nov 2025. Minor corrections: removed 'sonic' qualifier from electrospinning (sources say 'electrospinning'); corrected Iain Hosie's LinkedIn from the uk.linkedin.com variant to the canonical global linkedin.com URL; refined stage to note Series A. Could not load the company's own team page (TLS error) but role/bio facts are independently corroborated.", "statusDetail": "Placed into voluntary administration in October 2025 (Grant Thornton NZ; administrators Stephen Keen and Russell Moore). As of 11 November 2025 the administrators reported receiving multiple offers and expected to conclude a sale shortly, but no completed sale or new owner was confirmed in available sources.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Backed by Movac, Icehouse Ventures, Sir Stephen Tindall's K1W1, and Ngai Tahu. Raised ~NZ$6m in a Movac-led round (reported March 2020).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-preno	organization	Preno	Cloud hotel management software (PMS, channel manager, booking engine) for independent accommodation providers	Auckland, New Zealand	https://prenohq.com	{"Hotel Software",PMS,SaaS,"Property Management","Travel Tech","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Preno is a New Zealand cloud-based hotel management software company serving boutique hotels, motels, and lodges. Its platform combines a property management system (PMS), channel manager connecting to OTAs such as Booking.com, Expedia, and Airbnb, and a direct booking engine, with two-way accounting integrations to Xero and MYOB. Co-founded by Amelia Gain (CEO) and Max Podolian (CTO), the product launched to market in late 2015 and is used by independent hoteliers across more than 20 countries. The company remains active and privately held, headquartered in Auckland with a London presence.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the NZ hotel-software Preno (prenohq.com), not any same-named foreign entity. Founding-year ambiguity persists: Icehouse Ventures' job board and Crunchbase cite 2014 (used here), while Preno's marketing and multiple media pieces say the product launched in late 2015 — both reconciled in the description (Gain sold her hotel in 2014, began building Preno, launched late 2015). HQ is Auckland (Icehouse, PitchBook) with a London presence; some directories (Gust) list a Christchurch address, consistent with Gain's Christchurch origins. Co-founder is reliably \\"Max Podolian\\" (full name Maksym Podolian). Funding figures come from aggregators (PitchBook NZ$1.27M vs Tracxn ~$18K) with no primary disclosure, so amounts are approximate.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2014", "sources": ["https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/preno", "https://prenohq.com/nz/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/preno", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/ameliagain", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/mpodolian/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/story/23yo-hotelier-saas-enterpreneur", "https://hotelmagazine.co.nz/2024/03/08/women-in-business-amelia-gain-preno/", "https://hoteltechreport.com/news/automating-hotel-ops-amelia-gain", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/preno/__2sF55tea13LtMkMzTPHoG6spmFweiByPyR6V3b69txY", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/117969-04", "https://thespinoff.co.nz/podcasts/30-07-2020/how-preno-is-reimagining-the-future-of-hotel-bookings"], "website": "https://prenohq.com", "industry": "Hospitality / Travel SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed via fresh searches: both founders (Amelia Gain, CEO; Max Podolian, CTO) are real and correctly named/roled across multiple independent sources (NBR-sourced reporting, Hotel Magazine NZ, The Spinoff, Hotel Tech Report, Icehouse job board). Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed by Icehouse's own portfolio/job-board listing. Status confirmed active/independent (no acquisition or shutdown; SiteMinder is a partnership). Founder-background detail refined (Gain Christchurch-born; sister co-owned The Spire; both founders met during IT polytech studies). No facts were contradicted; only the funding amounts remain aggregator-sourced and approximate, and the 2014-vs-2015 founding/launch nuance is unchanged. Draft was accurate.", "statusDetail": "Active and independent; privately held (approx. 22 employees). No acquisition or IPO found. Maintains a technology-partner integration with SiteMinder (a partnership, not an acquisition).", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Third-party aggregators report a 2015-era Seed round; PitchBook cites roughly NZ$1.27M total, while Tracxn lists a much smaller figure — treat amounts as approximate (no primary disclosure found). Investors named across Icehouse Ventures' job board and aggregators (Crunchbase/Tracxn) include Icehouse Ventures, Creative HQ, Lightning Lab, New Zealand Growth Capital Partners (NZGCP), Arc Angels, and Aspire NZ Seed Fund.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-0