org:iv-parrot-analytics	organization	Parrot Analytics	Global entertainment analytics measuring audience demand for content across platforms and countries.	Los Angeles (West Hollywood), USA	https://www.parrotanalytics.com	{"entertainment analytics","audience demand measurement","media data science",streaming,"B2B SaaS","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Parrot Analytics is a data science company that measures and predicts global audience demand for TV shows, films and other entertainment content across streaming, social media and other platforms, built around its \\"Demand Expressions\\" metric. Founded in New Zealand by Wared Seger (who grew up in West Auckland and drew on the University of Auckland entrepreneurship ecosystem), it became a leading provider of cross-platform demand analytics for studios, broadcasters and streamers worldwide. The company is now headquartered in the Los Angeles / West Hollywood area, with additional offices including Auckland, New York and London. It remains an active, private, independent company as of 2026.", "notes": "Do not confuse with the unrelated French drone maker \\"Parrot.\\" Founding year varies across sources (2011/2012/2013): the company's own leadership page and PitchBook/Crunchbase state 2012, VideoAge says 2011, and the Icehouse jobs page plus several profiles say 2013; 2012 used here as the company's self-reported year. HQ is now Los Angeles / West Hollywood while the company retains Auckland (NZ) roots. Funding total (~US$12.7M) and exact stage are loosely reported across aggregators.", "stage": "Seed / venture-backed", "status": "active", "founded": "2012", "sources": ["https://www.parrotanalytics.com/company/leadership/wared-seger/", "https://www.parrotanalytics.com/company/", "https://www.videoageinternational.net/2022/11/28/cover-stories/insight-into-parrot-more-than-just-analytics-data/", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/alumni/our-alumni/40-under-40/a-z-list-of-profiles/wared-seger.html", "https://www.velocity.auckland.ac.nz/project/wared-seger/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/parrot-analytics", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/58343-50", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/waredseger/", "https://www.stuff.co.nz/business/unlimited/10228206/Big-data-is-big-business"], "website": "https://www.parrotanalytics.com", "industry": "Media & entertainment analytics / data science", "confidence": "medium", "verifyNote": "Dropped co-founders Chris Riddell and Adel Shahin: VideoAge International explicitly states these names appear on \\"various online accounts\\" but were \\"not officially confirmed by anyone at the company,\\" and no authoritative source independently confirms them, so they fail the sourcing bar. Wared Seger confirmed as founder/CEO (company site says \\"founder and CEO\\"; some external sources use \\"co-founder\\"). Corrected founded year from 2013 to 2012 to match the company's own leadership page and PitchBook/Crunchbase (year still disputed; noted). Changed stage from the unsupported \\"Series B\\" to \\"Seed / venture-backed\\" (Crunchbase lists the last disclosed round as a 2017 seed). Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via reporting that it participated in a 2017 round alongside Ice Angels/Melbourne Angels/NZ Growth Capital Partners. Status confirmed active/private/independent; layoffs reference is a personal social post, not a confirmed company event. Confidence lowered from high to medium given founder-list correction and founding-year/funding-stage ambiguity.", "statusDetail": "Active, private and independent as of 2026, expanding internationally (e.g., a Qatar Film Committee partnership and Middle East office in Nov 2025) and still hiring. A March 2025 personal social-media post referenced layoffs, but no acquisition or shutdown is confirmed.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Reported total funding of approximately US$12.7M (Crunchbase/PitchBook). Icehouse Ventures, Ice Angels, Melbourne Angels and New Zealand Growth Capital Partners participated in a 2017 round; founder also raised early capital via the University of Auckland ecosystem (K1W1 / Sir Stephen Tindall cited). Specific round amounts/stage are not consistently disclosed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-tnx	organization	TNX Logistics	AI and behavioural-science SaaS for autonomous spot road-freight procurement	Auckland, New Zealand (offices also in Berlin and Chicago)	https://www.tnx.co.nz	{logistics,"freight procurement",SaaS,"supply chain","machine learning","Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "TNX Logistics (branded \\"TNX\\") was an Auckland-founded SaaS company providing an autonomous road-transport procurement platform that combined data science and behavioural science for carrier profiling, price prediction and spot pricing to lower shippers' freight costs. Founded in 2016, it used New Zealand as a pilot market before adding offices in Berlin and Chicago and serving customers across multiple continents. It was acquired by German logistics-platform company Transporeon GmbH in 2021 (announced June/July 2021), with the product folded into Transporeon's freight-sourcing offering. Financial terms were not disclosed.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is \\"TNX Logistics\\" (LogTech / freight-procurement SaaS, tnx.co.nz), NOT US biotech Tonix Pharmaceuticals (ticker TNX/TNXP) nor any same-named foreign firm. Post-acquisition the brand became \\"Transporeon Freight Sourcing\\" (Transporeon was itself later acquired by Trimble). HQ is consistently reported as Auckland, NZ with additional offices in Berlin and Chicago (the draft's \\"later Berlin\\" overstated a HQ move). Acquisition date varies by source: FreightWaves/Crunchbase/Tracxn cite 10 June 2021, while Buddle Findlay's deal notice cites a 5 July 2021 announcement; terms undisclosed. Funding total (~$1.41M) comes from PitchBook/Tracxn aggregators and is shown in USD (not NZ$); not confirmed via a primary source, and exact round/stage labels are approximate (seed-stage). LinkedIn URLs for Hoffmann and Bryan left null because multiple same-name profiles surfaced and none could be uniquely verified; only Jonah McIntire's profile was confidently attributed.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2016", "sources": ["https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/portfolio", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/226577-89", "https://www.buddlefindlay.com/insights/buddle-findlay-advises-tnx-logistics-on-its-sale-to-transporeon-gmbh/", "https://itsupplychain.com/transporeon-to-offer-autonomous-spot-freight-procurement-services-following-acquisition-of-tnx-logistics/", "https://www.freightwaves.com/news/startups/technology/do-more-with-the-data-how-tnx-logistics", "https://www.shippingandfreightresource.com/executive-insights-tnx-logistics-co-founder-managing-director-alex-hoffman-on-striking-the-perfect-human-machine-balance/", "https://www.fleetpoint.org/expert-bio/jonah-mcintire/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/tnx", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/tnx/__Q3iJgXcQgrGGI0nJuhF-k7qp0aOLrDJPUfbBKuPmuCE", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jonahmcintire/"], "website": "https://www.tnx.co.nz", "industry": "Logistics / Supply-chain software (LogTech)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed via fresh searches: all three founders (Jonah McIntire CEO; Alexander/Alex Hoffmann and Joshua/Josh Bryan, both Co-founder & Managing Director) are real and correctly roled; founded 2016; acquired by Transporeon (terms undisclosed); and Icehouse Ventures/ICE Angels/The Icehouse backing is confirmed (TNX appears in the Icehouse portfolio and across aggregators, including via Tuhua). Corrections: standardised founder name to \\"Alexander Hoffmann\\" and \\"Joshua Bryan\\"; corrected HQ to Auckland NZ with Berlin and Chicago offices (draft implied a HQ move to Berlin); changed funding currency claim from NZ$1.41M to US$1.41M (aggregator figure, unconfirmed by primary source); softened acquisition month to reflect conflicting June-10 vs July-5 2021 reporting; trimmed unverifiable specifics (Manhattan Associates/Panalpina roles, McIntire's textbook, Bryan's exact universities) from bios rather than assert them. Could not confirm: exact funding round/stage, precise total, and LinkedIn profiles for Hoffmann and Bryan.", "statusDetail": "Acquired by Transporeon GmbH (Germany) in 2021; terms undisclosed", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Reported to have raised roughly US$1.41M (per PitchBook/Tracxn aggregators) from investors including Icehouse Ventures, ICE Angels, The Icehouse, Coda Group and Sparkbox Ventures, prior to its 2021 acquisition.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-vortex-power-systems	organization	Vortex Power Systems	NZ cleantech turning industrial waste heat into clean power via man-made atmospheric vortices	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.vortexpowersystems.com	{cleantech,"waste-heat recovery","renewable energy","deep tech","atmospheric vortex","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Vortex Power Systems is a New Zealand deep-tech / cleantech company that grew out of research at the University of Auckland and converts low-grade industrial waste heat into zero-carbon electricity. Its proprietary system uses waste heat to saturate air and create a controlled, free-standing atmospheric buoyancy vortex (a man-made whirlwind) whose rising, swirling column of air drives a turbine to generate power. After proving the physics in the University of Auckland's aerodynamics lab, the company has broken ground on a pilot plant near Gisborne (Whangara) aimed at driving a roughly one-megawatt generator. It remains an early-stage, pre-revenue R&D company and has reportedly sought around NZ$5 million to build the demonstration plant at scale.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the NZ University of Auckland spin-out (vortexpowersystems.com), distinct from same-named foreign firms (e.g. Vortex Energy in the UAE). Founders are Neil Hawkes (CTO) and Prof. Richard Flay (CSO), the technology originators. Perzaan Mehta is the CEO (joined 2020, formerly of investor Pacific Channel) and is correctly NOT listed as a co-founder. Icehouse Ventures backing is confirmed via investor aggregators (Tracxn names Icehouse Ventures and Pacific Channel as the institutional investors; Crunchbase corroborates). Pacific Channel and the University of Auckland Inventors' Fund were the earliest backers. Funding figures (NZ$5M, NZ$1.3M) are reported targets, not confirmed closed rounds; exact amounts and stage are unconfirmed.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.vortexpowersystems.com/about", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/news/2022/10/28/whirlwind-way-generate-electricity-waste-heat.html", "https://www.pacificchannel.com/stories/vortex-power-systems", "https://www.pacificchannel.com/stories/vortex-power-systems-achieves-key-milestone", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/vortex-power-systems-is-raising-5m-to-build-demo-plant/", "https://www.uniservices.co.nz/case-studies/vortex-power-systems-revolutionary-green-energy", "https://www.enterpriseangels.co.nz/project/vortex-power-systems/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/gisborne-herald/news/vortex-ready-to-build-world-first-power-plant/D6MZ6F2UFVEZNFNW44PS5CAA3U/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/vortexpowersystems/__o8roH2QV8F73rGA6IUZgnlBtUrLES10tV-0kxrt-4lE", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/vortex-power-systems", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/richard-flay-7a3b7915/", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/perzaan-mehta-1aa56275/"], "website": "https://www.vortexpowersystems.com", "industry": "Cleantech / Renewable Energy", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Draft was substantively accurate. Independently confirmed: founders Neil Hawkes (CTO) and Richard Flay (CSO, Professor Emeritus 2024); Perzaan Mehta is CEO not a co-founder; Icehouse Ventures is an investor (Tracxn lists Icehouse Ventures + Pacific Channel as the institutional investors, corroborated by Crunchbase); 2017 founding; Auckland HQ; ~NZ$5M raise for a Gisborne demo plant driving a ~1MW generator. Corrected the status detail: the Gisborne pilot plant has broken ground / is under construction (per NZ Herald and Gisborne Herald) rather than merely being planned. Could not confirm Neil Hawkes' personal LinkedIn URL (left null); exact funding round sizes/stage remain unconfirmed (aggregator figures redacted). Trimmed an unverifiable specific employer detail from Hawkes' bio.", "statusDetail": "Active, early-stage pre-revenue deep-tech R&D; physics validated in the University of Auckland lab, pilot plant under construction near Gisborne (Whangara), and raising ~NZ$5M for an at-scale demonstration plant driving a ~1MW generator.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Reported ~NZ$5M raise toward an at-scale demonstration plant near Gisborne. Investors named across sources include Pacific Channel (early/lead deep-tech backer since spin-out), Icehouse Ventures, the University of Auckland Inventors' Fund, family office K1W1, and Enterprise Angels; an earlier round sought ~NZ$1.3M to design a 1MW station. Exact closed round sizes are unconfirmed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-upstock	organization	Upstock	B2B wholesale ordering platform for food & beverage suppliers and buyers, built by ex-Xero team	Wellington, New Zealand	https://www.upstock.app	{"B2B marketplace",Foodservice,FMCG,"Wholesale ordering",SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Upstock is a New Zealand-based B2B marketplace that simplifies wholesale food and beverage ordering between suppliers and buyers such as cafes, restaurants, bars, grocers and supermarkets, replacing disorganised texts, emails and phone calls with a digital platform. It was started by Foxton Fizz owner Matt Watson and built out by former Xero team members Philip Fierlinger and Duncan Ritchie, who lead the company as co-CEOs. By 2024 it connected over 30,000 wholesale buyers to more than 1,000 suppliers and around 90,000 products across New Zealand and Australia. The company has expanded into Australia and signed a distribution deal with Woolworths.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing is confirmed by multiple sources: Upstock's own About page lists Icehouse Ventures among VC investors; Scoop notes the 2020 round was Icehouse Ventures' 200th investment; NZ Herald reports Icehouse increased its investment in later rounds; and Icehouse Ventures' own job board hosts an Upstock company page. Co-CEO structure (Fierlinger + Ritchie) confirmed by Balance The Grind and Crowdcast. Note: Upstock's About page renders Ritchie's title as 'CEO & Director,' but he and Fierlinger are consistently described as co-CEOs elsewhere. Distinct from the unrelated US 'Upstock.io' equity-compensation startup. Only Philip Fierlinger's LinkedIn URL could be confirmed; Watson's and Ritchie's individual LinkedIn URLs were not verified (null).", "stage": "Seed (seed extension; ~$13m raised to date)", "status": "active", "founded": "2020", "sources": ["https://www.upstock.app/about", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/BU2009/S00286/upstockapp-raises-35-million-expands-in-nz-hospo-sector.htm", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/