org:iv-pyper-vision	organization	Pyper Vision	NZ aerospace startup using AI "fog-casting" to cut fog-related airport and airline delays	Christchurch, New Zealand	https://pypervision.com	{aerospace,aviation,"weather forecasting","AI/deep learning",drones,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Pyper Vision is a Christchurch, New Zealand aerospace startup founded by Emily Blythe that builds technology to reduce fog-related flight disruptions. It originally developed a drone-dispersed, water-absorbing (hygroscopic) system to clear fog, then pivoted around 2023 toward an AI/deep-learning \\"fog-casting\\" platform that aims to predict fog more accurately than traditional forecasts (which often warn of fog that never forms). The company has run trials and partnerships with Air New Zealand, Christchurch, Hamilton and Dunedin airports, and London City Airport (via BA CityFlyer). Fog is cited as causing billions of dollars in annual aviation losses worldwide.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via NZ Herald (37.33% stake) and the 2018 First Cut under-30 pitch-challenge NZ$700k win. Company was registered as Limpidity Limited and renamed Pyper Vision Limited in 2020. David Morgan (ex-Air NZ chief pilot) collaborates closely but is a senior executive/advisor, not a founder, so he is excluded from the founders array. Emily Blythe's LinkedIn URL is from search-result titles (page is auth-gated); Nick Jackson's LinkedIn could not be located (null). Not to be confused with same-named foreign companies; this is the NZ aviation-tech firm.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2016", "sources": ["https://pypervision.com/about-us", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/startup-blueprint-nick-jackson", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/aerospace-startup-pyper-vision-founder-emily-blythe-aim-to-save-airports-airlines-a-fortune-with-better-fog-forecasting/RYMRPLWHU5F6FADDD5FO54EYXE/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/pyper-visions-airport-fog-busting-