org:iv-shuttlerock	organization	Shuttlerock	NZ-founded Creative-as-a-Service firm producing platform-optimized video ads at scale	Nelson, New Zealand	https://www.shuttlerock.com/	{adtech,creative-as-a-service,"video advertising",martech,"social media","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Shuttlerock is a New Zealand-founded company that produces social and digital video advertising at scale, pioneering a \\"Creative-as-a-Service\\" (CaaS) model that blends human designers with proprietary technology to turn static images or existing assets into platform-optimized video ads. Founded in Nelson in 2011 by Jonny Hendriksen, who started with a small team from his kitchen table, it grew into a global creative network operating a \\"follow-the-sun\\" model across offices on multiple continents while keeping its head office in Nelson. In September 2024 it acquired dynamic ad-automation platform Shakr to scale personalized, geo-targeted video production.", "notes": "Icehouse backing firmly confirmed: Icehouse Ventures' own IVX fund article explicitly names Shuttlerock as an existing portfolio company \\"generating $10m+ revenue\\", and the Series A announcement lists \\"The Icehouse\\" as a participating early investor. This is the Nelson, NZ-founded adtech company (distinct from any same-named foreign entity). Jonny Hendriksen is consistently the sole named founder across EY, BusinessDesk, Idealog, Stuff and Crunchbase — no co-founders found. LinkedIn URL (nz.linkedin.com/in/jonathanhendriksen) appears consistently in search results as his profile but LinkedIn blocks direct bot fetches, so it is not independently page-verified. Founder location kept as Nelson (company head office); note some profiles (ZoomInfo) list him as personally Auckland-based. Total cumulative funding not authoritatively disclosed; the US$20M Series A (2021) and US$7.5M note (2019) are the documented major rounds. Stage left as \\"Series A\\" as the latest disclosed round.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2011", "sources": ["https://blog.shuttlerock.com/shuttlerock-series-a", "https://blog.shuttlerock.com/shuttlerock-announces-7.5m-funding-round", "https://blog.shuttlerock.com/shuttlerock-acquires-shakr", "https://resources.icehouseventures.co.nz/blog/ivx-fund", "https://www.ey.com/en_nz/entrepreneur-of-the-year/new-zealand/finalists-2024/jonny-hendriksen", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/news-in-brief/shuttlerock-founder-jonny-hendriksen-wins-ey-entrepreneur-of-the-year-award", "https://idealog.co.nz/venture/2024/11/shuttlerock-founder-named-eys-entrepreneur-of-the-year", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/business/shuttlerock-scores-sam-morgan-as-investor-and-director/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/shuttlerock", "https://www.shuttlerock.com/about-us"], "website": "https://www.shuttlerock.com/", "industry": "Advertising technology / digital creative services", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Draft was accurate. Independently confirmed via primary sources: sole founder Jonny Hendriksen (Founder & CEO), the US$20M Series A (May 3, 2021; Sam Morgan lead; GD1 + The Icehouse), the 2019 US$7.5M convertible note (Jasmine Holdings, GD1, T Station; Sam Morgan joined board), the Shakr acquisition (Sept 25, 2024), and Icehouse backing (IVX portfolio + Series A participant). Minor refinements: clarified Hendriksen WON (not just finalist) EY EOY NZ 2024; tightened oneLiner to \\"platform-optimized\\"; corrected ValueClick Japan listing detail to \\"first foreigner to list a company on the Tokyo Stock Exchange (May 2000)\\" and added Keio University; trimmed the specific office-city and global-brand-client list from the description since those were not all re-verified in this pass. LinkedIn URL could not be directly fetched (LinkedIn 999) but is consistently surfaced as his profile.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating globally. Acquired dynamic ad-automation platform Shakr in September 2024. Founder Jonny Hendriksen won EY Entrepreneur of the