org:iv-aglow	organization	aglow	Beauty membership platform turning salon clients into recurring subscription revenue.	Sydney (Pyrmont), Australia	https://www.getaglow.co	{beauty-tech,SaaS,"subscription memberships","fintech payments","salon software","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "aglow is a SaaS platform dedicated to powering beauty memberships, helping salons, clinics and spas convert pay-as-you-go clients into recurring subscription revenue. Launched in May 2023 by Karl Margrain (CEO) and Jo Blundell (CRO), it operates across Australia and New Zealand and reports use by 600+ salons serving 5,000+ members. In August 2024 it raised about A$1.25M led by New Zealand VC Icehouse Ventures via the Brand Fund (a JV with NZ firm Previously Unavailable), with Timely founder Ryan Baker and Tyro co-founder Peter Haig also investing. Headquartered in Sydney, it is strongly NZ-connected through its lead Kiwi investor and NZ-rooted co-founder.", "notes": "DISAMBIGUATION: The Icehouse-backed entity is aglow / getaglow.co, a trans-Tasman beauty-membership SaaS HEADQUARTERED IN SYDNEY (Pyrmont), NSW, Australia (Business News Australia headline \\"Sydney startup\\"; Tracxn \\"Pyrmont, Australia\\"; CEO Karl Margrain is Sydney-based, ex-Payleadr/Tyro). It is NOT NZ-domiciled but is strongly NZ-CONNECTED: lead investor is NZ VC Icehouse Ventures (via the Brand Fund JV with NZ firm Previously Unavailable, whose Simon Pound publicly backed the team), co-founder Jo Blundell has an NZ-rooted SaaS career (Timely, Xero, Kitomba), and it operates across AU and NZ. Do NOT confuse with unrelated same-named entities (e.g., Aglow International, a US religious organization). FOUNDING-YEAR DISCREPANCY: company about page and most media say launched May 2023; Tracxn lists 2024 — used 2023 per the company's own statement. Funding ~A$1.25M widely reported, announced 13 Aug 2024.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2023", "sources": ["https://www.getaglow.co/about-us", "https://www.