org:iv-appetise	organization	Appetise	NZ meal-planning app turning shopper behaviour into FMCG market-research insights	Christchurch, New Zealand	https://appetise.io	{FoodTech,"Meal planning","FMCG insights","Consumer data",SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Appetise (formerly MenuAid) is a New Zealand-founded food-tech company that operates a free consumer meal-planning and smart-grocery-shopping app across New Zealand and Australia. Its B2B arm, Appetise Insights, monetises anonymised observed shopper-behaviour data, selling market research to FMCG food and beverage brands such as Fonterra, Kraft Heinz and Lee Kum Kee. The company launched as MenuAid in September 2021 on a paid subscription model, then dropped consumer fees and rebranded to Appetise in August 2024 to fuel its data platform. By early 2026 it reported more than 110,000 active users and tripling B2B revenue (around NZ$3.5M).", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the New Zealand food-tech company Appetise (appetise.io), formerly MenuAid (menuaid.co.nz) — NOT the UK online food-ordering company Appetise.co.uk nor any same-named US firm. The Crunchbase profile lives at crunchbase.com/organization/menuaid. Series A headline figure is reported as both ~NZ$7M (Startup Daily, Capital Brief, SmartCompany) and NZ$8M (NZ Herald), Feb 2026; reported B2B revenue ~NZ$3.5M tripling over six months, with Australia driving ~70% of growth. User figures vary by metric: 110,000+ active users across NZ + Australia (Startup Daily), vs NZ Herald's narrower 70,000 Kiwi households. HQ is Christchurch (~20 staff) with a Sydney office (~6 staff); company operates across NZ and Australia. The 2022 ~NZ$1M seed was led by Sprout (NZ AgriTech/FoodTech seed investor), not Icehouse. FMCG clients named across sources include Fonterra, Kraft Heinz, Lee Kum Kee, Tegel, Farmland Foods, Barker's and Angel Bay.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2021", "sources": ["https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/kiwi-gro