org:iv-mushroom-material	organization	Mushroom Material	NZ startup making home-compostable mycelium packaging to replace polystyrene styrofoam	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.mushroommaterial.com/	{mycelium,packaging,cleantech,biomaterials,sustainability,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Mushroom Material is a New Zealand cleantech startup developing home-compostable, mycelium-based packaging as a direct replacement for expanded polystyrene styrofoam. Its process grows millions of fungi-based pellets from agricultural and organic waste, then coats them in a binding agent and shapes them into protective packaging using conventional moulding equipment. Founded in 2020 by Shaun Seaman and Jotinder Singh, the company operates out of Auckland while being registered/headquartered in Singapore to improve access to venture capital and Southeast Asian customers. In 2024 it raised over US$5 million (about NZ$8.5 million) in seed funding to build a pilot plant in Mount Roskill, Auckland.", "notes": "Do not confuse with same-named foreign companies; a separate NZ mycelium-packaging startup, BioFab (founders James Ferrier, Phil Matheson, Michel Khuwattansenee, founded 2018), is distinct. Mushroom Material is registered/headquartered in Singapore but founded and operating out of Auckland, NZ, so some sources call it \\"Singapore-based.\\" The seed round is reported as both ~US$5M and ~NZ$8.5M (same round, different currencies).", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2020", "sources": ["https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/news/2024/12/12/biotech-company-mushroom-material-aims-remove-polystyrene.html", "https://wavemaker.vc/mushroom-material-secures-over-us5m-seed-round-for-fungi-based-styrofoam-alternative/", "https://technode.global/2024/08/13/wavemaker-partners-seeds-capital-back-mushroom-material-in-5m-seed-funding/", "https://www.mycostories.com/post/mushroom-material-secures-8-5-million-to-revolutionize-packaging-with-mycelium-based-composites", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/material-startup-mushroom-material-raises-8m-in-seed-round/", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/shaun-seaman", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/jotindersingh", "https://theorg.com/org/mushroom-material/org-chart/jotinder-singh", "https://theorg.com/org/mushroom-material/org-chart/shaun-seaman", "https://www.mushroommaterial.com/"], "website": "https://www.mushroommaterial.com/", "industry": "Sustainable packaging / advanced materials (biotech cleantech)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All material claims independently confirmed via fresh searches. Both founders verified: Shaun Seaman (Founder & CEO) and Jotinder Singh (Co-founder & COO/CTO) — the draft left Jotinder's role, LinkedIn and location partly blank, now filled (nz.linkedin.com/in/jotindersingh, Auckland NZ, Mechatronics degree, ex-StretchSense/Greefa). Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed (led ~NZ$470k pre-seed and participated in the 2024 seed round). Seaman's Entrepreneur First and Fisher & Paykel background and the 2018 Indonesia surfing inspiration are confirmed; also added StretchSense founding-team detail. Funding, Aug 2024 timing, Mount Roskill pilot plant, Techstars Singapore, and Singapore registration / Auckland operations all confirmed. No fabrications found in the draft.", "statusDetail": "Active; building a ~1,300 sqm pilot plant in Mount Roskill, Auckland following its 2024 seed round, with first customer orders planned from 2025. Registered/headquartered in Singapore while operating out of Auckland.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised over US$5M (~NZ$8.5M) seed round announced August 2024, led by Wavemaker Partners and Singapore's SEEDS Capital, with participation from Icehouse Ventures, K1W1 (Sir Stephen Tindall) and Black Kite Capital. Icehouse Ventures previously led a ~NZ$470,000 pre-seed round. Accepted into the Techstars accelerator in Singapore (only the second NZ company to do so).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57