org:iv-insite-ai	organization	Insite AI	Autonomous AI for category & revenue growth management at the world's largest consumer brands	Bentonville, Arkansas, USA (Auckland, New Zealand office)	https://www.insite.ai	{AI,"Consumer Goods (CPG)","Category Management","Revenue Growth Management","Retail Tech","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Insite AI builds a configurable, AI-powered decision platform that helps large consumer packaged goods (CPG) brands optimize category management, assortment, pricing, space and trade promotion decisions across retail channels. Founded in New Zealand by Shaveer Mirpuri and Jonathan Reid around 2018-2019, it scaled into a US-headquartered (Bentonville, Arkansas) business serving top-100 consumer goods companies while retaining an Auckland, NZ technology team. In October 2022 it raised a US$19M Series A led by NewRoad Capital and M12 (Microsoft's venture fund). It tripled revenue in the ~15 months before that round.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the NZ-founded Insite AI for CPG/category & revenue growth management, NOT same-named foreign companies. Founding year varies by source (2018 per Crunchbase/Tracxn/Enterprise Angels; 2019 per the company's own Series A press release and the Icehouse job board); kept 2018 as the earliest corroborated year. HQ is now Bentonville, AR (with Austin/Bee Cave, TX locations) while retaining an Auckland tech team. Icehouse Ventures backing is UNCONFIRMED: Insite AI appears on the Icehouse Ventures job board, but that page contains no investment statement, and no funding announcement or investor database (Crunchbase, CB Insights, Tracxn, PitchBook) names Icehouse Ventures as a direct investor. Note co-founder Jonathan Reid was a director of the Icehouse Group (2015-2020) — a relationship to the Icehouse organisation, but not evidence of an Icehouse Ventures investment in Insite AI. Shaveer Mirpuri's personal LinkedIn could not be fetched (likely nz.linkedin.com/in/shaveer-mirpuri-09697b102 per search), so left null.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/insite-ai-leader-in-consumer-brands-category--revenue-growth-management-solutions-lands-19m-series-a-funding-led-by-newroad-capital-and-m12-microsofts-venture-fund-301646102.html", "https://www.enterpriseangels.co.nz/project/insite-ai/", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/new-zealand-intelligent-merchandising-platform-insite-ai-raises-1-8-million/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/shaveer-mirpuri", "https://theorg.com/org/insite-ai/org-chart/shaveer-mirpuri", "https://theorg.com/org/insite-ai/org-chart/jonathan-reid-1", "https://makercapital.fund/people/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/insite-ai", "https://newroadcp.com/companies/insite-ai/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/insite-ai/__-GuI1jw0WpEnkpsvcDMoN_JtrtUC7CDF4qGb1Z5ySBY"], "website": "https://www.insite.ai", "industry": "Artificial Intelligence / CPG & Retail SaaS", "confidence": "medium", "verifyNote": "Corrected Jonathan Reid's bio: the draft wrongly attributed a ~10-year Spark executive background (Chief Strategy Officer / Chief Product Officer / founder of Spark Ventures) to him — that career belongs to Rod Snodgrass (a separate Maker Capital partner), per makercapital.fund/people. Reid's verified background is The VMG Group, VMG Ventures, Goat Ventures, Maker Partners, and director of the Icehouse Group (2015-2020). Downgraded Icehouse backing from 'likely' to 'unconfirmed' — the job-board listing shows no investment statement and no investor database names Icehouse Ventures. Trimmed unverified claims about Mirpuri (two nine-figure exits, TEDxAuckland, Forbes Technology Council could not be independently confirmed; Goat Ventures founding confirmed). Corrected/added early-round investors: Goat Ventures (lead), NZ Venture Investment Fund, Lewis Holdings (NZ$2M, Nov 2018) plus Enterprise Angels (2020); removed unverified 'NZ Growth Capital Partners' and