org:iv-designer-wardrobe	organization	Designer Wardrobe	NZ peer-to-peer marketplace to buy, sell and rent pre-loved designer fashion.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://designerwardrobe.co.nz	{"fashion resale",marketplace,"circular economy",peer-to-peer,"clothing rental","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Designer Wardrobe is a New Zealand online marketplace where people buy, sell and rent pre-loved and designer fashion. It began as a Facebook buy/sell/swap group started by Donielle Brooke and grew into a website and apps, with the company reporting over 325,000-350,000 members across NZ and Australia by 2025. Based in Auckland, it has also offered high-end garment rental and ran physical stores (since closed during the COVID-19 pandemic), and expanded into Australia in 2024. It positions itself around sustainability and the circular fashion economy.", "notes": "Founding year is reported inconsistently: the Facebook group dates to ~2013, NZ Herald says 2015, but the company's own About page and the Newmarket profile say 2014, which is used here as the best-supported value. Founder roles have shifted: Donielle Brooke is the original creator/co-founder (creative/brand side); Aidan Bartlett is co-founder and tech lead who is now CEO. Ruby Morgan was CEO from Jan 2019 (per NZ Herald, June 2020); more recent coverage and his LinkedIn list Bartlett as CEO, so leadership has changed since 2019/2020. Not to be confused with same-named foreign resale sites (e.g. Designer-Wardrobe in the UK/US).", "stage": "Seed / equity crowdfunding", "status": "active", "founded": "2014", "sources": ["https://designerwardrobe.co.nz/about", "https://newmarket.co.nz/something-borrowed-designer-wardrobes-donielle-brooke/", "https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/whos-who/snowball-effect", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/how-designer-wardrobe-pivoted-during-covid-and-kept-its-shirt-on-its-back/ZDKWUSJYMGNRX2GAJD5JDR4PX4/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/covid-19-delta-outbreak-investor-simon-moutters-message-to-the-govt-as-designer-wardrobe-closes-stores/NILJK2QV7KH45P4BDIZWLZIFJU/", "https://www.newstalkzb.co.nz/news/business/chaos-and-covid-how-aidan-bartlett-turned-designer-wardrobe-around/", "https://business.scoop.co.nz/2017/05/23/designer-wardrobe-completes-1-7m-capital-raising/", "https://www.snowballeffect.co.nz/offers/show/designer-wardrobe", "https://auckland.scoop.co.nz/2025/09/designer-wardrobe-launches-ai-powered-selling-to-nzs-growing-pre-loved-market/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/531261/new-zealand-pre-loved-fashion-start-up-expands-into-australia", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/aidan-bartlett"], "website": "https://designerwardrobe.co.nz", "industry": "Fashion resale / e-commerce marketplace", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Both founders independently confirmed (company About page, Newmarket, NewstalkZB, NZ Herald): Donielle Brooke (co-founder, creative/brand) and Aidan Bartlett (co-founder, tech lead, now CEO). Icehouse backing upgraded from the draft's caveat: multiple NZ Herald sources explicitly name Icehouse Ventures / Ice Angels among investors and confirm the founders graduated from The Icehouse incubator/Lightning Lab (Moutter discovered them via an Icehouse Lightning Lab pitch event), so 'confirmed' holds with higher confidence. Confirmed Simon Moutter as chairman and Shane Bradley as director/co-lead investor, plus Sir Stephen Tindall (K1W1), Sam Morgan and Aaron Bhatnagar. Status confirmed active into 2025-2026 (325,000+ members, ~NZ$5m revenue, AU expansion 2024, AI listing tools 2025); physical stores closed during COVID. Removed the unverified Donielle Brooke LinkedIn URL (could not independently confirm) and the unverified 'hairdresser at Stephen Marr' detail. Confidence raised to high. Draft's reported '~NZ$1.92m total on aggregators' was not separately verified and was folded into the funding narrative. Aidan Bartlett LinkedIn URL retained but not directly fetchable (HTTP 999).", "statusDetail": "Active private company as of 2025-2026; live marketplace website and apps with 325,000+ members, reported ~NZ$5m annual revenue (2025), Australia expansion (2024) and AI-powered listing tools (2025). Physical stores were closed during COVID-19. No acquisition or closure reported.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~NZ$1.7m via Snowball Effect equity crowdfunding (2017; one of Snowball Effect's most notable offers, cited at ~NZ$2.6m total) plus a ~NZ$1.9m round in Dec 2019. Named backers include Icehouse Ventures / Ice Angels, NZ Growth Capital Partners, Aspire NZ Seed Fund, Creative HQ, Shane Bradley (co-lead investor/director), former Spark CEO Simon Moutter (chairman/co-lead investor), Sir Stephen Tindall (K1W1), Sam Morgan and Aaron Bhatnagar.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-aply-id	organization	APLYiD	NZ regtech: AML/KYC and biometric identity verification for compliance-heavy businesses	Auckland, New Zealand	https://aplyid.com	{"identity verification",AML,KYC,biometrics,regtech,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "APLYiD is an Auckland-based regtech company founded in 2018 that provides an AML (anti-money laundering), KYC (know your customer) and biometric identity-verification platform. Its product verifies a customer's identity via a smartphone capture of a government ID plus a facial/selfie check, targeting mid-market organisations in real estate, legal, financial services and accounting. In October 2021 the company raised a NZ$7m Series A led by UK firm Octopus Ventures (Octopus's first NZ investment), with Australian fund Tribe Global Ventures also participating. The company maintains operations across New Zealand, Australia and the UK.", "notes": "\\"APLY ID\\" input corresponds to APLYiD (Auckland, NZ regtech). Founder roles vary across sources: Russell Smith is consistently CEO; Claudia Smith is described as COO by Octopus Ventures but as Co-CEO on APLYiD's current about page — COO retained as the most widely reported role. The two founders share a surname but are not related.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://aplyid.com/nz/about", "https://octopusventures.com/blog/our-investment-in-aplyid/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/aplyid", "https://fintech.global/2021/10/28/aplyid-nets-nzd-7m-from-octopus-ventures-led-series-a-in-regtech/", "https://www.finsmes.com/2021/10/aplyid-secures-nzd7m-in-series-a-funding.html", "https://www.finextra.com/pressarticle/90009/regtech-aplyid-secures-nz7m-series-a-led-by-uks-octopus-ventures", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/customer-id-startup-aplyid-raises-7m-says-nz-chasing-the-rest-of-the-world-with-outmoded-miq/I56JGF6S7ONUVWCHZTGL3LDLIM/", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/aplyid", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/aplyid", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/claudiaclaytonsmith/"], "website": "https://aplyid.com", "industry": "Regtech / Identity Verification (AML/KYC)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders (Russell Smith CEO, Claudia Smith COO), 2018 founding, Auckland HQ, NZ$7m Oct 2021 Series A led by Octopus Ventures, and active status all independently confirmed. Corrections: (1) added co-investor Tribe Global Ventures, which the draft omitted; (2) removed the unsupported claim that Octopus took a ~25% stake (no source found); (3) downgraded icehouseBacked from \\"confirmed\\" to \\"likely\\" — Icehouse appears in PitchBook's investor list and APLYiD sits on the Icehouse job board, but no primary press coverage of the round names Icehouse and the job-board listing alone does not confirm investment; (4) softened Claudia Smith's prior-venture claims (Renti/MoovMe) to only what Octopus sourced (Experian, LexisNexis). Note Claudia's title also appears as Co-CEO on the company's current about page.", "statusDetail": "Operating; company website and product/sector pages live, LinkedIn active. No acquisition or closure found as of mid-2026.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "NZ$7m Series A in October 2021 led by Octopus Ventures (UK) — Octopus's first investment in a NZ-headquartered company — with Australian fund Tribe Global Ventures also participating (APLYiD was Tribe's foundational investment). PitchBook also lists Icehouse Ventures (and Quesnay) among investors, but no primary press coverage of the Series A names Icehouse, so its exact role/round is unconfirmed.", "icehouseBacked": "likely"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
