org:iv-compostic	organization	Compostic	NZ maker of the world's first certified home-compostable cling wrap and resealable bags.	Parnell, Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.compostic.co.nz	{"compostable packaging",sustainability,"consumer goods","plastic alternatives",cleantech,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Compostic is an Auckland, New Zealand company (Compostic Limited, incorporated 17 Jan 2018) that makes certified home- and commercially-compostable kitchen packaging, including what it markets as the world's first home-compostable cling wrap, plus resealable bags. The products are derived from renewable plant-based materials such as corn and potato and are certified to break down in home compost (within about 24 weeks) rather than persisting like conventional plastics. After a New Zealand retail rollout, it expanded into Australia (Woolworths) and launched in the United States in 2021, reaching retailers including Erewhon. It remains a registered, operating company.", "notes": "Icehouse backing confirmed by two independent signals: Compostic is listed on Icehouse Ventures' official portfolio page, AND the NZ Companies Office cap table lists \\"ICEHOUSE VENTURES NOMINEES LIMITED\\" as a shareholder (alongside Hillfarrance and VMG Ventures Nominees). The company also went through Icehouse's Flux Accelerator (June 2019). Co-founder caveat: the company's own About page credits only \\"Jon,\\" but the Companies Office register lists Jonathan Reed as sole director and Joshua Bowden as a shareholder, and multiple NZ media outlets name both Reed and Bowden as co-founders — so the two-founder claim stands. The same Josh Bowden also co-founded noissue (not a different person). LinkedIn URLs could not be machine-verified (LinkedIn blocks fetches with HTTP 999); they are best-match from search and remain unverified. Funding amount (~NZ$500K) is from Icehouse's blog and aggregators, not a primary disclosure.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "source