try": "Climate tech / Carbon offsetting", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Icehouse Ventures backing is now firmly CONFIRMED: CarbonClick appears directly on Icehouse Ventures' own portfolio page (icehouseventures.co.nz/portfolio), not only PitchBook. The four founders (Czaplicki, Brady, Noordermeer, Rouse) and their roles were independently corroborated by The Spinoff, investible.com and a Purposely podcast interview. Key correction: Dave Rouse was NOT an original founder in the strict sense — per his own interview he was an early investor (friends/family round) approached by the technical founders (Czaplicki, Brady, Noordermeer) to be CEO; the company nonetheless lists him as \\"Founder,\\" so he is retained with a clarified bio. Could NOT independently confirm several draft bio claims for Rouse (Sea Cleaners co-founder, multiple board roles, The David Awards Supreme Winner, Maori heritage, Clevedon residence), so these were removed/softened. Corrected stage to \\"Seed\\", trimmed the \\"expanding into Southeast Asia\\" status claim (not freshly verified), and removed the unverified Centrality NZ$100k detail from funding (no source confirmed it in this check). B Corp certification confirmed via B Lab Global directory.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating as an independent private company; certified B Corporation since 2022.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Reported to have raised approximately US$1.66M across early-stage rounds (per PitchBook and Tracxn). Named investors across sources include Icehouse Ventures, Velocity Ventures, Creative HQ, Canterbury Angels, NetX, Investible and Plug and Play Tech Center. Latest reported round was a Seed round in November 2022 (undisclosed amount, Velocity Ventures). Totals are not officially disclosed by the company and vary by source.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-extraordinary	organization	Extraordinary (formerly HealthNow)	Auckland fintech: employer-funded wellbeing/benefits accounts spent via a Mastercard.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.extraordinarypay.com/	{fintech,"employee benefits",rewards,"HR tech",SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Extraordinary is an Auckland, New Zealand employee benefits and rewards platform that lets employers fund personal wellbeing accounts which staff spend via a customisable Mastercard across health, transport, gym, supermarket and other approved categories. It replaces manual gift cards, reimbursements and allowance tracking through an employer portal, employee app and physical/digital card. The company originally launched as HealthNow (initially a healthcare buy-now-pay-later service) and rebranded to Extraordinary on 30 October 2024 as it broadened from a health focus to wider employee rewards. It reports more than 100 business customers and around 10,000-12,500 cardholders, and is expanding into Australia.", "notes": "Disambiguation: this is the NZ employee-benefits fintech \\"Extraordinary\\" (extraordinarypay.com), the rebrand of HealthNow — not unrelated foreign companies named Extraordinary. The legacy healthnow.co.nz domain now resolves to the Extraordinary brand. Founding-year nuance: sources (The Org; founder narrative) indicate HealthNow was founded in 2020, initially as a healthcare buy-now-pay-later service, then pivoted to employee benefits with the productised offering/Mastercard launching in January 2024; the draft's \\"2021\\" was changed to 2020. No co-founders were confirmed in public sources — Steven Zinsli is consistently described as sole founder & CEO. His \\"partner\\" is mentioned only in relation to the earlier PhysioConnect venture, not as an Extraordinary co-founder. Cardholder count varies by source (~10,000 per RNZ at rebrand, ~12,500 cited elsewhere).", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2020", "sources": ["https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/health-allowance-platform-healthnow-raises-3-4m-seed-round/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/532352/tech-start-up-healthnow-rebrands-to-extraordinary", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/532361/auckland-company-extraordinary-develops-work-benefits-card", "https://www.extraordinarypay.com/resources/healthnows-rebrand-to-extraordinary-answering-your-faqs", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/companies/retail/entrepreneur-anna-mowbray-invests-in-ambitious-healthcare-start-up/TJ5B7LYVJOJKSFC2FFWQ2VASMQ/", "https://theorg.com/org/healthnow/org-chart/steven-zinsli", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/steven-zinsli-aa813184", "https://www.extraordinarypay.com/", "https://howto.stuff.co.nz/articles/start-up-rebrands-to-extraordinary-10-months-after-launching-as-its-offering-expands"], "website": "https://www.extraordinarypay.com/", "industry": "Fintech / Employee benefits software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founder (Steven Zinsli, Founder & CEO, sole founder), active status, the 30 Oct 2024 HealthNow-to-Extraordinary rebrand, the NZ$3.4m June 2024 seed round led by Icehouse Ventures / Brand Fund 1 / NZ Fintech Fund, Anna Mowbray's ~4.8% angel stake, and the product/HQ were all independently confirmed (NBR, RNZ, NZ Herald, The Org, company site). Corrections: changed foundedYear from 2021 to 2020 and clarified HealthNow began as a healthcare buy-now-pay-later service before pivoting to employee benefits; tightened the oneLiner to <=110 chars; corrected the LinkedIn URL to the clean slug (the emoji-encoded variant in the draft was a search artifact, and personal LinkedIn could not be directly fetched). The earlier customer list (ASB, Port of Tauranga, etc.) was not re-confirmed in this pass and was dropped from the description; the ~4.8% Mowbray stake comes from NZ Herald reporting, not a filing.", "statusDetail": "Active. Rebranded from HealthNow to Extraordinary on 30 October 2024; reported ~10,000-12,500 cardholders and 100+ business customers, with expansion into Australia.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised NZ$3.4m seed round (announced June 2024) led by Icehouse Ventures, Brand Fund 1 and the NZ Fintech Fund. Earlier backed by angel investors including Anna Mowbray (Zuru co-founder), reported to hold roughly a 4.8% stake.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
