rald. Exact amount and close date not publicly disclosed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-starboard	organization	Starboard Maritime Intelligence	AI maritime intelligence platform protecting oceans and subsea infrastructure	Wellington, New Zealand	https://www.starboardintelligence.com/	{"maritime intelligence","satellite/earth observation",AI,"defence & security",SaaS,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Starboard Maritime Intelligence is a Wellington, New Zealand SaaS company providing an AI-powered maritime domain awareness platform. It fuses over a billion daily data points from AIS, satellite imagery, radar, oceanographic and autonomous sensors to detect suspicious vessel activity, protect subsea cable infrastructure, and issue real-time alerts. The platform was developed by the government-backed Xerra Earth Observation Institute, launched commercially in 2021, and spun out as a separate company (Starboard Maritime Intelligence Ltd) in April 2023. It is used by governments, defence agencies and commercial operators across 30+ countries.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing is CONFIRMED via Starboard's own press release and NZ Herald, which list Icehouse Ventures as a participant in both the April 2024 NZ$5M seed round and the September 2025 NZ$23M Series A. The company has NO conventional individual founders: it was institutionally created/incubated by the Xerra Earth Observation Institute (a NZ government Regional Research Institute based in Alexandra, formerly the Centre for Space Science Technology) and incorporated as the separate Starboard Maritime Intelligence Ltd in April 2023; Xerra retains roughly a 33% stake. Trent Fulcher is the hired CEO & Executive Director (joined July 2022, replacing first CEO Steve Cotter) and is explicitly NOT a founder, so he has been removed from the founders array. Fulcher is an Idaho native in NZ since 2013; prior roles include head of strategy at Kiwibank, CEO of AirShare (Airways' drone-tracking unit) and Director Strategy at NZTE. Do not confuse with the unrelated US activist hedge fund \\"Starboard Value\\" or other same-named firms.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2023", "sources": ["https://www.starboardintelligence.com/press/starboard-maritime-intelligence-secures-nz-23m-series-a-to-scale-global-ai-powered-maritime-intelligence-technology", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/security-start-up-starboard-maritime-intelligence-raises-5m-tools-up-for-ai/V6HRCP5WIRDNRGM6NG2O7MTPOM/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/513403/starboard-maritime-intelligence-attracts-weighty-backers-for-expansion-plans", "https://www.starboardintelligence.com/press/ceo-appointment", "https://www.mbie.govt.nz/science-and-technology/science-and-innovation/funding-information-and-opportunities/investment-funds/regional-research-institutes/xerra-earth-observation-institute/starboard-platform", "https://www.alteredcapital.com/case-studies/starboard-series-a", "https://www.starboardintelligence.com/"], "website": "https://www.starboardintelligence.com/", "industry": "Maritime intelligence / geospatial defence SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed (both seed and Series A) and Series A details (NZ$23M, Sept 2025, lead investors) confirmed verbatim from the company press release and NZ Herald. Corrected the founders: the draft listed CEO Trent Fulcher in the founders array (flagged as 'not a founder') — removed entirely since Starboard has no individual founders and was institutionally spun out of Xerra; no real founder could be sourced, so the array is empty. Corrected foundedYear from the unverifiable 2019 to 2023 (the standalone Starboard Maritime Intelligence Ltd was incorporated April 2023; the platform itself launched commercially in 2021) — could not source a 2019 founding from any authoritative outlet. Refined the seed-round investor list (added Whakatupu Aotearoa Foundation and US-based SeaAhead, per NZ Herald). Tightened the description to remove the unverifiable founded-2019 framing. Confidence raised to high.", "statusDetail": "Active; raised an oversubscribed NZ$23M Series A in September 2025 to scale globally, and relocated its HQ into Wellington's CBD in late 2025.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "NZ$23M oversubscribed Series A (Sept 2025) co-led by Altered Capital, OIF Ventures and King River Capital, with Co:Act Capital, Icehouse Ventures and Whakatupu Aotearoa Foundation. Earlier NZ$5M seed round (April 2024) led by Altered Capital, with Icehouse Ventures, Invest South, Soul Capital, Whakatupu Aotearoa Foundation and SeaAhead participating.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-neocrete	organization	Neocrete	NZ cleantech making a concrete additive that cuts cement use 30-50% to lower emissions	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.neocrete.com	{"low-carbon concrete","cement reduction",decarbonization,"construction materials",cleantech,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Neocrete is a New Zealand cleantech startup decarbonising concrete. Its core product, the Neocrete Activator, is a powder additive (about 3% of cementitious material) that \\"supercharges\\" abundant low-carbon materials such as volcanic ash, fly ash and steel slag so they can replace 30-50% of the cement in concrete without losing strength. The technology builds on roughly 20 years of concrete-additive research by co-founder Zarina Bazoeva's father, Russian civil-engineering professor Dr Oleg Bazoev, and the company aims to produce cement-free, zero-carbon concrete by 2027. It has been used on NZ projects (including the Kāinga Ora Bader Ventura housing development), operates labs in Parnell and a manufacturing plant in South Auckland, and was selected for CRH Ventures' 2025 Sustainable Building Materials Accelerator.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed as a participating (not lead) investor in the March 2024 seed round, named in the press release, on Neocrete's Our Story page, and in the NZGIF release; round was led by Wavemaker Partners (Singapore). Matt Kennedy-Good's LinkedIn URL left null (no profile directly verified); his prior-role details (e.g. Goldman Sachs) come from data-aggregator/LinkedIn listings rather than primary sources, so carry mild uncertainty. The additive activates multiple materials (volcanic ash, fly ash, steel slag/GGBS); some media frame it as volcanic ash specifically. Note the company cites two distinct goals: zero-carbon concrete production by 2027 and reducing global emissions by 1% by 2033. Not to be confused with any same-named foreign entity.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://www.neocrete.com/", "https://www.neocrete.com/ourstory", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/BU2403/S00358/neocrete-secures-65m-in-seed-venture-funding-led-by-wavemaker-partners-singapore.htm", "https://www.nzgif.co.nz/news-and-events/nzgif-and-co-investors-invest-in-neocrete-to-support-low-emissions-concrete-production", "https://businessdesk.co.nz/article/news-in-brief/nz-green-concrete-startup-neocrete-secures-6m-in-seed-funding", "https://wavemakerpartners.com/wavemaker-portfolio/neocrete/", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/sustainable-business-and-finance-start-up-neocrete-tackles-concretes-carbon-footprint-costs-less/GRJPVKDPZNGNFDFXU76XPHQ76E/", "https://www.neocrete.com/post/world-s-largest-building-materials-company-crh-chooses-neocrete-for-2025-accelerator", "https://www.crhventures.com/news/meet-our-accelerator-finalists", "https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/stories/cementing-eco-friendly-building/"], "website": "https://www.neocrete.com", "industry": "Cleantech / Construction materials", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders, roles, 2018 founding, Auckland HQ, the US$4m/NZ$6.5m March 2024 seed led by Wavemaker, and Icehouse Ventures participation all independently confirmed via Neocrete's site, the press release, NZGIF, and BusinessDesk. Corrections: (1) dropped Zarina Bazoeva's UCL education claim, which could not be independently sourced; (2) changed Matt Kennedy-Good's location from Auckland to Wellington per sources; (3) clarified the founding tech originates from her father's research in Russia (not NZ) and that the company's own site does not name Dr Oleg Bazoev (confirmed via Wavemaker). CRH Ventures 2025 Accelerator selection and active status confirmed. oneLiner softened from the unverified \\"up to 50%\\"/\\"by up to 50%\\" framing to the sourced 30-50% cement-reduction figure.", "statusDetail": "Active. Raised a US$4m (NZ$6.5m) seed round announced 26 March 2024; operates labs/offices in Parnell and a manufacturing plant in South Auckland, runs international pilot/testing programmes, and was selected for CRH Ventures' 2025 Sustainable Building Materials Accelerator.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "US$4m (NZ$6.5m) seed round announced March 2024, led by Wavemaker Partners (Singapore), with participation from New Zealand Green Investment Finance (NZGIF) and Icehouse Ventures.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
