af-derived-protein/", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/company/470538-37", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/leaft-foods", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/leaft-foods-partners-with-lacto-japan-to-introduce-revolutionary-leaf-rubisco-protein-to-japanese-market-302550053.html", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/country/573399/nz-green-protein-producer-sprouts-new-deal-with-asian-food-giant", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ross-milne-7551a3110/", "https://www.selwyn.govt.nz/news-And-events/news/from-team-nz-trailblazer-to-protein-pioneer", "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/synlait-founder-john-penno-to-step-down-as-ceo-after-12-years/AOCSOCTDQZGSKSJJO44FDKNQDA/"], "website": "https://www.leaftfoods.com/", "industry": "Food technology / alternative protein agritech", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Dropped Ross Milne from founders: official team page lists only Maury Leyland Penno and John Penno as co-founders, and sources describe Milne as the CEO who was invited to join in 2019, not a co-founder. Adjusted both remaining founders' roles to \\"Co-founder\\" (neither is CEO). Corrected the funding note: Icehouse Ventures backing is confirmed as a portfolio investor (PitchBook; Icehouse job board) but Icehouse was NOT named in the 2022 Series A announcement, which listed only Khosla Ventures (lead), Steven Adams, Ngai Tahu, and ACC. Trimmed unverifiable specifics from the description (e.g. \\"Leaft Blade\\" consumer drink and pet products were not re-confirmed; demonstration-plant phrasing softened to \\"scaling production\\"). Founders, 2019 founding, Rolleston HQ, Rubisco/lucerne tech, and the September 2025 Lacto Japan partnership all independently confirmed.", "statusDetail": "Active; scaling production at Rolleston, Canterbury, and announced a September 2025 supply partnership with Lacto Japan.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised a ~US$15M Series A in 2022 led by Khosla Ventures, with Ngai Tahu, ACC's Climate Change Impact 