-make-energy-pricing-and", "https://gentrack.com/market-announcements/gentrack-acquires-factor-for-on-demand-energy-pricing/", "https://itbrief.co.nz/story/gentrack-buys-factor-in-nz-24m-energy-software-deal", "https://www.thepost.co.nz/business/361005919/gentrack-buys-utility-pricing-platform-factor-24m", "https://www.nzx.com/announcements/472765", "https://usefactor.com"], "website": "https://usefactor.com", "industry": "Energy technology / SaaS", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Core facts all confirmed by multiple independent sources: both founders (Jessica Venning-Bryan CEO, Simon Pohlen — refined to CTO, both ex-Flick Electric/Flux Federation), Wellington HQ, legal entity Prospero Energy Limited, Icehouse-led ~NZ$3m round, and the Gentrack acquisition (NZ$24m + up to NZ$10m earn-out, completed 15 May 2026). Corrections: Pohlen's role specified as CTO; both founder LinkedIn URLs set to null (unverifiable, auth-gated); Motion Capital and Angel HQ softened to \\"appear in aggregated coverage but unconfirmed\\" as they were absent from the primary NBR/NZ Herald articles. The total ~NZ$34.9m figure and exact pre-seed vs seed framing remain minor source discrepancies, noted rather than asserted.", "statusDetail": "Acquired by Gentrack (NZX/ASX: GTK) at NZ$24m enterprise value, plus a potential earn-out of up to NZ$10m tied to growing annual recurring revenue to ~NZ$17m over three years. Sale and purchase agreement signed and completed simultaneously on 15 May 2026.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised ~NZ$3m (reported as seed by NZ Herald/NBR; also described as an oversubscribed NZ$3.22m pre-seed) led by Icehouse Ventures, with participation from Blackbird, K1W1 (Sir Stephen Tindall's fund) and Func Ventures. Motion Capital and Angel HQ appear in some aggregated coverage but were not confirmed in the primary articles checked.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-miruku	organization	Miruku	Molecular-farming startup growing real dairy proteins and fats in oilseed crops, no cows required.	Palmerston North, New Zealand	https://www.miruku.com/	{"molecular farming","alternative dairy","precision fermentation alternative",agritech,"food biotech","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Miruku is a New Zealand biotech/agritech startup using \\"molecular farming\\" to produce real dairy proteins, fats and sugars inside specially designed oilseed crops (notably safflower) rather than from cows. Its proprietary Dairy Seed System aims to supply animal-free dairy ingredients via existing agricultural infrastructure. Founded in 2020, it positions molecular farming as a more scalable alternative to precision fermentation. The company runs crop trials with farming partners and works toward regulatory approvals and co-developed products with food-industry partners.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed by lead investor Motion Capital's own notes (round included \\"Movac, Icehouse Ventures, Aspire, Cultivate Ventures and NZVC\\") and corroborating funding coverage. HQ: NZ company registry (OpenCorporates) lists Palmerston North (John Lyttleton Building, 31 Dairy Farm Road); the 2022 emerge-from-stealth release said \\"Auckland,\\" but the registered/current HQ is Palmerston North — all sources agree the company is NZ-based. Funding figures mix USD (press: ~US$2.4M seed, ~US$5M pre-Series A, ~US$7.4M total) and NZD (NZ$8M pre-Series A); treat the USD/NZD labels with care. Oded Shoseyov is an Israel-affiliated academic; his city is not confirmed and is set to null. No same-name foreign company confusion; this is the NZ molecular-farming dairy company.", "stage": "Pre-Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2020", "sources": ["https://www.miruku.com/team", "https://www.miruku.com/", "https://www.motioncapital.co.nz/media/miruku-investment-notes", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/miruku-a-new-zealand-animal-free-dairy-start-up-emerges-from-stealth-on-foodtech-vc-investment-301507390.html", "https://www.finsmes.com/2024/02/miruku-raises-nzd5m-closes-nzd8m-pre-series-a-funding.html", "https://vegconomist.com/protein/miruku-secures-5m-proteins-oilseed-crops-dairy-2-0-products/", "https://opencorporates.com/companies/nz/8137365", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/mirukultd"], "website": "https://www.miruku.com/", "industry": "Food & beverage biotechnology (alternative dairy / molecular farming)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "All four founders (Amos Palfreyman, Ira Bing, Oded Shoseyov, Harjinder Singh) and their roles independently confirmed via Miruku's own team page; founding year 2020, active status, Palmerston North HQ, and the seed + pre-Series A funding (Movac-led seed; Motion Capital-led NZ$8M pre-Series A) all confirmed. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via Motion Capital's investment notes. Corrected: removed the unsupported \\"Executive Chair\\" descriptor on Ira Bing (the team page lists a separate Chair, Jerry Steiner) and trimmed/sourced the founder bios to verified facts. Founder LinkedIn URLs carried over from the draft but not independently re-verified.", "statusDetail": "Active; site shows \\"© Miruku Ltd 2025\\" with full team listed. Closed an NZ$8M (~US$5M) pre-Series A in February 2024, bringing total raised to ~US$7.4M.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "~US$7.4M total raised: ~US$2.4M oversubscribed seed (2022, led by Movac; Better Bite Ventures, Ahimsa Foundation, NZGCP's Aspire fund) and an NZ$8M (~US$5M) pre-Series A (Feb 2024, led by Motion Capital with Movac, Icehouse Ventures, Aspire, Cultivate Ventures and NZVC).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-caruso	organization	Caruso	AI-native fund administration and registry software for private-markets fund managers.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.getcaruso.com	{fintech,"fund administration",SaaS,"private markets",AI,"Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Caruso is a New Zealand-founded B2B fintech that combines AI-native software with fund administration services for real estate, private credit, and private equity fund managers, spanning CRM, registry, compliance, capital raising, distributions, and investor portals. It was spun out of commercial real estate firm Jasper in early 2023, where the technology had been built in-house over three years before being offered to third-party managers. By its 2026 Series A, the platform was used by more than 80 fund managers running around 900 funds across Australia, New Zealand, and the US. It operates offices in Auckland, Sydney, and Dallas.", "notes": "Disambiguation: This is the Auckland-based fund administration fintech (getcaruso.com), NOT Caruso's Natural Health (an Australian supplements brand), Caruso Real Estate / The Grove (US developer Rick Caruso), or the tenor Enrico Caruso. Funding/AUM-figure caveat: Caruso's NZ blog and NBR state the Series A as NZ$11.2m at a near-NZ$100m valuation; international wire coverage (PR Newswire, Startup Daily) reports the same single round in USD as ~US$9.3m (one variant US$6.5m) with AUM as US$80bn (vs NZ$100bn+ on the NZ blog) — these are currency conversions and rounding of one round, not separate raises. Oliver Shaw's title appears as \\"CTO, Executive Director & Co-founder\\" across sources; a couple list him as \\"Co-CEO,\\" but CTO is his primary role.", "stage": "Series A", "status": "active", "founded": "2023", "sources": ["https://www.getcaruso.com/en-nz/resources/blog/Caruso-raises-seed-capital", "https://www.getcaruso.com/en-us/resources/blog/caruso-series-a-2026", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/fund-admin-firm-caruso-closes-11-2m-series-a-at-100m-valuation/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/caruso-capital-raising-software-raises-3-2m-seed-capital-round/", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/kiwi-fund-administration-fintech-caruso-banks-9-3-million-series-a/", "https://www.jasper.io/news/jasper-spins-out-technology-into-new-saas-company", "https://www.prnewswire.com/apac/news-releases/caruso-raises-9-3m-series-a-assets-under-admin-surge-to-80bn-302744339.html", "https://theorg.com/org/getcaruso/org-chart/ollie-shaw", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/mark-hurley-3", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/oliverjshaw"], "website": "https://www.getcaruso.com", "industry": "Fintech / SaaS (fund administration software)", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed via fresh searches: both founders (Mark Hurley, Co-founder/CEO; Oliver Shaw, Co-founder/CTO) are real, correctly named/roled, and corroborated by Jasper's spin-out announcement, Caruso's own blogs, NBR, Startup Daily, The Org, and Crunchbase. Status is active and scaling. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed as lead of both the 2023 seed and the April 2026 Series A. Description and oneLiner are accurate. Minor refinements only: clarified that Jasper built the tech in-house over three years; noted that Shaw's primary title is CTO/Executive Director (some sources also say Co-CEO); reaffirmed the NZD/USD and AUM figure differences as one round reported in different currencies. No facts required correction.", "statusDetail": "Active and scaling; closed Series A in April 2026 with plans to grow to 80+ staff across its offices.", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised a ~NZ$3.2m seed in 2023 (announced Nov 2023) led by Icehouse Ventures, with GD1, Pushpay founder Chris Heaslip, and Rae Capital. Closed a NZ$11.2m Series A on 15 April 2026 at a near-NZ$100m valuation, led by Icehouse Ventures and GD1 with Balmain participating. International wire coverage reports the same round in USD as ~US$9.3m (some variants US$6.5m) at AUM reported as US$80bn (NZ$100bn+).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-af-drinks	organization	AF Drinks	NZ alcohol-free adult RTD cocktail brand with its proprietary Afterglow warming botanical.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.af-drinks.com	{"non-alcoholic drinks",alcohol-free,"RTD cocktails","consumer packaged goods",beverages,"New Zealand","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "AF Drinks is a New Zealand non-alcoholic beverage brand founded in 2020 by Lisa King, making premium alcohol-free ready-to-drink cocktails. Its products feature a proprietary warming botanical called Afterglow designed to mimic the sensation of alcohol. The company pioneered the alcohol-free RTD category in New Zealand, where it holds roughly a 35-40% market share, and expanded into the United States in 2023 (trading there as \\"Free AF\\") and into the UK (Morrisons) in late 2025.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed: AF Drinks is a portfolio company of the Brand Fund (Previously Unavailable + Icehouse Ventures partnership) and appears on the Icehouse Ventures job board, where a Head of Finance posting references an upcoming capital raise. In the US the company trades as \\"Free AF\\"; it entered the US in Feb 2023 (~4,000+ stores incl. Target/Walmart) and the UK via Morrisons in Dec 2025 (~350 stores). Pernod Ricard, via Convivialité Ventures, holds a 14.2% minority stake from 2023 (corrected from the draft's \\"approx. 15%\\"); it also distributes AF in NZ. NZ market share is cited as ~35% (2023, per King) rising to ~39-40% in later coverage. Lisa King is consistently described as the (sole) founder by the company, EY and NZ media; brand creation also involved Previously Unavailable / The Tuesday Club / Inhouse Design as equity partners and co-creators, but no individual co-founders are titled, so only Lisa King is listed. Stage is approximate. Crunchbase/PitchBook pages were not directly accessible, so funding figures rely on NZ/drinks-trade media.", "stage": "Seed / growth", "status": "active", "founded": "2020", "sources": ["https://previously.co/brand-fund-1", "https://previously.co/projects/af-drinks", "https://jobs.icehouseventures.co.nz/companies/af-drinks/jobs/69566012-head-of-finance", "https://www.af-drinks.com/en-us/pages/our-mission", "https://us.af-drinks.com/blogs/free-af-podcast/lisa-king-free-af-founder", "https://www.ey.com/en_nz/entrepreneur-of-the-year/new-zealand/meet-the-finalists/lisa-king", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisa_King", "https://drinks-intel.com/spirits/pernod-ricard-makes-alcohol-free-play-in-new-zealand-through-af-drinks/", "https://www.navibes.com/post/pernod-ricard-takes-stake-in-new-zealand-non-alcoholic-firm-af-drinks", "https://www.thespiritsbusiness.com/2025/12/non-alcoholic-rtd-free-af-lands-in-the-uk/", "https://www.beveragedaily.com/Article/2026/01/30/free-af-the-brand-riding-the-canned-cocktail-wave-in-alcohol-free/", "https://www.just-drinks.com/news/non-alcoholic-rtd-business-free-af-expects-to-triple-sales/"], "website": "https://www.af-drinks.com", "industry": "Food & Beverage", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently re-verified with fresh searches. Confirmed: founded 2020 by Lisa King (sole listed founder; the company and EY/media name only her, with Previously Unavailable/The Tuesday Club/Inhouse Design as co-creator equity partners but no titled co-founders), her Eat My Lunch + corporate-marketing background, Icehouse Ventures backing via the Brand Fund, active status, and US/UK expansion. Corrected the Pernod Ricard/Convivialité Ventures stake from \\"approx. 15%\\" to the reported 14.2% (2023), and softened NZ market share to \\"roughly 35-40%\\" since sources range from 35% (2023) to ~40% (later). Removed the unverifiable \\"approx.\\" precision on the stake. No unsourced founders were present to drop. Confidence high.", "statusDetail": "Operating and scaling across New Zealand, the US (as \\"Free AF\\") and the UK (Morrisons debut Dec 2025, ~350 stores); pursuing a further capital raise per the Icehouse Ventures job board.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Backed by Icehouse Ventures via the Brand Fund (its partnership with innovation studio Previously Unavailable), which lists AF Drinks as a portfolio company. Pernod Ricard's Convivialité Ventures took a 14.2% strategic minority stake in 2023 to fund US expansion; specific funding amounts are undisclosed.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-alimetry	organization	Alimetry	NZ medtech behind Gastric Alimetry, a non-invasive wearable for diagnosing gut disorders.	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.alimetry.com	{medtech,"medical devices",diagnostics,"gut health","gastric mapping",wearables,"digital health","University of Auckland spinout","AI healthcare","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Alimetry is a New Zealand medical technology company that develops Gastric Alimetry, a non-invasive, wearable device performing body-surface gastric mapping to diagnose neuromuscular and sensory gut disorders. A flexible electrode array applied to the abdomen measures the stomach's electrical activity through the skin, with cloud and AI-based analysis aiding clinicians. It is a University of Auckland / Auckland Bioengineering Institute spinout founded in 2019, built on roughly a decade of gut electrophysiology research. The flagship product has received multiple US FDA clearances and is used by 40-plus hospitals and clinics worldwide.", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed: explicitly named as a participating investor in the Oct 2024 US$18M Series A2 by TechCrunch, IP Group, PRNewswire and ITBrief. The round (US$18M / A$27M, hence the \\"$27M\\" headline) was led by GD1 with AGA GI Opportunity Fund, Olympus Innovation Ventures and existing backers. CORRECTION vs draft: Movac IS a genuine Alimetry investor - it LED the earlier NZ$16.3M Series A (March 2022, per NZ Herald, Scoop, Tracxn, Crunchbase), not the 2024 A2; the draft's note dismissing Movac was wrong. Founder set of four (O'Grady, Gharibans, Calder, Du, 2019) is corroborated by Tracxn and ABI/University of Auckland descriptions; the company's own team page emphasizes O'Grady (CEO) and Gharibans as the two named co-founders, lists Calder as CSO, and does not list Du (consistent with founders who have since left day-to-day roles). Gharibans' current title on the company team page is \\"President\\" (external aggregators still list him as CTO), so role reflects both. Only Gharibans' LinkedIn URL is verifiable (and consistently returned in search); others left null. Founded 2019 confirmed across multiple sources. Total raised ~US$29M (Tracxn); figures vary by aggregator so treated as approximate.", "stage": "Series A2", "status": "active", "founded": "2019", "sources": ["https://www.alimetry.com/our-team", "https://techcrunch.com/2024/10/24/medtech-alimetry-gases-up-with-18-million-for-a-wearable-to-help-diagnose-gastric-disorders/", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/alimetry-revolutionises-gut-health-diagnosis-by-integrating-ai-into-its-wearable-device-raises-us-18m-to-fuel-next-phase-of-growth-302289142.html", "https://www.startupdaily.net/topic/funding/kiwi-medtech-startup-alimetry-raises-27-million-series-a2-for-gut-health-wearables/", "https://www.ipgroupplc.com/news-and-events/portfolio-news/2024/2024-10-25", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/alimetry/__lM4vjAsaekVEqBXDglkCwl6Y23TXEfUmrma_czEJywA", "https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/SC2203/S00007/alimetry-raises-163-million-to-launch-wearable-diagnostic-device-for-the-gut.htm", "https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/news/2021/04/20/guts-glory-rise-biotech-start-up-alimetry.html", "https://nz.linkedin.com/in/armen-gharibans-05033a12", "https://www.olympusamerica.com/blog/medical-technologies/ai-integrated-wearables-gut-health-diagnosis-olympus-innovation-ventures"], "website": "https://www.alimetry.com", "industry": "Medtech / Medical Devices", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Fresh searches confirm the core record: 2019 University of Auckland/ABI spinout; Gastric Alimetry non-invasive wearable; multiple FDA clearances; 40-plus hospitals/clinics; Series A2 US$18M (A$27M) Oct 2024 led by GD1 with Icehouse Ventures participating (Icehouse-backing CONFIRMED). Two corrections applied: (1) Movac is a real investor that led the prior NZ$16.3M Series A in March 2022 (draft had wrongly dismissed it); the fundingNotable and notes now reflect this. (2) Gharibans is now listed as \\"President\\" on the company's own team page (was CTO), so his role was updated to capture both. All four founders are retained as each is sourced (Tracxn + ABI/University of Auckland coverage); none dropped. Confidence high.", "statusDetail": "Active and commercializing; the flagship Gastric Alimetry device has multiple US FDA clearances and 40-plus hospitals and clinics globally have signed on to use it. Operates across New Zealand, the US and the UK, with the US the primary expansion market.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised an oversubscribed US$18M (A$27M) Series A2 in October 2024, led by GD1 (Global From Day One) with the American Gastroenterological Association (AGA) GI Opportunity Fund, Olympus Innovation Ventures and Icehouse Ventures participating alongside existing backers. Prior rounds include a ~US$3.3M seed and a NZ$16.3M Series A (March 2022) led by Movac, with IP Group, UniServices, Matu Karihi and K1W1 participating. Total raised reported at roughly US$29M (Tracxn).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
