org:iv-sealogs	organization	SeaLogs	Digital logbook and fleet management platform for maritime operators	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.sealogs.com	{maritime,SaaS,"fleet management",compliance,"vessel management","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "SeaLogs is a New Zealand maritime software company offering a cloud-based digital logbook and fleet management platform for vessel operators, covering logbooks, maintenance, crew, safety and regulatory compliance. The product was built by founder Kylie Tomlin after she lost a paper logbook holding nearly six months of records days before a maritime audit. New Zealand customers include Fullers Group, Ports of Auckland, Queenstown Ferries and SeaLink, and the platform is designed to align with both Maritime New Zealand and Australian (AMSA) commercial-vessel compliance. It markets itself as New Zealand's first digital platform for maritime operators.", "notes": "Do not confuse with (a) Starboard Maritime Intelligence, a separate NZ maritime SaaS firm, or (b) same-named foreign \\"SeaLogs\\" listings (e.g. a Bakersfield, CA Nextdoor page). Founding year is reported inconsistently: SeaLogs' LinkedIn and several sources indicate 2018, while Crunchbase and Tracxn list 2016 — used 2018. HQ is listed as Auckland on LinkedIn and Tracxn, though some aggregators placed the founder in Queenstown/Canterbury. \\"Guy Wilson\\" appears as a SeaLogs team member in aggregator data but could not be independently confirmed as a co-founder and is not asserted. A \\"Roger A\\" CEO listing in one low-quality aggregator was not confirmed and is excluded.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2018", "sources": ["https://www.sealogs.com/about", "https://www.sealogs.com/testimonials", "https://nz.linkedin.com/company/sealogs", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/kylie-tomlin", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/kylie-tomlin-a30205a1/", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/sealogs/__ViY1IexbRQSeF_6s9Dk8aIyOnAz0ky-3QaJZXvPieHQ", "https://www.zoominfo.com/p/Laila-Grace/7616756301", "https://theorg.com/org/icehouse-ventures/org-chart/laila-grace", "https://www.fka.nz/"], "website": "https://www.sealogs.com", "industry": "Maritime software (SaaS)", "confidence": "medium", "verifyNote": "Most of the draft confirmed via fresh searches: founder Kylie Tomlin, the lost-logbook founding story, the product, the named NZ customers (Fullers, Ports of Auckland, Queenstown Ferries, SeaLink), AMSA/Maritime NZ alignment, Auckland HQ, and the active status. Corrections: (1) founder role updated from \\"Founder\\" to \\"Founder & CEO\\" (per Crunchbase/LinkedIn); (2) added Flying Kiwi Angels as a second investor alongside Icehouse Ventures (Crunchbase lists both; FKA portfolio lists \\"Marine HLDG (SeaLogs)\\" from Sep 2021). Icehouse backing remains confirmed via Tracxn's investor listing plus an Icehouse associate's board-observer seat, but no funding round size/date or Icehouse press release was found, and Tracxn's profile is internally inconsistent on whether a formal round closed — so funding specifics and the \\"Seed\\" stage remain unconfirmed and confidence stays medium.", "statusDetail": "Active and operating; product aligned with both Maritime New Zealand and Australian (AMSA) commercial-vessel compliance.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "No public round size or date was found. Crunchbase lists two investors — Icehouse Ventures and Flying Kiwi Angels (an Auckland/Wellington seed angel network, whose portfolio lists \\"Marine HLDG (SeaLogs)\\" from Sep 2021). Tracxn lists Icehouse Ventures as an institutional investor, and an Icehouse Ventures associate (Laila Grace) holds a board-observer seat at SeaLogs. Exact amount/stage unconfirmed; Tracxn's profile is internally inconsistent on whether a formal round was raised.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
