org:coherence-neuro	organization	Coherence Neuro	Closed-loop brain-computer interface that monitors and electrically treats cancer.	San Francisco, United States	https://www.coherenceneuro.com	{Healthtech,Active,"Blackbird Portfolio",Neurotechnology,"Brain-Computer Interfaces"}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "Healthcare", "status": "Active", "twitter": "https://x.com/coherenceneuro", "website": "https://www.coherenceneuro.com", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/coherenceneuro", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio/coherence-neuro", "https://www.coherenceneuro.com/team", "https://www.coherenceneuro.com/company", "https://www.capitalbrief.com/briefing/coherence-neuro-raises-10m-for-cancer-treatment-technology-08d52fb2-f186-450e-9eea-9f63d061b5f6/", "https://techfundingnews.com/startup-in-spotlight-coherence-neuro-raises-10m-to-launch-closed-loop-neuro-dystem-for-cancer-treatment/", "https://www.massdevice.com/coherence-neuro-raises-10m-seed-round-for-bci-that-aids-in-cancer-treatment/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/opto-biosystems", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ben-woodington/", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/elise-jenkins-/", "https://x.com/WoodingtonBen/status/1985530831390306521"], "confidence": "high", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["logoUrl", "founders[0].website", "founders[1].website"]}, "hqCountry": "United States", "crunchbase": "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/opto-biosystems", "subSectors": ["Neurotechnology", "Brain-Computer Interfaces", "Medical Devices", "Bioelectronics", "Oncology", "Neuro-oncology"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": 2022, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": "$10M", "fundingStage": "Seed", "snappedSector": "Healthtech", "matchedCompany": "Coherence Neuro (Coherence Neuro, Inc.; Crunchbase org slug \\"opto-biosystems\\")", "totalRaisedUsd": 10000000, "longDescription": "Coherence Neuro is a neurotechnology company operating at the intersection of neurotech, neurobiology, and machine learning, building a closed-loop, bi-directional brain-computer interface to track and treat cancer. Its flagship product, SOMA-1, is a coin-sized wireless implant paired with an over-ear wearable that continuously monitors neural electrical activity and delivers precisely tuned stimulation, aiming to bring cancers such as glioblastoma into stasis. The company treats cancer as a correctable \\"system-state error\\" addressable through electrical stimulation rather than only surgery, chemotherapy, or radiation. It was founded by two Cambridge Bioelectronics Laboratory PhDs and is preparing for its first human trials."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
