l Intelligence\\" by integrating lab-grown human neurons (from induced pluripotent stem cells) onto silicon microelectrode arrays to create programmable biological computers. It gained global attention with DishBrain, a system in which neuronal cultures learned to play the video game Pong, and in 2025 launched the CL1 — described as the world's first commercially available biological computer — priced at roughly US$35,000, alongside a remote-access \\"Cortical Cloud\\" service. The company positions neuron-based computing as a low-energy alternative for AI research and a tool that can reduce animal testing in medical research."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
