); formerly Operatr.IO", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Factor House is a Melbourne-based, engineering-led software company (formerly Operatr.IO) that builds enterprise tools for managing real-time, streaming data. Its flagship product Kpow is a single UI and API for Apache Kafka, while Flex brings the same simplicity to Apache Flink, and the unified Factor Platform lets customers manage their entire streaming ecosystem from one place. Bootstrapped for roughly six years to over US$1M in revenue, the company counts clients such as Hewlett Packard Enterprise, Block, Binance, Airwallex, Afterpay and several Fortune 500 companies. In February 2025 it raised a $5M seed round led by Blackbird Ventures to accelerate the commercial rollout of its platform."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
