org:hall	organization	Hall	AI visibility platform tracking how brands appear in ChatGPT, Perplexity and other LLMs.	Sydney, Australia	https://usehall.com/	{"AI & ML",Active,"Blackbird Portfolio","AI Search / Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)","Marketing Analytics"}	\N	{"kind": "portfolio_company", "sector": "Marketing Technology", "status": "Active", "twitter": null, "website": "https://usehall.com/", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/usehall/", "research": {"sources": ["https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio/hall", "https://www.blackbird.vc/portfolio", "https://usehall.com/", "https://usehall.com/company", "https://www.businessnewsaustralia.com/articles/blackbird-tips--2m-into-sydney-startup-that-measures-brand-performance-in-ai-search.html", "https://aiworld.eu/story/hall-raises-2m-from-blackbird-ventures-to-expand-ai-powered-visibility-tracking-platform", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/kaiforsyth", "https://au.linkedin.com/in/thomas-urie"], "confidence": "high", "researchedAt": "2026-05-31", "missingFields": ["totalRaisedUsd", "crunchbase", "twitter", "logoUrl", "founders.Leo Orpilla.linkedinUrl", "founders.Ajay Singh.linkedinUrl", "founders.twitterUrl", "founders.website"]}, "hqCountry": "Australia", "crunchbase": null, "subSectors": ["AI Search / Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)", "Marketing Analytics", "SaaS", "Artificial Intelligence", "SEO/AEO"], "exitDetails": null, "foundedYear": 2023, "statusGroup": "active", "totalRaised": "$2M", "fundingStage": "Pre-Seed", "snappedSector": "AI & ML", "matchedCompany": "Hall (Hall Technologies Pty. Ltd. — usehall.com), Sydney AI search/GEO analytics startup", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Hall builds the infrastructure for \\"AI marketing\\" — helping businesses understand, measure and optimise how they appear across conversational AI assistants and generative answer engines like ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Claude, Gemini and Perplexity. Using an approach known as Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO/AEO), the platform monitors brand visibility, website citations, AI agent activity and conversational-commerce performance across millions of AI queries, turning that into actionable insights for marketing teams. Hall launched a free self-serve product in April 2025 and aims to become the operational platform businesses rely on to manage their entire AI channel strategy."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
org:iv-andfoods	organization	ANDFOODS	NZ foodtech making plant-based dairy-free creams from legume pulses via fermentation.	Palmerston North, New Zealand	https://www.andfoods.co	{plant-based,"alternative proteins",fermentation,"dairy alternatives",foodtech,legumes,"New Zealand","Icehouse Ventures","Massey University","Riddet Institute","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "ANDFOODS is a Palmerston North, New Zealand foodtech startup that develops plant-based dairy alternatives, notably high-performance dairy-free creams and milk powders, from legume seeds (pulses such as black mung bean) using fermentation to remove off-flavours. The company spun out of research at Massey University and the Riddet Institute and targets professional foodservice and food-manufacturing applications. In March 2024 it raised a NZ$2.7 million seed round led by Icehouse Ventures. Former Synlait CEO Leon Clement chairs the company.", "notes": "Spun out of Massey University and the Riddet Institute. Six co-founders are confirmed by the Massey press release: Arup Nag (CTO), Alex Devereux (CEO), Alejandra Acevedo-Fani, Yiran Wang, Debashree Roy, and Harjinder Singh — Devereux and Nag are the lead operating founders. None dropped; all six are independently sourced. Chair is Leon Clement, former Synlait CEO and ex-Fonterra (confirmed via Massey and andfoods.co/about-us; board also lists directors Paul Maughan and Barnaby Marshall). Core tech is fermentation applied to pulses (e.g. black mung bean) to remove off-notes; signature dairy-free whipping cream cited at ~140% overrun. Corrections vs draft: removed \\"precision fermentation\\" framing (sources describe general fermentation, not precision fermentation); added Alex Devereux LinkedIn (alex-devereux-nz) and corrected his location to Christchurch (ZoomInfo) and enriched his Fonterra/Snowball Effect/Sidekicker background; clarified Acevedo-Fani/Wang/Roy/Singh company roles per andfoods.co. Website confirmed as andfoods.co (.co). Founding year 2023 is INFERRED from \\"launched less than a year ago\\" before March 2024 — no source states an exact incorporation date.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2023", "sources": ["https://www.massey.ac.nz/about/news/dairy-free-start-up-creams-it-with-27-million-seed-round/", "https://www.masseyventures.co.nz/26032024", "https://www.andfoods.co/about-us", "https://vegconomist.com/investments-finance/investments-acquisitions/andfoods-raise-legume-based-dairy-alternatives/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/512554/scientists-making-dairy-free-cream-milk-powder-from-seeds", "https://idealog.co.nz/venture/2024/03/andfoods-creaming-it-with-seed-based-products", "https://www.foodingredientsfirst.com/news/andfoods-leverages-fermentation-to-develop-creamy-alt-dairy-from-legume-seeds.html", "https://www.zoominfo.com/p/Alex-Devereux/4301517755", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/alex-devereux-nz/"], "website": "https://www.andfoods.co", "industry": "Food Technology / Alternative Proteins", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Most facts confirmed by fresh independent searches. Icehouse Ventures-led NZ$2.7m seed round (March 2024) confirmed by Massey, vegconomist, Idealog, foodmag, and foodingredientsfirst. All six co-founders confirmed by the Massey primary press release (none unsourced, none dropped). Leon Clement as chair confirmed by Massey and the company's own about page. Alex Devereux's Fonterra background confirmed and enriched (Global Manager Strategy Foodservice; also Snowball Effect, Sidekicker); his LinkedIn was located and his location corrected to Christchurch (was wrongly Palmerston North in draft). Corrections made: dropped the \\"precision fermentation\\" descriptor (sources say fermentation, not precision fermentation). Unconfirmed: exact founding/incorporation year (2023 is inferred, not directly stated); LinkedIn URLs for the five non-CEO founders were not located so left null. No 2025/2026 news surfaced, so \\"active\\" rests on the March 2024 evidence and the live company site.", "statusDetail": "Active; raised a NZ$2.7m seed round in March 2024 and taking its first product (a plant-based whipping cream) to market while developing products with major food companies.", "verifyVerdict": "partly-confirmed", "fundingNotable": "NZ$2.7M seed round (March 2024) led by Icehouse Ventures.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-kwetta	organization	Kwetta	NZ power-electronics startup unlocking ultra-fast EV charging by tapping grid capacity directly.	Napier, New Zealand	https://kwetta.com	{"EV charging","power electronics","clean energy","grid technology",hardware,"heavy transport","New Zealand","climate tech","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Kwetta is a Napier, New Zealand-based energy technology startup founded in 2021 that develops power electronics for ultra-fast EV charging. Its flagship Prime Grid Gateway connects directly to the medium/high-voltage distribution grid, unlocking up to ten times more power at constrained sites without costly grid upgrades or large battery storage. The company targets heavy transport, fleets and large charging hubs, and has partnered with Z Energy to roll out ultra-fast chargers across NZ service stations. In 2024 it closed an oversubscribed Series A led by Blackbird, with Icehouse Ventures, Virescent Ventures and Z Energy also backing the company; it is now expanding into Australia and Europe (with an Amsterdam office).", "notes": "Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed: named as a Series A investor across multiple independent outlets (EVs & Beyond, NZ Herald, pv magazine, Startup Daily) and listed in Icehouse's own portfolio/job board. Funding amount reported variously as NZ$15.8m / NZ$15.9m / NZ$17.5m (US$10.5m) for the same Blackbird-led 2024 round; one source also names Outset Ventures as a participant (single-sourced, treat as tentative). Website kwetta.com verified live (Napier HQ at 7b Sheffield Place, Onekawa, plus an Amsterdam, Netherlands office). Dustin Murdock LinkedIn located and added; his prior background (ABB, Beca, Powercorp; Univ. of Wisconsin-Madison MEng; ~20 yrs) is richer than the draft's \\"~11 years,\\" so corrected. LinkedIn URLs for Turner and Lazelle not located, left null. Dealroom lists the company under slug \\"red_phase_1,\\" consistent with a likely prior/related name \\"Red Phase\\" (unverified).", "stage": "Series 