orm built specifically for the chemical industry. It captures and structures a company's fragmented technical, product, and regulatory knowledge — from scientific literature, internal documentation, and supplier catalogs — and applies domain-specific chemical reasoning to deliver technically accurate, source-grounded answers to commercial and technical teams in real time. The platform aims to help chemical businesses scale scarce expert knowledge rather than rely on a handful of specialists, and is already deployed with enterprise customers including Bostik, Univar Solutions, and Stahl. Kimia raised a $7M seed round in April 2026 led by Airtree Ventures, with Blackbird Ventures and Skip Capital participating."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
