 & Energy", "matchedCompany": "SunDrive Solar Pty Ltd (Sydney, Australia)", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "SunDrive is a Sydney-based solar technology company founded in 2015 that has developed a proprietary metallisation process replacing the costly silver used in conventional solar cell electrodes with cheaper, far more abundant copper. The approach produces thinner metal lines that let more light into the cell, and SunDrive has set multiple world efficiency records for commercial-sized cells (including 25.54% in 2021 and 26.41% in 2022). Following a 2024 restructuring, the company shifted its focus from in-house panel manufacturing toward developing and licensing its copper-plating tooling and automation technology. It is backed by Blackbird, Main Sequence, the Clean Energy Finance Corporation, Mike Cannon-Brookes' Grok Ventures and ARENA."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
