RaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Ternary Kinetics is an Auckland-based deep-tech energy company developing \\"liquid electricity\\" — a sustainable liquid-phase carrier that stores renewable energy and can be pumped, shipped, and distributed through existing fossil-fuel infrastructure. The company says its liquid is around 10x more energy-dense than typical lithium EV battery cells, non-toxic, and safe to handle, targeting hard-to-decarbonise sectors such as aviation, maritime, mining, trucking, rail, and industrial hydrogen. Founded in 2023 by chemical engineer Sean Molloy, electrochemist Prof. Aaron Marshall, and LanzaTech founder Dr. Sean Simpson, it has raised early-stage capital from local and international deep-tech investors."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
