cs startup", "totalRaisedUsd": 10000000, "longDescription": "Vexev is a Sydney-based medtech company building the next generation of vascular imaging by combining custom robotics, machine learning, and high-resolution ultrasound. Its VxWave system performs autonomous, non-specialist 3D tomographic ultrasound scans of the vasculature (likened to MRI/CT outputs), aiming to shift vascular medicine from reactive to proactive. The company initially targets high-risk hemodialysis patients, where regular vessel surveillance enables earlier detection of vascular disease, and has run clinical studies at U.S. Renal Care dialysis clinics. The technology grew out of founders' UNSW PhD research into vascular fluid dynamics and computational imaging."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
