edUsd": null, "longDescription": "Sessions was a behavioral-health/coaching startup that paired users with a dedicated human health coach to complete a structured 12-week lifestyle-modification program, with the coach interacting via Skype, email and text to keep members motivated (monthly plans ran roughly $69-$199 depending on coach contact). Founded in 2012 by Australians Nick Crocker and Ben Hartney and incubated out of San Francisco's Rock Health accelerator, it reported roughly 90% program-completion rates, far above industry engagement norms. It raised under $1M from SV Angel, Collaborative Fund, Blackbird Ventures and Joshua Kushner (Thrive Capital). MyFitnessPal acquired Sessions in February 2014 — MyFitnessPal's first acquisition — with the founders and team joining to build coaching into MyFitnessPal's 50M+ user base; the standalone Sessions coaching service was subsequently wound down."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
