: 990000000, "longDescription": "Zoox is an autonomous-vehicle company founded in 2014 that designs purpose-built, symmetrical, bi-directional battery-electric robotaxis from the ground up, rather than retrofitting conventional cars, to deliver an autonomous ride-hailing (mobility-as-a-service) experience. Co-founded by Australian artist-designer Tim Kentley-Klay and Stanford self-driving researcher Dr. Jesse Levinson, it became one of the most prominent and well-capitalized startups in the robotaxi space, reaching a $3.2B valuation. Amazon acquired Zoox in June 2020 for over $1.2 billion, operating it as a wholly owned subsidiary; the company has since launched public robotaxi services in Las Vegas and San Francisco. Blackbird Ventures was Zoox's first investor, backing the 2014 seed round and later participating in the Series B."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
