s fragmented OSINT tools, proprietary databases, analytical workflows, and internal systems into a single platform where human analysts and autonomous AI agents can run hundreds of concurrent investigations in parallel. The platform proactively surfaces emerging threats through continuous monitoring of online platforms before harm occurs. The company was incorporated as Azonic Limited in Auckland in March 2026. Co-founder and CEO Caden Scott also founded the non-profit International Online Crime Coordination Center (IOC3), which connects victims, online platforms, analysts and law enforcement agencies such as the DIA, FBI and Interpol. Co-founder and CTO Thomas Holdom leads engineering, with a background building AI infrastructure and production agentic systems."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
