scription": "Aō Air (formerly known as O2O2) is a New Zealand-founded respiratory-protection company building the next generation of personal air filtration to replace cloth and N95 masks. Its flagship product, the ATMOS, is a transparent wearable \\"faceware\\" band that uses dual induction fans to draw air through proprietary nanofibre filters, creating a positive-pressure air seal that captures over 98% of PM2.5 particulate matter — claimed in independent testing (Auckland University of Technology) to offer up to 50x better protection than market-leading respirators. The company was the inaugural investment from Blackbird Ventures' New Zealand fund and also passed through accelerators including SOSV/HAX, URBAN-X and Dassault's 3DEXPERIENCE Lab. It is now recorded as written off in Blackbird's portfolio."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
