lRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Bardee is a Melbourne-based agtech / climate-tech company founded in 2019 that uses black soldier fly larvae to transform pre- and post-consumer food waste into high-value products such as insect protein for livestock and pet feed, plus organic fertiliser. Founders Phoebe Gardner and Alex Arnold began the venture by chopping discarded tuna heads in a university car park to feed insects in a benchtop-scale lab, later building a ~2,500sqm vertical-farming facility in Melbourne's northwest (Sunshine). The company raised a $5M seed round led by Blackbird Ventures in late 2021, but struggled to raise further capital, laid off around 30 staff in May 2023, and its former parent company was handed to liquidators in 2024."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
