"Series B", "snappedSector": "Fintech", "matchedCompany": "Hey You (formed from the 2014 merger of Posse and Beat the Q; café order-ahead & mobile payments platform)", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Hey You was an Australian mobile order-ahead and payments platform that let consumers order and pay ahead at cafes and restaurants to skip the queue. It was formed in 2014 from the merger of Rebekah Campbell's recommendation app Posse with Adam Theobald's cafe-ordering startup Beat the Q (plus E-Coffee Card), and rebranded to \\"Hey You\\" in 2015. At its peak it was Australia's largest cafe-focused mobile payments platform, with over a million users and tens of millions of orders. In December 2022 the business merged with last-mile courier Drive Yello to form 4You Innovation; Blackbird's investment in the company was ultimately written off."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
