nsumer & Marketplace", "matchedCompany": "Shoes of Prey (Shoes of Prey Pty Ltd) — custom-shoe design e-commerce startup founded in Sydney, Australia by Jodie Fox, Michael Fox and Mike Knapp; Blackbird Ventures portfolio company (invested 2013)", "totalRaisedUsd": null, "longDescription": "Shoes of Prey was an Australian-founded fashion-technology brand that let customers design their own bespoke women's shoes online — choosing style, heel, materials, color and embellishments — which were then hand-made and shipped worldwide. Launched in 2009 in Sydney by Jodie Fox, Michael Fox and Mike Knapp, it grew rapidly, won World Retail Awards recognition, expanded to the US with concessions inside Nordstrom and David Jones, and raised tens of millions of dollars from top-tier investors. After struggling to scale its mass-customization model beyond a niche audience, the company paused taking orders in August 2018 and went into liquidation in March 2019, with investors set to lose a reported ~A$35 million."}	community:blackbird-ventures	\N	2026-06-01 01:42:34.43	2026-06-01 01:44:40.738	Portfolio Company
