org:iv-yabble	organization	Yabble	NZ generative-AI platform turning unstructured data into market research insights in minutes	Auckland, New Zealand	https://www.yabble.com	{AI,"market research","consumer insights",SaaS,"generative AI","Icehouse Portfolio",Acquired}	\N	{"bio": "Yabble is a New Zealand-founded generative-AI market research company that turns unstructured customer data into insights in minutes. Founded in Auckland in 2017 by Kathryn Topp and Rachel O'Shea, its products include Virtual Audiences (AI personas), Gen (AI research agent), Summarize, and Count for theming and sentiment. It served global brands and expanded across NZ, Australia, and the US. In August 2024 it was acquired by AIM-listed global research firm YouGov.", "notes": "Auckland, NZ generative-AI research firm, now a YouGov company; distinct from any same-named foreign entity. Founding year 2017 confirmed by Yabble's own about page (some secondary sources say \\"since 2019,\\" which refers to gen-AI product development, not company founding). Acquisition firmly August 2024 (announced 7 Aug 2024) per Research Live, NBR and YouGov.", "stage": "Acquired", "status": "acquired", "founded": "2017", "sources": ["https://www.yabble.com/about-us", "https://www.yabble.com/blog/media-release-yabble-sells-to-global-insights-leader", "https://www.research-live.com/article/news/yougov-buys-yabble-in-45m-deal/id/5129173", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/tech/kiwi-ai-startup-yabble-sold-to-yougov-for-4-5m-plus/", "https://today.yougov.com/economy/articles/50596-yougov-acquires-yabble", "https://www.startupdaily.net/2021/09/new-zealand-ai-insights-startup-yabble-raises-3-million-for-australian-expansion/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/kathryn-topp-f5ec", "https://www.crunchbase.com/person/rachel-oshea", "https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/why-uc/our-alumni/notable-alumni/kathryn-topp"], "website": "https://www.yabble.com", "industry": "Market research / AI software", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Independently confirmed via fresh searches: both founders (Kathryn Topp - Co-founder & CEO; Rachel O'Shea - Co-founder & COO) verified against Yabble's about page, Crunchbase and LinkedIn; 2017 Auckland founding verified on Yabble's own site; YouGov acquisition (announced 7 Aug 2024, £4.5m cash + three-year revenue earn-out) verified by Research Live, NBR and YouGov; Icehouse Ventures backing explicitly named in Yabble's own acquisition media release. Corrections to draft: removed the unsupported \\"ArcAngels fund managed by Icehouse Ventures\\" claim (not present in the media release, which names \\"Icehouse Ventures\\" directly); statusDetail/sources tightened. The 2021 round was reported as NZ$3m by Startup Daily/Research Live (one outlier source said $3.2m).", "statusDetail": "Acquired by YouGov (announced 7 August 2024) for an initial £4.5m cash consideration plus a three-year revenue-based earn-out", "verifyVerdict": "confirmed", "fundingNotable": "Raised NZ$3m in September 2021 (led by Hillfarrance, with Movac, NZGCP, Enterprise Angels and others) for Australian/US expansion. Investors named in Yabble's own acquisition release include Hillfarrance, NetX Partners, Movac, Aspire NZ, Enterprise Angels, Angel Investors of Marlborough and Icehouse Ventures, plus NZTE and Callaghan Innovation support.", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
org:iv-zincovery	organization	Zethos (formerly Zincovery)	Christchurch cleantech recovering zinc and critical minerals from steel-industry waste at up to ~95% lower emissions.	Christchurch, New Zealand	https://zethos.tech/	{cleantech,"zinc recycling","critical minerals",electrochemistry,"deep tech","Icehouse Portfolio"}	\N	{"bio": "Zethos, formerly Zincovery, is a University of Canterbury spin-out building a low-carbon metal refining platform that recovers high-purity zinc and other critical minerals (copper, nickel, manganese) from steel-industry waste such as furnace/mill dust. Its selective-reduction process runs at lower temperatures and can be powered by renewable electricity, reported to use about 70% less energy, cut carbon emissions by up to ~95%, and lower operating costs by up to ~50% versus conventional coal-based methods. In 2025 the company rebranded from Zincovery to Zethos to reflect a broader critical-minerals focus, and it has opened a roughly 2,500 sqm large-scale metal refining demonstration facility in Bromley, Christchurch. It raised a NZ$3m seed round in October 2022 with Icehouse Ventures as the largest investor, and reports total funding of roughly NZ$16-20m.", "notes": "The company rebranded from \\"Zincovery\\" (legal entity Zincovery Process Technologies Limited) to \\"Zethos\\" in 2025; zincovery.com still carries Zethos branding and the live site is zethos.tech. Founding year is cited inconsistently: the company/NBR/KiwiNet/RNZ describe the spin-out as founded in 2021, while earlier coverage dates the underlying University of Canterbury research/initial venture to 2018-2019; 2021 used here as the most commonly cited company founding date. Icehouse Ventures backing confirmed via the Icehouse Ventures portfolio page (listed as Zincovery) and Oct 2022 NZ$3m seed coverage (reported ~22% stake; Icehouse does not publish exact percentages). Total funding figures (NZ$16m vs NZ$20m) vary by source and date. LinkedIn URLs surfaced via search but not directly verified on LinkedIn (which blocks automated fetch). This is the NZ Zethos/Zincovery, not any unrelated same-named entity.", "stage": "Seed", "status": "active", "founded": "2021", "sources": ["https://zethos.tech/team/", "https://www.icehouseventures.co.nz/portfolio", "https://newsroom.co.nz/2022/10/24/nz-deep-tech-startup-raises-3m-for-zinc-recycling/", "https://climatevcfund.com/why-were-backing-zincovery-for-zinc-recycling-without-coal/", "https://www.nbr.co.nz/your-business/from-zincovery-to-zethos-more-than-a-name-change/", "https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/593327/empty-warehouse-transformed-into-state-of-the-art-metal-refining-facility", "https://kiwinet.org.nz/SuccessStories/Zincovery", "https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/news-and-events/news/zincovery-wins-callaghan-innovation-s-c-prize-19-20", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Marshall"], "website": "https://zethos.tech/", "industry": "Cleantech / Metal recycling and refining", "confidence": "high", "verifyNote": "Founders, current status, and Icehouse Ventures backing all independently confirmed (NBR, newsroom.co.nz, KiwiNet, Climate VC Fund, company team page, Icehouse portfolio). Corrections: softened \\"seed round led by Icehouse Ventures\\" to \\"Icehouse the largest investor (~22% stake),\\" since sources describe Icehouse as biggest investor rather than the named lead (Climate VC Fund/Icehouse/Outset framed together); added the reported \\"~70% less energy\\" figure to the description; trimmed two founder bio claims I could not independently confirm in this pass (Ring's exact degree years and role as \\"Manager, Scale Up & Commercialization\\"; Marshall's 2025 Pickering Medal and specific degree years/dates). Could not access Crunchbase/LinkedIn directly (blocked/paywalled); the NBR full article and the \\"$9.1m first close\\" headline are paywalled, so the higher funding total is reported as a range. Confidence remains high.", "statusDetail": "Active; rebranded from Zincovery to Zethos in 2025 and opened a large-scale (~2,500 sqm) metal refining demonstration facility in Bromley, Christchurch.", "verifyVerdict": "corrected", "fundingNotable": "Raised a NZ$3m seed round in October 2022 with Icehouse Ventures the largest investor (reported ~22% stake), alongside the Climate Venture Capital Fund, Outset Ventures and K1W1 (Sir Stephen Tindall's family office). Media reports cite total funding raised of roughly NZ$16-20m (figures vary by source/date).", "icehouseBacked": "confirmed"}	community:icehouse-ventures	\N	2026-05-31 08:57:29.572	2026-06-01 01:42:36.222	Startup
